{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left","id":960027,"title":"What monsters are left?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-29T14:46:17-07:00","id":960027,"title":"What monsters are left?","content":"The CofD seems to be moving away from a new gameline every single year, and with good reason; it seems like most of the major monster archetypes have already been tapped. But I doubt new games will stop entirely, especially with the willingness to completely alter the narrative (Demon being about renegade eldritch program spies, Promethean taking Frankenstein's monster and turning it into a grand human journey) or move away from a central archetype in favor of a build-your -own model (Beast and Deviant seem especially focused on this), and so we need new monsters to draw upon.<br /> <br /> Are there any you feel are especially prime and untapped territory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:21:45-07:00","id":960044,"title":"","content":"Godzilla? So much for a 'secret' world of darkness.<br /> \u200bThere are still aliens, outer space or alternate dimensions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:30:36-07:00","id":960049,"title":"","content":"Giant Ants.<br /> <br /> More specifically, the struggle of trying to maintain individuality against the growing pull of a hive mind. Although... that thought space is sort of filled by the Angels in Demon and that aesthetic is covered by Beast. Hmm...<br /> <br /> <br /> Stranded Extraterrestrials.<br /> <br /> There could be a lot of interesting material in the vein of a community of alien beings marooned on Earth, especially if they're hiding their presence and/or trying to assemble functional high technology (to get home, conquer Earth, or what have you) with rudimentary parts (It's like trying to build a particle accelerator from stuff you find in a national park. Not impossible, but wicked hard).<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also suggest Lagoonas (Creatures from the Black Lagoon... and yes, I just made the term &quot;Lagoonas&quot; up.) but I can't really think of a good driving force for them.<br /> <br /> They'd want to adapt to surface life, but their mindset is completely alien to the human experience. Making them humans who realize they're actually sea monsters would fall too close to Werewolf (better suited as a setting substitute for a Mirrors shard) but putting them the other way around plops them on Demon's toes (stealing human identities to live on the surface and hide from something chasing them out of the deep). Alternatively, the sea creature cult approach aligns itself with Mummy, so no room there.<br /> <br /> <br /> The last one I can think of is some sort of contagious mutation, but it sounds like Deviant's got that.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... fingers crossed for giant ants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:48:05-07:00","id":960061,"title":"","content":"Dragons <i>dragons </i>as a singular focus? Typical dragons, at least aesthetically and fully revealed. But not as something that just lets you go &quot;giant firebreathing flying lizard&quot; in the middle of times square.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about themes. Hm. Dark Souls? Something. But we already have splats that do &quot;lost and fading ancient glories&quot; well, and one of them very centrally (although somewhat superficially in relation to the rest of its ideas.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-29-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:54:44-07:00","id":960065,"title":"","content":"well, let's say the two answers someone say every time such thread is made- Aliens and Monster of the Black Lagoon. As for a more creative answer- perhaps a full, Dorian Gray like immortal template (I know about the Eternal for Immortals is my favorite book, but still).<br /> <br /> Also- I'm still waiting for CofD Wraith version assuming that Geist would stay, well, Geist, and perhaps we could also get something less from horror books and more from mythology, like Fury: the Scourge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T16:04:49-07:00","id":960067,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say since Beast can cover so much. On one hand I could argue the intersection of Naga/Mer/DeepOnes deserves its own game ala Leviathan the Tempest (fan game)... But it's easy enough to say that Beast covers &quot;the Creature from the Black Lagoon&quot; as its focus already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T16:16:33-07:00","id":960072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960067#post960067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to say since Beast can cover so much. On one hand I could argue the intersection of Naga/Mer/DeepOnes deserves its own game ala Leviathan the Tempest (fan game)... But it's easy enough to say that Beast covers &amp;quot;the Creature from the Black Lagoon&amp;quot; as its focus already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast felt a lot more like Leviathan when the Homecoming was so prominently featured and you could create Ahabs (Heroes, rather) yourself. I wish there were more lines where the focus isn't &quot;I was a human who turned into a monster&quot; or &quot;I'm a monster masquerading as human,&quot; but instead the rare &quot;I've been a monster all along and thought I was human.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T16:38:01-07:00","id":960088,"title":"","content":"Things not already touched on...<br /> <br /> Angels have not really been done as playable characters, although we do have some rules for them. That isn't to say we couldn't have an entirely different type of being that that of themselves as angels; God knows we already had some ten different things called demons before Demon ever came out. Rather than going grand terrible divine asshole route I would want something more akin to a being of superlative empathy trapped and cut-off in the mortal realm trying its best to alleviate the misery around it before being overwhelmed; a bleeding heart bleeding to death. I don't know if anyone would want to play such a thing though.<br /> <br /> Revenants, our ghosts possessing their own bodies, in a manner similar to the Risen from Wraith. Geist touches on this but doesn't quite scratch it; it might be worth making a more fleshed out option in that gameline.<br /> <br /> There still isn't really a ghost game so much as pieces of one.<br /> <br /> I've batted the idea of zombies back and forth for a while, which would almost the reverse of vampire. Less horror about the corruption of the soul so much as the corruption of the body, and the inevitable feeling of time running out. It's be a game less made for long running campaigns and more for one-shots.<br /> <br /> Djinn.<br /> <br /> There isn't much left.<br /> <br /> I have resisted the thought of aliens for some time, largely because that is a really broad category that doesn't pin anything down, but with the advent of Beast and Deviant being so broad, it may be something like Outsiders - various alien beings from outside our dimension - might be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T16:59:02-07:00","id":960102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960067#post960067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to say since Beast can cover so much. On one hand I could argue the intersection of Naga/Mer/DeepOnes deserves its own game ala Leviathan the Tempest (fan game)... But it's easy enough to say that Beast covers &quot;the Creature from the Black Lagoon&quot; as its focus already.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, Promethean gave us mummies first, and Immortals gave us the Purified- and yet we still got a new game. Beast is a game about giants, dragons, sea monsters, gorgons and raptors- in sort, it is a game about myths, legends about our greatest fears and the heroes who slay them. Beast can cover things like the Black Lagoon, sure- but it doesn't mean it can't support its own gameline, especially when taken to a new direction. After all, Beast could, potentially, cover up everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:01:05-07:00","id":960104,"title":"","content":"Let's see. If we base on what fangames have been made or being done, so far there's:<br /> <br /> Leviathan The Tempest - Lovecraft/Deep Ones<br /> Genius the Transgression - Mad Scientists<br /> Princess the Hopeful - Magical Girls/Boys<br /> Demigod the Empyrean - Demigods<br /> Siren the Drowning - Merfolk<br /> Djinn the Binding (even though mainly exists in ideas than playability) - Genies<br /> Monarch the Endless - Aliens<br /> Dragon the Embers/Inheritance - Dragons<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not saying that the Onyx Path Guys can't make gamelines out of the fangames above. Just that some parts may be similar and possible argument from the creators of the respective fangames if they're feeling gypped. I'm wondering though, does anyone play the Sims? They make use of supernaturals. Heck, playing Sims 3 and using mermaids is what sorta made me wonder &quot;why isn't there a mermaid splat in the wod&quot;. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sims.wikia.com/wiki/Life_state\" target=\"_blank\">http://sims.wikia.com/wiki/Life_state</a><br /> <br /> Looking through these, the only ones that haven't been touched by the WoD is the Plantsim one and &quot;Imaginary Friend&quot;. But I don't know how they could carry out either of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:07:16-07:00","id":960108,"title":"","content":"I did Imaginary Friend. Check out the Brothers Grimm <b>Changeling </b>Dark Era.<br /> <br /> And one can easily take care of mermaids in <b>Beast</b>. I know, because I've made a textbook mermaid with <b>Beast</b>, but I can't say much more about that until something comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 08-29-2016, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:12:48-07:00","id":960110,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I don't know how useful this question is any more. Lots of concepts have been repeated across multiple game lines (how many ways can we make wolfmen, for example?) so we can't really narrow down what concepts future games might focus on based on what has already been done. And Beast has shown that new gamelines don't need to be based on any one specific classic horror monster, so we can't reliably predict what they might try to cover that hasn't been covered.<br /> <br /> That said, I think Alien is a pretty clearly &quot;missing&quot; type, but I don't know if CofD will ever get closer to that then Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-29-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:31:51-07:00","id":960119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960104#post960104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just that some parts may be similar and possible argument from the creators of the respective fangames if they're feeling gypped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you know, the term &quot;gypped&quot; comes from the word &quot;gypsy&quot; and its use as a colloquial for being tricked or ripped off is based on negative stereotypes about the Romani. I'm sure you didn't mean it offensively, a lot of people don't even realize how offensive the turn of phrase is, but as an informal, black text warning, just be aware that it <i>is</i> offensive, and you should be careful with it in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-29-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T17:34:40-07:00","id":960121,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the question that should be asked is not, &quot;what monsters are left,&quot; but rather, &quot;what kind of monster stories are left?&quot;<br /> <br /> As noted, pretty much any monster can be made in at least one of the games at this point, even if that isn't the focus of the game. The Gill-man is a bit flat for a game. He's a cryptid at best, with simple bestial motivations. So if there's going to be a Creature from the Black Lagoon inspired game, one of the key things to ask is, &quot;what's the focus of this game, and what kind of stories does it tell?&quot; and see if those answers are really different from what's already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:07:16-07:00","id":960141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960121#post960121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the question that should be asked is not, &quot;what monsters are left,&quot; but rather, &quot;what kind of monster stories are left?&quot;<br /> <br /> As noted, pretty much any monster can be made in at least one of the games at this point, even if that isn't the focus of the game. The Gill-man is a bit flat for a game. He's a cryptid at best, with simple bestial motivations. So if there's going to be a Creature from the Black Lagoon inspired game, one of the key things to ask is, &quot;what's the focus of this game, and what kind of stories does it tell?&quot; and see if those answers are really different from what's already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally exactly what David Hill and I were just talking about--games should focus on theme, and if it wouldn't examine a new theme, the monster should be left with the ways it can be portrayed in already existing games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  SHOULD focus on theme, not shouldn't. 08-29-2016, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:20:12-07:00","id":960150,"title":"","content":"I am fairly certain Magical Girls will never become an actual gameline.<br /> <br /> Unless Onyx Path has different ideas about my April Fool's Pitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T18:29:51-07:00","id":960154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960141#post960141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Literally exactly what David Hill and I were just talking about--games should focus on theme, and if it wouldn't examine a new theme, the monster should be left with the ways it can be portrayed in already existing games.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960104#post960104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathan The Tempest - Lovecraft/Deep Ones<br /> Genius the Transgression - Mad Scientists<br /> Princess the Hopeful - Magical Girls/Boys<br /> Demigod the Empyrean - Demigods<br /> Siren the Drowning - Merfolk<br /> Djinn the Binding (even though mainly exists in ideas than playability) - Genies<br /> Monarch the Endless - Aliens<br /> Dragon the Embers/Inheritance - Dragons</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Combining these, several of these games have their themes laid out in their titles, some of which are unique.<br /> <br /> Djinn is (was going to be) about having power, yet being in many ways a slave to it.<br /> Dragon, Inheritance atleast , has been in a sense about inheritance of power.<br /> Leviathan is about playing a monster, perhaps to a more obvious degree than others.<br /> <br /> Monarch the Endless, the one I contribute had a title that had more than one meaning. Despite being about alien space monster genetic horrors, the first part of the title speaks about nobility, the aspect about being a ruler... and the realities of having dominion over a nation would mean. In the Endless, it was about the theme of repetition, things are cyclical, a rise and a fall, and also of being rather literal using several definitions of the word &quot;endless&quot; depending on context.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm wondering though, does anyone play the Sims? They make use of supernaturals. Heck, playing Sims 3 and using mermaids is what sorta made me wonder &quot;why isn't there a mermaid splat in the wod&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I found this a while back on the forums. May be relevant, who knows? I thought about mermaids when I read it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B1vWDWuLUfXsTGR2cGh3dkpaNnc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B1vW...h3dkpaNnc/edit</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 08-29-2016, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T21:29:57-07:00","id":960224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960119#post960119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so you know, the term &amp;quot;gypped&amp;quot; comes from the word &amp;quot;gypsy&amp;quot; and its use as a colloquial for being tricked or ripped off is based on negative stereotypes about the Romani. I'm sure you didn't mean it offensively, a lot of people don't even realize how offensive the turn of phrase is, but as an informal, black text warning, just be aware that it <i>is</i> offensive, and you should be careful with it in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for this, I'm usually the one who has to say it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T22:04:39-07:00","id":960234,"title":"","content":"Huh... ghosts? Like in Wraith? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T22:31:34-07:00","id":960244,"title":"","content":"Again though, what kind of ghost stories are we telling with the CofD take on Wraith? What do these PC-ghosts do that's interesting?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T01:30:47-07:00","id":960297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960104#post960104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's see. If we base on what fangames have been made or being done, so far there's:<br /> <br /> Leviathan The Tempest - Lovecraft/Deep Ones<br /> Genius the Transgression - Mad Scientists<br /> Princess the Hopeful - Magical Girls/Boys<br /> Demigod the Empyrean - Demigods<br /> Siren the Drowning - Merfolk<br /> Djinn the Binding (even though mainly exists in ideas than playability) - Genies<br /> Monarch the Endless - Aliens<br /> Dragon the Embers/Inheritance - Dragons<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not saying that the Onyx Path Guys can't make gamelines out of the fangames above. Just that some parts may be similar and possible argument from the creators of the respective fangames if they're feeling gypped. I'm wondering though, does anyone play the Sims? They make use of supernaturals. Heck, playing Sims 3 and using mermaids is what sorta made me wonder &amp;quot;why isn't there a mermaid splat in the wod&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sims.wikia.com/wiki/Life_state\" target=\"_blank\">http://sims.wikia.com/wiki/Life_state</a><br /> <br /> Looking through these, the only ones that haven't been touched by the WoD is the Plantsim one and &amp;quot;Imaginary Friend&amp;quot;. But I don't know how they could carry out either of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>ArcaneArts aside (because he's a glutton for punishment) most writers avoid reading fangames entirely, and they do not factor into our decisions when pitching new games to Rich and White Wolf.<br /> <br /> The first nwod/cofd fangame I remember seeing, some ten years ago, was a Changeling game. It did not stop us from making Changeling: The Lost. Dragon and Leviathan did not stop us making Beast. Genius factors not at all into how we portray fringe science in Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T01:38:43-07:00","id":960303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960297#post960297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Leviathan did not stop us making Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no way it could. The two games have very little in common.<br /> <br /> In fact I'd go so far as to say the difference between a Makara and a Leviathan is many times larger than the difference between a Eshmaki and a Requiem Vampire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-30-2016, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T01:50:25-07:00","id":960307,"title":"","content":"Something I haven't seen played with a lot is service to humanity. One of the unifying themes of CofD is that humanity is an unalloyed good thing, for all its warts, and doing a light subversion of that seems like an interesting direction to go. It overlaps a little with Deviant and Promethean, but the tone is significantly different from revenge or redemption... but I'm not really sure what that tone <i>is</i>. But make a splat with some created purpose, where it's clear that being subservient makes sense and is a good thing... but... it's ultimately pretty terrible for you and you need to figure out how to balance that. The antagonists would be those who go all-in on service, to make it more clear that that's <i>not</i> what you're actually supposed to do.<br /> <br /> Hm.<br /> <br /> I could also see something interesting playing off the kind of domain-management that Beast has, or Mummy's cult-management. I'd start with Ents or Dryads, and make it about putting down semi-metaphorical roots in the community. Have some &quot;Law and Order&quot; versus &quot;Chaos and Growth&quot; things going on. Have some significant problems when important people decide to move away from your community, such that it's actually a big power-loss for you, so it's very tempting to entangle them and make them stay, but that has its own problems. What happens when you <i>make</i> people breed, because that strengthens you, for instance? Can reflect on whether or not some forests are the result of going too far and stagnating everything into a non-city, perhaps. Definitely some Beast there, so probably needs another something to differentiate.<br /> <br /> I'd kinda like to see a mechanic where the power stat gets crossed with the subjective stat into a 2d graph, but I'm not even sure how the math would work.<br /> <br /> There's also Moai statues, and sun worship; I feel like there might be something there to mine. (I may have been reading Erfworld lately.)<br /> <br /> Hm. Also, Greek Muses seem like a neat little seed, though I think there's a fansplat that tried to tap into that already. Kinda want to reference Simmons' muses in Iliad, Gaiman's Calliope, and Plato's daemon all in one there. The push-pull between creating inspiration and creating mania. Not really sure what they'd do when they're not tinkering with mortals, though, or what the power spectrum would really look like.<br /> <br /> I would like to see a mature take on religion. Not really sure how to go about that.<br /> <br /> Also wonder if it'd be possible to do economic horror. I know <i>Red Markets</i> is aiming somewhere around that; don't know where exactly it'll land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T01:55:04-07:00","id":960308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960234#post960234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... ghosts? Like in Wraith? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this not territory is eaten by <b>Geist</b> line? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:17:32-07:00","id":960309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960307#post960307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I haven't seen played with a lot is service to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of feels like Mummy's thematic territory. Sure you're not in service to humanity as a whole conceptually, but thematically it's still about character that are bound in service to others, and how that's often not really the best thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:20:23-07:00","id":960311,"title":"","content":"Not entirely sure that it counts as a &quot;monster&quot;, but what about something involving time travel, or rather the paradoxes therein? Be it from carelessness, malice or the good intentions that paved Hell's paths, careless actions in the past create the problems people were send to eradicate if not worse ones. Alternatively, you go back in time to change something...and you have the power to change so many wrongs. What kind of person would only do it for a certain set of gains, and how would they feel if they wanted to go and help everyone but couldn't due to some limitation? How would it feel to go back in time to fix your loved ones' fatal cancer, only to give them a rapid flesh eating disease that evolved thanks to your time travel equipment? Worse, messing with your own past to prevent your own time travel?<br /> <br /> Perhaps not a monster story, but mucking in time's backwaters (thank you Big Finish) can definitely be a source for horror. I know that Demons, Mages and to some degree Changelings can affect time, but in a limited fashion. Imagine giving the reigns of that horse to someone who wouldn't know how to get it to walk and how to get it to buck and throw them off?<br /> <br /> Alternate timelines and space aliens seem appropriate, but I'm not too sure - the Mirrors supplements rather handily showed how any gameline could be edited to such a game.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a game idea where someone goes about their lives and then, out of nowhere, they come to the startling and undeniable fact that not only are they not human, nothing about them was ever human? That they were made to fit in with humanity for some purpose, but now they are breaking down and can never be human again? That the world was a fine puppet show, except now the audience is realizing that they are not actually part of it? I admit, it sounds like Fetch: The Game, except in this case there was no life that they took the place of. The life was fabricated out of nowhere...<br /> <br /> I dunno, these are ideas I've had before for fansplats and it just never really worked. Just thought I'd throw my two cents in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T03:28:33-07:00","id":960326,"title":"","content":"Maybe we should think less about which archetype doesn't have a gameline yet and think more along the lines of what storytelling themes haven't been explored yet that a new gameline could revolve around in a unique way. So far we have..<br /> <br /> Vampire: Addiction and lust<br /> Werewolf: Violence, savagery, animism, companionship and a carnivorous cosmos<br /> Mage: Hubris and capital M Mystery<br /> Promethean: Isolation, birth, rejection, and the meaning of humanity<br /> Changeling: Identity issues and living with trauma<br /> Hunter: Gazing into the abyss and taking a stand against overwhelming odds<br /> Geist: Second chances and what is owed to the dead<br /> Mummy: Memory, civilization and slavery <br /> Demon: Paranoia and living a lie<br /> Beast: Family, the unconscious, fear, and the myth of &quot;heroes&quot; vs &quot;villains&quot;<br /> Deviant: Vengeance and transhumanism <br /> <br /> I am over simplifying these but with all those games you can sum up what they are about in several words or a short sentence. So now let's look at the most common unused archetypes in myth and horror and see if whether a game could focus around them or not.<br /> <br /> Mad Scientists: Failure, bitterness, broken dreams.<br /> Sea Monsters: I don't even know. The unknown? <br /> Genies: Slavery, be careful what you wish for.<br /> Angels: Obedience.<br /> Ghosts: How lives never &quot;end&quot; and echo throughout history. Memory.<br /> Aliens: Being an outsider in the most literal sense of the term.<br /> Dragons: Glory and hubris.<br /> Zombies: Hunger and greed<br /> <br /> As we can see pretty much every single one of the themes these archetypes are associated with have already been done in previous games. I'm not coming down on fan games. Personally I enjoy reading them and consider Genius and Leviathan as part of my head canon. But I think for future Darkness games we shouldn't try to force things. Beast and Deviant are creating entirely new supernaturals drawn from a massive array of inspirations. I expect any future games will be similar. Taking themes, archetypes, and fears that have yet to be used and creating something unique.<br /> <br /> To be honest though I still want my Reptilian: Why Won't Anyone Believe Me and Sasquatch: The Blurry Footage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 08-30-2016, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:09:59-07:00","id":960335,"title":"","content":"I'd like to play as a supernatural parasite of some kind (literal parasite - it lives inside the bodies of people or other supernaturals. For agency purposes, it probably subsumes control). <br /> <br /> It'd be a good way to explore themes of dependance, and the struggle to break free and be your own being, self-actualized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:17:14-07:00","id":960337,"title":"","content":"There's one question I always wanted to ask: Why not a science fiction world of darkness? Since the begining there has always been a focus on mythological monsters because they're the most known, but Science Fiction has plenty of horror. That way you could include aliens and many more science fiction monsters and concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:26:50-07:00","id":960340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960337#post960337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one question I always wanted to ask: Why not a science fiction world of darkness? Since the begining there has always been a focus on mythological monsters because they're the most known, but Science Fiction has plenty of horror. That way you could include aliens and many more science fiction monsters and concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Looks at Promethean, Ordo Dracul, Demon, God-Machine Chronicle, Changeling (this one can be argued), Hunter, Bleeding Edge, Infinite Macabre, and Deviant*<br /> I think there is Sci-Fi in world of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-30-2016, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:38:29-07:00","id":960346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left#post960027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...willingness to completely alter the narrative (Demon being about renegade eldritch program spies...</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that's the <i>narrative</i> - just the window dressing. It's still a game about fallen angels. Anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960102#post960102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Promethean gave us mummies first, and Immortals gave us the Purified- and yet we still got a new game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll never really understand this. I'll grant you that yes, <b>Immortals</b> was meant as the one-book quick-fix for mummies since it didn't seem they'd be getting the update, but Osiran Prometheans don't really scratch the mummy itch. If I go and watch a mummy movie I'm not seeing them wake up after thousands of years to chase down tomb robbers who stole their magic treasure and flinging around Biblical miracles (that last bit not in all mummy films, though), and I'm not seeing cinematic mummies really long to be human and go on a spiritual journey to find internal and external acceptance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960121#post960121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gill-man is a bit flat for a game. He's a cryptid at best, with simple bestial motivations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies faced a similar predicament: &quot;What's cool about playing a near-mindless slave who just protects ancient tombs?&quot; Answer? &quot;Uh, well how about a game where they try to reclaim their autonomy and break free their enslavement?&quot; Like...oh, duh, how did I not think of that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960119#post960119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so you know, the term &quot;gypped&quot; comes from the word &quot;gypsy&quot; and its use as a colloquial for being tricked or ripped off is based on negative stereotypes about the Romani. I'm sure you didn't mean it offensively, a lot of people don't even realize how offensive the turn of phrase is, but as an informal, black text warning, just be aware that it <i>is</i> offensive, and you should be careful with it in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard people get offended by this, so that's new to me. &quot;Geez&quot; comes from &quot;Jesus&quot; which takes the Lord's name in vain and surely there are those who will be offended, so we shouldn't say &quot;geez&quot; here anymore either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T04:48:42-07:00","id":960353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960340#post960340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Looks at Promethean, Ordo Dracul, Demon, God-Machine Chronicle, Changeling (this one can be argued), Hunter, Bleeding Edge, Infinite Macabre, and Deviant*<br /> I think there is Sci-Fi in world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's fantasy with some sci fi in it. I'm talking about pure Sci fi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T05:15:34-07:00","id":960369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960353#post960353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's fantasy with some sci fi in it. I'm talking about pure Sci fi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of that is fantasy with some sci-fi, though GM/Demon/Infinite Macabre/Bleeding Edge are not (though Infinite Macabre does have content for supernatuals in it, it's Sci-Fi with some fantasy in it), and in Hunter and Deviant supernatural &quot;Can&quot; be part of it, but has no reason to, you can just use super science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-30-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T06:10:03-07:00","id":960385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960346#post960346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never heard people get offended by this, so that's new to me. &quot;Geez&quot; comes from &quot;Jesus&quot; which takes the Lord's name in vain and surely there are those who will be offended, so we shouldn't say &quot;geez&quot; here anymore either?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about offense, we're talking about harm against a still oppressed group in many parts of the world, but in case you were being totally serious at the end, there, we're also not talking about &quot;someone said something that sort of invokes something negative in my religion, where I'm not a member of a traditionally oppressed group&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not difficult to pull these articles, hundreds of thousands came up with a simple search, so attaching just one here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://europe.newsweek.com/officials-warn-modern-racism-against-roma-commemorations-forgotten-holocaust-331172\" target=\"_blank\">http://europe.newsweek.com/officials...locaust-331172</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T06:17:23-07:00","id":960390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960307#post960307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a mature take on religion. Not really sure how to go about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Separate from OPP, an OPP writer is currently making a game along these lines! Not sure how much he wants me to say right now, so if you want to know more, I can ask him what I'm allowed to share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T06:32:13-07:00","id":960397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960308#post960308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this not territory is eaten by <b>Geist</b> line? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I totally think there's room for a Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:01:24-07:00","id":960412,"title":"","content":"Aliens, Demigods and Timetravellers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T07:23:08-07:00","id":960422,"title":"","content":"Clowns. Not even joking. Oh, you can do clowns in other games, but c'mon, imagine a hidden society of Pennywises, Twistys, and Jokers. Monsters that can hide in plain sight, are invited into parties, and are dismissed as threats by all but the innocent. That's who they feed on. They don't do anything so crass as drink blood, or eating souls. They feed on trust, wonder, and laughter, turning people against the light, and hardening them against life's joys. Yeah, they hate themselves for it, but that's the price of survival. Clowns are as cursed as any vampire or changeling. They aren't alone in the darkness, and the best of them use their stolen mirth to hold off the elder terrors who would use all of humanity as their playthings. Rakshasa, primarily, because I haven't bothered to flesh out this aspect, but hungry, bored devils who are too dangerous to be unleashed on the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T08:48:23-07:00","id":960467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960422#post960422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clowns. Not even joking. Oh, you can do clowns in other games, but c'mon, imagine a hidden society of Pennywises, Twistys, and Jokers. Monsters that can hide in plain sight, are invited into parties, and are dismissed as threats by all but the innocent. That's who they feed on. They don't do anything so crass as drink blood, or eating souls. They feed on trust, wonder, and laughter, turning people against the light, and hardening them against life's joys. Yeah, they hate themselves for it, but that's the price of survival. Clowns are as cursed as any vampire or changeling. They aren't alone in the darkness, and the best of them use their stolen mirth to hold off the elder terrors who would use all of humanity as their playthings. Rakshasa, primarily, because I haven't bothered to flesh out this aspect, but hungry, bored devils who are too dangerous to be unleashed on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... I can't even.... clown are people, you know? By making a splat dedicated specifically to clowns as a form of a monster, I can't even begin to say how inappropriate it may be- and this is from someone who is scared from clowns in general. It's just... something you shouldn't do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:32:10-07:00","id":960493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960422#post960422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clowns. Not even joking. Oh, you can do clowns in other games, but c'mon, imagine a hidden society of Pennywises, Twistys, and Jokers. Monsters that can hide in plain sight, are invited into parties, and are dismissed as threats by all but the innocent. That's who they feed on. They don't do anything so crass as drink blood, or eating souls. They feed on trust, wonder, and laughter, turning people against the light, and hardening them against life's joys. Yeah, they hate themselves for it, but that's the price of survival. Clowns are as cursed as any vampire or changeling. They aren't alone in the darkness, and the best of them use their stolen mirth to hold off the elder terrors who would use all of humanity as their playthings. Rakshasa, primarily, because I haven't bothered to flesh out this aspect, but hungry, bored devils who are too dangerous to be unleashed on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aren't clowns handled under Beast already (due to the Primal Fear, thing)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:35:01-07:00","id":960497,"title":"","content":"Well, you could same the same about Deviants, really. Or the twisted core of Changeling. And I'm not talking about all clowns, most, or even the profession. That these things exist are their cover, why they can exist in plain sight. But grease paint and stage magic are about obfuscation. There are legitimate entertainers, of a profession dating back to the dawn of time, and there are stories surrounding them, about haunted dolls, disappearing children, clowns whose faces aren't made up at all. There are stories about jesters who appeased gods and monsters, trickster gods, and performers who wanted to be loved and were trapped in their roles.<br /> <br /> And do a news search for clowns, right now. We're on the cusp of a great and terrible harlequin eschaton.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm thinking a more terrifying name than &quot;clown&quot;, like &quot;Grotesque: the Carnival&quot;. Some distance between reality and fantasy, naturally. Hunters and magicians are real life professions, but we can separate them from horror tropes too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T09:44:42-07:00","id":960505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960390#post960390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Separate from OPP, an OPP writer is currently making a game along these lines! Not sure how much he wants me to say right now, so if you want to know more, I can ask him what I'm allowed to share.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, yeah. Primarily because it's so unclear to me what I'm looking for that anything that helps me refine that peaks my interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T10:39:36-07:00","id":960536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960346#post960346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never heard people get offended by this, so that's new to me. &quot;Geez&quot; comes from &quot;Jesus&quot; which takes the Lord's name in vain and surely there are those who will be offended, so we shouldn't say &quot;geez&quot; here anymore either?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Jeez imply that a marginalized group of people are thieves and con artists? Does it imply anything negative about any group of people? No? Then why would I care if you say it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T12:34:44-07:00","id":960605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960119#post960119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so you know, the term &quot;gypped&quot; comes from the word &quot;gypsy&quot; and its use as a colloquial for being tricked or ripped off is based on negative stereotypes about the Romani. I'm sure you didn't mean it offensively, a lot of people don't even realize how offensive the turn of phrase is, but as an informal, black text warning, just be aware that it <i>is</i> offensive, and you should be careful with it in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T12:36:05-07:00","id":960606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960605#post960605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:05:10-07:00","id":960626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960308#post960308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this not territory is eaten by <b>Geist</b> line? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda, I guess. The monster itself is still not being used, only people who relates to ghosts. I think a Wraith game could work really well with Geist, adding to it instead of conflicting to it like the Yin to it's Yang. Geist's symbol is the key, but Wraith's symbol is the lock, after all.<br /> <br /> The thematic would be very different, as it deals with being dead itself. Perhaps like Promethean having a final objective, like transcending or something like that. Also, I think like most CofD games it should take inspiration from Oblivion, but do it's own take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:22:29-07:00","id":960637,"title":"","content":"How about<br /> \u200bPolitician: The Corrupt, power without purpose.<br /> A game about monsters who push social agendas they don't believe in for the acquisition of power and influence, with no care for the consequences.<br /> Boring I know but even Vampires work to ensure their own survival, only the rare few can say they destroyed and murdered many just for self aggrandizement.\u200b<br /> How does the saying go? Kill one man and you are a murderer, kill twelve and you are a psychopath, kill a hundred and you are a president, but kill millions and you are a god!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 08-30-2016, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:46:32-07:00","id":960650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960637#post960637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about<br /> \u200bPolitician: The Corrupt, power without purpose.<br /> A game about monsters who push social agendas they don't believe in for the acquisition of power and influence, with no care for the consequences.<br /> Boring I know but even Vampires work to ensure their own survival, only the rare few can say they destroyed and murdered many just for self aggrandizement.\u200b<br /> How does the saying go? Kill one man and you are a murderer, kill twelve and you are a psychopath, kill a hundred and you are a president, but kill millions and you are a god!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is falling under the same problem as the Clown suggestion; namely, it's not a good idea turning actual people doing a job into monsters. Politics, as noted, are used by monsters and the consequences therein can be monstrous, but turning an occupation and those who fill it into a supernatural creature is not that tasteful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:47:17-07:00","id":960787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960536#post960536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Jeez imply that a marginalized group of people are thieves and con artists? Does it imply anything negative about any group of people? No? Then why would I care if you say it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because no one says &quot;jipped&quot; with the intention of calling someone &quot;a stereotype of an untrustworthy Roma.&quot; On top of being irrelevant to the fact that there are Christians who do take offense to &quot;geez&quot; nonetheless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:59:59-07:00","id":960793,"title":"","content":"I wonder if something could be done with a djinn/genie game. Changeling and Demon have both eaten up a lot of the deal-making stuff in Pledge and Pacts, respectively, and Mummy has the idea of being in service to mortal masters, but I think there's room for a unique spin on things. I also do think a suitably interesting Alien splat, provided that it tried to play nice with the more supernatural bent of the CofD. Maybe that's just me being bitter about Outsider crumbling, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960787#post960787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because no one says &quot;jipped&quot; with the intention of calling someone &quot;a stereotype of an untrustworthy Roma.&quot; On top of being irrelevant to the fact that there are Christians who do take offense to &quot;geez&quot; nonetheless</div> </div> </div> </div>Reseru, I'm coming to you as a friend; there is literally no reason to defend your stance. My boyfriend is Romani and people of his ethnicity are horribly mistreated on a systemic level throughout Europe due to their stereotypical reputation as criminals. Intent to offend does not matter. Would you call someone a shyster, knowing that term has been sometimes associated with anti-Semitism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:23:54-07:00","id":960806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960787#post960787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because no one says &quot;jipped&quot; with the intention of calling someone &quot;a stereotype of an untrustworthy Roma.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't stop it from being hurtful to Romani to hear. Most people who use &quot;retarded&quot; to refer to things they find stupid don't do it with the intent of attacking people with developmental disabilities. Most poeple who use &quot;gay&quot; to refer to things they don't like don't do it with the intent of attacking people who are attracted to people of the same sex or gender. They're still not ok things to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960787#post960787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of being irrelevant to the fact that there are Christians who do take offense to &quot;geez&quot; nonetheless</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about whether or not people are offended. I don't know if anyone on these forums is Romani or not, nor do I know if any Romani posters are offended by the statement in question. I do know that a term that is derived from harmful stereotypes against an oppressed group is such an ingrained part of the colloquial lexicon that people use it without even realizing the implications or caring that it might be hurtful to someone listening (or reading). It's not a question of whether or not people will be offended by an idiom - It's a big world out there, and for pretty much any combination of words, there's probably someone out there who would be offended by it. It's a question of whether or not an idiom contributes to an ongoing pattern of oppression against a group of people. I am well aware that there are Christians who would be offended by me saying &quot;Jesus Christ&quot;, or even &quot;jeez&quot; as an expression of exasperation. But Christians are not an oppressed group of people, and more importantly in the context of these forums, neither of those idioms imply anything negative about Christians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:02:58-07:00","id":960818,"title":"","content":"Everybody calm down... it's clear that the monster OP needs to do next is evil dolls and ventriloquist dummy that turn their owners into puppets to carry out their will. And just as our fear of clowns was justified in many people's minds by John Wayne Gacy, our fear of ventriloquist dummies was vindicated by <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_23080_6-absurd-horror-movie-plots-that-actually-happened.html\" target=\"_blank\">Ronald </a>Brown, who is a puppet of his evil dummies if I have ever seen a man turned into a puppet of his evil dummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:12:21-07:00","id":960848,"title":"","content":"What about a D.N. Angel approach? That is, art pieces turned living beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:30:43-07:00","id":960909,"title":"","content":"I hate to double post, but one idea I just had that also relate to time travel is temporal anomolies - that is, people from timelines that are not their own, caused by a temporal portal (a person walking through a doorway from one timeline into another), being summoned by an entity, or just simply being the leftovers of a messy paradox (such as a person whose parents now never met yet is still alive). However they went through, the event changes them, meaning that even if they came back to their normal timeline (should it still exist) they are unable to return as they once were. They know of the changes to time, and are resistant to powers that would alter their past or stop them in time. Their memory of events could be entirely off too - for example, Project VALKYRIE could be named Project YGGDRASIL in their timeline, should they be aware of Hunters, or maybe Vampires have a weakness to helium instead of light. Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:47:27-07:00","id":960917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960848#post960848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a D.N. Angel approach? That is, art pieces turned living beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar wou D.N. Angel, but this brief description sounds like Prometheans to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:49:15-07:00","id":960919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960909#post960909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to double post, but one idea I just had that also relate to time travel is temporal anomolies - that is, people from timelines that are not their own, caused by a temporal portal (a person walking through a doorway from one timeline into another), being summoned by an entity, or just simply being the leftovers of a messy paradox (such as a person whose parents now never met yet is still alive). However they went through, the event changes them, meaning that even if they came back to their normal timeline (should it still exist) they are unable to return as they once were. They know of the changes to time, and are resistant to powers that would alter their past or stop them in time. Their memory of events could be entirely off too - for example, Project VALKYRIE could be named Project YGGDRASIL in their timeline, should they be aware of Hunters, or maybe Vampires have a weakness to helium instead of light. Just an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you proposing Quantum Leap as a horror game? Because that works better than it has any right too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T00:07:13-07:00","id":960928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960917#post960917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar wou D.N. Angel, but this brief description sounds like Prometheans to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a manga about a teen named Daisuke who, due to a genetic curse, becomes Kaito Dark after he falls in love and transforms when he has strong feelings for said person. Dark then goes about stealing various works of art, assisted by a being who becomes black wings for him to use. Most of the series is about said thefts and love shennanigains, but there are a lot of (later) stories that are around works of art that are alive in some way, even taking on humanoid forms; I admit the concept is a bit too close to Promethean though, or Changeling even.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960919#post960919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you proposing Quantum Leap as a horror game? Because that works better than it has any right too.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've seen an episode of Quantum Leap (I believe it was one where the main character became a woman temporarily) but I wasnt really thinking of it when I suggested the story. I was more thinking of Elizabeth Klein from Big Finish's Doctor Who range. Both work though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T03:27:28-07:00","id":960967,"title":"","content":"Something has to be done with the Deep Space.<br /> <br /> That said, hybridity (and monstrous descent that will manifest) and slow contamination (promoting transformation) are themes not yet worked.<br /> <br /> Nor cults dilettantes messing with forces beyond comprehension and even cults hysterical hyper-socialized in their artificial atmospheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T03:38:50-07:00","id":960970,"title":"","content":"Another thing I like is a line of Changing Breeds. In the opposite direction of Lobisomem, animals and criptideos (as Gargoyles) chosen by primal forces to share a human form and time, but not born human, nor were human, no spiritual connections (except to its creators that can treat an axis ye may be things like the sun, the trickster, the sea, the time, etc.) as forces of change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:49:49-07:00","id":961023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960787#post960787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because no one says &quot;jipped&quot; with the intention of calling someone &quot;a stereotype of an untrustworthy Roma.&quot; On top of being irrelevant to the fact that there are Christians who do take offense to &quot;geez&quot; nonetheless</div> </div> </div> </div>And here are the two problems.<br /> <br /> I'll try to address them in an understandable way.<br /> <br /> Your intention is completely and totally irrelevant. Really. Racist things aren't only racist if you mean for them to be. Really. If you step on someone's foot and accidentally break their toe, you don't sit there wondering why they're crying. Instead of talking about what you ~meant~ to do, let's talk about what you actually did. Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> Second thing: We're running into understanding issues because you think we're talking about offense. We're not. Really. To be frank, I don't care if you or anyone else is offended. Offense is not what concerns me. I care about harm. And that's what you're missing. We're not talking about someone getting offended. We're talking about harm that perpetuates oppressive systems. You're going to keep having these misunderstandings as long as you think that your intention matters, and as long as you think we're talking about offense, like &quot;a black person called me cracker one time&quot; is as bad as a white man calling someone the n-word. I'm sure white men do get very offended when they're called cracker. I don't care about offense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T09:21:54-07:00","id":961083,"title":"","content":"The mods have good intentions, they want to protect a minority of people who have been prosectuted and torments across muchvof Europe. This is a morally understandible thing to do, to try and stand up for the oppressed.<br /> <br /> But there inability to pick they're battles intelligently leads to it back firing and making things worse.<br /> <br /> You want to do something for the Romani, have a really cool and accurate Romani character, with an engaging hook, but don' draw attention to it with excessive back patting.<br /> <br /> What making a big deal about this world being used in way that wasn't intended, did was create a natural defensive response, so they push back, then the thread gets detailed by a back and forth over this word and the core fact that everyone essentially agrees that the Romani have a shitty deal, especially in Europe.<br /> <br /> So what would make a Romani feel more like an outsider/self conscious, that one use of a common word with a very unfortunate history, or mods that make it thing, triggering a defensive reaction, that in turn gets a defensive reaction from the mods, that then causes things just get worse and worse.<br /> <br /> We can see what happens when authority figures don't wisely pick their battles, and instead go petty, the history of law enforcemet is filled with it, and its lead to far too many men dead from police over really minor stuff.<br /> <br /> Now obviously things won't escalate that far, but the essential truth is still there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:04:17-07:00","id":961097,"title":"","content":"... Yeah, fuck that. I have lived and worked in Eastern Europe. Those are my friends you want to slur because thinking about what you say is too hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:38:43-07:00","id":961112,"title":"","content":"I want to slurred? I didn't say it and I didn't use the term.<br /> <br /> My only point was leading by example is more effective. I don't believe anyone intended to slur anybody.<br /> <br /> Look all I want is for everyone to cool down.<br /> <br /> I used to be hyper politically correct like you, and all it ever did was make things worse. No one here is anti Romani, everyone here agrees with you that the Romani have gotten a shitty deal historically, from Nazi consentration camps to discrimination and so much more.<br /> <br /> I'm not the enemy, I have alot of sympathy of the Romani people and have on repeated occasions defended the Romani to a Yugoslavian friend who sadly importanted his prejuidices with him.<br /> <br /> Look I have done the giving people shit for using certain words thing since I was a kid, and it might feel good, but it doesn't get the results you want, greater understanding and tolerence.<br /> <br /> You know what does really work in my experience? Meeting people like the Romani, that they can really relate to, that are top notch people, that are fucking awesome, then focusing on them not as Romani, but just really awesome people, that have simular life concerns that they do.<br /> <br /> They don't even have to be real people at first, fictional characters that represent what the Romani have to offer for example.<br /> <br /> Please tell me you understand what I'm trying to get at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:28:07-07:00","id":961127,"title":"","content":"I don't get how its &quot;hyper politically correct&quot; to ask that people not use a particular word. No one is saying that they can't express the same opinion with different word choice. <br /> <br /> I used to say things like &quot;gay&quot; and &quot;retarded&quot; all the time, and at first I didn't really see why people objected. I still stopped using them though because 'lo and behold <i>not using them didn't harm or even effect me in any way.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:44:13-07:00","id":961139,"title":"","content":"Maybe this conversation belongs in a different thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:52:41-07:00","id":961144,"title":"","content":"On the original topic: I've had notes for a while on a prospective fan game centering on &quot;The Possessed.&quot; Species splat is determined by the entity possessing you (ghost, demon, Loa, etc.), an organizational splat determined by broad philosophical approaches to the problem (denial, control, redemption, etc.), and general themes of autonomy, identity, and the loss thereof. Unfortunately it all shares a little too much space with Geist, Beast, Mummy, the Lucifuge, and I strongly suspect Deviant. As such unless I can come up with a fresh angle on it they're probably just going to stay notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:18:23-07:00","id":961198,"title":"","content":"This question gets asked after every new game. And yet, it hasn't stopped anyone yet.<br /> ....<br /> <br /> I still vote for that Fury / valkyrie game of David Hill's. You play an avenging angel, but do you really like being told to kill, and what about not killing people you think actually deserve it? I'm honestly still in love with that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-31-2016, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:52:29-07:00","id":961221,"title":"","content":"...I'm sorry for saying the word that started this huge discussion/argument on the romani. &gt;&lt;&quot; <br /> <br /> Anyways, I have another idea for a possible splat. Giants. Titans. Pretty much, the idea of the primordial things that shaped the world into existence, but they lacked the ability to communicate as it seemed. They were unable to interact with reality without damaging it in some way or without massive difficulties in doing so, and for this, the very beings they created rose up and sealed them away or destroyed them. The themes I can imagine is the attempt to connect to reality, to be fully in sync with it. Without the ability to have a gentle hand, they risk destroying everything they touch. <br /> <br /> The idea above also sounds like a good idea, the Valkyrie/Fury game. Heck, perhaps it could be something like Hunter the Reckoning in the CoD? I'm just musing ofc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:14:21-07:00","id":961228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961198#post961198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still vote for that Fury / valkyrie game of David Hill's. You play an avenging angel, but do you really like being told to kill, and what about not killing people you think actually deserve it? I'm honestly still in love with that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes please. I want this so hard. The few pages David posted on his blog were not enough to sate me.<br /> <br /> Even if they get turned into a minor splat instead of a full book, I'd still be <i>very<b> very</b></i> happy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:17:36-07:00","id":961231,"title":"","content":"What about some kind of item finding itself inserted into a person's soul, something with an intense emotional connection to the world, that causes a dramatic change to both the person and the soul itself. Effectively, a person is possessed by the possession, and they get both a compulsion and abilities that allow them to re-enact how that item was used. A person possessed by an iPod may have the compulsion to sing constantly, or perhaps to do podcasts; a weapon would cause its possessed to be more threatening, or even to cause harm or kill; a key would naturally make someone want to open doors, possibly to pick locks. The item wouldn't be sentient, but its new connection to the soul would cause it to have some form of life.<br /> <br /> I dunno, it's another idea I've been having for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:29:42-07:00","id":961241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961083#post961083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Wants authorities to pick their battles more carefully to avoid derailing threads*</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Is largely on-topic*</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961083#post961083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*picks the same battle to make their point, continuing to derail the thread*</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961112#post961112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Says all they want is for everyone to cool down*</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Everyone</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Is cool*</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961112#post961112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Encourages people to lead by example*</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T16:35:27-07:00","id":961280,"title":"","content":"I have a weak spot for Basque mythology because, well, it was only written down once christian monks felt like gathering the Lore, and that means that what we've got is both incomplete and biased. So, what happens with Gods whose followers are killed, or whose followers forget them? I don't know if this is covered anywhere, but it could be interesting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:17:20-07:00","id":961319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode