 Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, my boyfriend is a Romani immigrant from Eastern Eyrope /and/ a White Wolf fan who endured years of Ravnos bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>slight derail, but I will be quick about it.<br /> <br /> Does it count as stereotyping Romani if the stereotype is an in-universe one that doesn't exist in real life due to alternate history stuff? I am asking because in novel's setting, the stereotype people have of Romani is that they are all uberwealthy farmers, family members of such or are otherwise involved in agribussiness. In universe reason being that it's an open magic setting and while trying to figure out how vampires exist openly, I discovered a romani folktale about &quot;vampire watermelons and pumpkins&quot; that produce blood instead of melon/pumpkin juice and I figured most vampires usually just drink the blood fruit juice with real blood being a treat for special occasions. Anyway, I didn't comfortable having a different ethic group be the ones that profit of a produce of romani folklore, so I just had the romani get rich growing the plants to sell to vampires because who says my alternate history has to be as hard on the romani as the real world.... is that alright?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb