y on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:56:44-07:00","id":961689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961668#post961668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, there is the Dark Hero from Mirrors- sure, chances of it gaining future support are slim, but it is already a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, with only a little settings hacking you could easily turn players in CoD into superheroes. Beasts in particular have aa ironic propensity for being like supers as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:27:52-07:00","id":961712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961689#post961689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, with only a little settings hacking you could easily turn players in CoD into superheroes. Beasts in particular have aa ironic propensity for being like supers as it stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supervillains or anti-heroes, maybe. Mages (and Proximi) make good ones as well (especially leveraging their Shadow Names). Demon has alternate identities Covered (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:29:27-07:00","id":961714,"title":"","content":"If only most supernaturals didn't <i>prey</i> on humans in some way, that is.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-01-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:36:27-07:00","id":961723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961714#post961714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only most supernaturals didn't <i>prey</i> on humans in some way, that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, most don't, really. Or don't have to. Vampires do. Beasts do. Changelings, <i>maybe</i> depending on what they are doing for glamour. Werewolves <i>can</i>, but don't need to. Mages straight up don't need to. Nor Mummies. Prometheans either (though them being near has other consequences). Demons, it depends on the terms and aspects of the Pacts (there isn't anything preventing them from being mutually beneficial). Deviants, no clue, but I doubt it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This isn't to say they can't (or in most cases, don't) use or exploit humans. But very few have the requirement as part of their nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:43:46-07:00","id":961727,"title":"","content":"Vampires got to suck that blood.<br /> Werewolves are less scary about eating people as they are about the deadly hair trigger tempers.<br /> Changelings (and fae in general) suck the will out of people when they're not murderous Huntsmen.<br /> Prometheans poison everything around them.<br /> Mage nimbi (nimbuses?) twist the very nature of everyone that mage is close to.<br /> Demons bargain for bits of your soul.<br /> Beasts are natural sadists that literally feed off of pain, loss and suffering.<br /> <br /> Mortal psychics are pretty much the only 2e supernaturals that don't have a natural way of screwing over humanity just by existing. Everyone, by their nature, are dangerous to humanity in some way. And that's the good guys. <br /> <br /> Remember, these are <i>monsters</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:57:58-07:00","id":961732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961624#post961624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus I think my Succubus/Incubus idea explores very different themes then Beast over all, Beast is about fear and hunger, Succubus/Incubus would be about how do you deal with a judgemental society when your sexual nature is so outside the normal and taboo.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't indulgance in the taboo a Vampire thing? And the whole consequence-even-with-consent thing? Totally Vampire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T09:59:18-07:00","id":961733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961727#post961727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires got to suck that blood.<br /> Werewolves are less scary about eating people as they are about the deadly hair trigger tempers.<br /> Changelings (and fae in general) suck the will out of people when they're not murderous Huntsmen.<br /> Prometheans poison everything around them.<br /> Mage nimbi (nimbuses?) twist the very nature of everyone that mage is close to.<br /> Demons bargain for bits of your soul.<br /> Beasts are natural sadists that literally feed off of pain, loss and suffering.<br /> <br /> Mortal psychics are pretty much the only 2e supernaturals that don't have a natural way of screwing over humanity just by existing. Everyone, by their nature, are dangerous to humanity in some way. And that's the good guys.<br /> <br /> Remember, these are <i>monsters</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danger to != prey upon.<br /> <br /> And hey, Sin-Eaters are helpful. Most times. Depending on the Archetype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:07:40-07:00","id":961742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961733#post961733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Danger to != prey upon.</div> </div> </div> </div> Putting aside the quibble on word choice, though, it doesn't change that the CofD gameline PCs are still monsters. Even hunters and sin-eaters are meant to be monsters that are at odds with the mortals around them. Making that kind of being into a superhero is highly questionable.<br /> <br /> Not that there couldn't be a superhero game, but the current games really don't support that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:16:35-07:00","id":961861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961632#post961632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking maybe being fed off by Succubus/Incubus risks/causes sterility and some kind of negative consquence depending on fetish or taint, like risk of a supernatural STD.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is the problem with being too on the nose with the metaphor.<br /> <br /> You just (and I don't mean to say you want this to be the case, but it's the result of mixing the metaphor with the consequences needed for the CofD) made this &quot;The Gays Spread AIDS on Purpose: The Prudes are Right to Stop Them.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you make the narrative a direct metaphor for the oppression of a real world group, and then turn the protagonists into supernatural STD monsters... you just made the metaphor that the real world oppressed group are a disease, and the antagonists are actually right to hunt them down and stop them.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not that a game that explores the themes you're talking about can't work, but it needs to tread lightly (I mean look at the backlash Beast got).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:51:25-07:00","id":961884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961861#post961861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this is the problem with being too on the nose with the metaphor.<br /> <br /> You just (and I don't mean to say you want this to be the case, but it's the result of mixing the metaphor with the consequences needed for the CofD) made this &amp;quot;The Gays Spread AIDS on Purpose: The Prudes are Right to Stop Them.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> If you make the narrative a direct metaphor for the oppression of a real world group, and then turn the protagonists into supernatural STD monsters... you just made the metaphor that the real world oppressed group are a disease, and the antagonists are actually right to hunt them down and stop them.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not that a game that explores the themes you're talking about can't work, but it needs to tread lightly (I mean look at the backlash Beast got).</div> </div> </div> </div>My boyfriend did a Succubus/Incubus fansplat that acted as a metaphor for human trafficking, but that was just as much a bit of self-therapy as something meant for play. I'd tread very carefully on that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:55:16-07:00","id":961887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961884#post961884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My boyfriend did a Succubus/Incubus fansplat that acted as a metaphor for human trafficking, but that was just as much a bit of self-therapy as something meant for play. I'd tread very carefully on that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a CSA survivor, I'd like to read it. But no worries if he'd rather keep it to himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:51:18-07:00","id":961916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960121#post960121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the question that should be asked is not, &quot;what monsters are left,&quot; but rather, &quot;what kind of monster stories are left?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In that vein, we don't really have a monster that's a parallel evolution alongside humanity - a metaphysical and moral equal, for all the better and worse that entails. The Creature from the Black Lagoon is one such, but looked at another way, so could a djinn be (even if a lot of djinn might argue the point).<br /> <br /> For those monsters with access to otherworlds, said otherworlds are usually a double-edged resource. We don't really have a monster for whom the otherworld is home, and for whom <i>Earth</i> is the double-edged resource. Again, djinn might fit that bill, as might a game based on Changeling's hobgoblins, or perhaps naga.<br /> <br /> All the monsters we have come through a very Western lens. To take a nonwestern monster, and extend its own metaphysical context into something global would be hard, but rewarding. Mummy does this to a certain extent, but still with a monster rooted in Western pop culture. The aforementioned djinn and naga could work, but really, there's an embarrassment of riches.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:37:31-07:00","id":961933,"title":"","content":"Mario Acevedo has an interesting take on how to keep aliens balanced in a World of Darkness-type setting. In his <i>Felix Gomez</i> series, Earth is sort of a Wild West for the aliens. Officially, they're not supposed to interfere . . . but the aliens aren't putting the resources in necessary to keep <i>everyone </i>out. Naturalist/sociologists run the barricade to study the humans in their natural habitat. Scientists to perform research on the strange supernatural phenomena native to Earth . . .or conduct their own &quot;side projects&quot;. Criminals to hide out. Slavers to supply the burgeoning black market in exotic &quot;pets&quot; . . .<br /> <br /> And since none of them are supposed to be here, they can't exactly radio for reinforcements or supply drops . . .<br /> <br /> A setup like that should translate well into a WoD game. Alien PCs would still have the usual need for &quot;Resources&quot; and &quot;Contacts&quot;, with new merits/backgrounds for &quot;Alien Tech&quot; or &quot;Off-world Connections&quot;. Crossovers when the aliens run afoul of other splats (&quot;Gomez&quot; revolves around escalating tensions at the vampires and aliens become aware of each other), whether for better or worse . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960307#post960307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I haven't seen played with a lot is service to humanity. One of the unifying themes of CofD is that humanity is an unalloyed good thing, for all its warts, and doing a light subversion of that seems like an interesting direction to go. It overlaps a little with Deviant and Promethean, but the tone is significantly different from revenge or redemption... but I'm not really sure what that tone <i>is</i>. But make a splat with some created purpose, where it's clear that being subservient makes sense and is a good thing... but... it's ultimately pretty terrible for you and you need to figure out how to balance that. The antagonists would be those who go all-in on service, to make it more clear that that's <i>not</i> what you're actually supposed to do.<br /> <br /> (. . .)<br /> <br /> I would like to see a mature take on religion. Not really sure how to go about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever run across the <b>Witchcraft</b>/<b>Armageddon </b>RPGs? It has both angels and saints as playable splats, handled in WoD style. As they remember it, the angels were ordered to &quot;look after&quot; humanity. Tens of thousands of years later, they're still trying to follow that order. But dissension has fractured their ranks into three factions, every day humanity comes up with new ways to tempt them, and . . . its just been so long! <br /> <br /> One faction leader preaches a very fascist version of hardcore fundamentalism as a solution. Another, wiping out humanity. And the third is pro-humanity largely because its members are hooked on vices that only humanity can supply. . .<br /> <br /> Saints/prophets/etc. could be an interesting addition to the WoD. Humans touched by divinity (for better or worse), and having to deal with the &quot;profane&quot; world Might take a bit of work, but keeping it distinct from <b>Demon</b> and <b>Mage</b> should be doable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also wonder if it'd be possible to do economic horror. I know <i>Red Markets</i> is aiming somewhere around that; don't know where exactly it'll land. </div> </div> </div>Interesting looking game . . . although I get more of a &quot;<i>Shadowrun</i> meets the zombie apocalypse&quot; vibe. Who knows, though<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:00:57-07:00","id":961945,"title":"","content":"I feel like an Alien game is one that could be done well, but it needs to fit the CofD setting: Demon is about as close to sci-fi as I think anyone is comfortable with (some might say it's already passed that point, but I think they're wrong), and that game succeeds because it's full of occultism and other High Strangeness dressed in a technological skin. Doing an actual &quot;from another planet and smashed to earth in a space ship&quot; Alien would be a thematic mismatch that would chafe with the wider setting, but drawing on some of the stuff hinted at by Werewol'f material on the idigam as strange things foreign to reality and uncomfortable with the physical world. A game about aliens from somewhere else - some sort of inner realm, or the depths of a known realm - who <i>do not belong here</i> and want to go home but cannot for whatever reason might work well.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I think there's a point to be made that maybe we don't need too many more gamelines. There's eleven of them now, and trying to get at least a single piece of new content out for each of them a year seems like a Herculean task. Vampire still doesn't have any supplements, and Werewolf and Mage each only have one, Changeling, Hunter, Geist, and Mummy still need 2e updates, Demon could use at least an antagonist book, Beast and Deviant will need full suites of supplements... I'd sooner see things focus on depth than breadth.<br /> <br /> As a side note: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a>, <i>Red Markets</i> has been awesome so far; there are several actual play podcasts for it, and I have the backer draft of the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:03:34-07:00","id":961946,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that the only real territory that could be argued for would be aliens/cosmic horror-style &quot;outsiders&quot;. Personally, I'm not someone who's particularly eager for aliens in ChroD, but I realize that I don't really have a good argument for why, it's just personal preference. <br /> <br /> Maybe have them be recent? Like, they're nomads who just discovered earth, or refugees who ended up trapped there? Even though I'm not a fan of aliens in ChroD, I still thought Alien: The Stranded looked pretty good. <br /> <br /> Though my personal preference would be to have no new lines after Deviant, and to focus on content for the existing games. You can have big things that get the players excited even without new lines- look at how excitement there was in the fandom for Dark Eras. The upcoming Crossover Chronicle is another Big Event Book that's not a new line. So I'd rather OP focused on things like that that played with their existing universe. Maybe have something like Mirrors 2e as the next kickstarted blue book? That's something I would get very excited about, and I bet plenty of others would too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:11:09-07:00","id":961951,"title":"","content":"The thing about Alien is that Alien Abductees are already covered by Changelings and Alien Invaders are already covered by Idigam and to a lesser extent Spirits. The only conceptual space I really see left fit an Alien game is Stranded Aliens.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And even that might be covered by Deviant - Area 51 eacapee, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-01-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:14:01-07:00","id":961956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961951#post961951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Alien is that Alien Abduction is already covered by Changeling and Alien Invasion is already covered by Idigam. The only conceptual space I see left fit an Alien game is stranded Aliens.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could be a space there, though - something akin to the stranded Fae from Changeling. Possibly inventing a new realm, or having the splats be based on existing realms, where the figures have to learn to be human to survive against the forces of the world itself. It would need a little work to differentiate from stranded Fae and Demon, but it could be made to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:14:56-07:00","id":961957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961951#post961951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Alien is that Alien Abductees are already covered by Changelings and Alien Invaders are already covered by Idigam and to a lesser extent Spirits. The only conceptual space I really see left fit an Alien game is Stranded Aliens.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then those are the Charlatans from Changeling! We had one as the main antagonist of an awesome chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:37:24-07:00","id":961972,"title":"","content":"How about gods? hellovg has another current thread about his idea for &quot;Celestial: the Reclamation&quot;, but this idea is a bit different. I'm not thinking about gods as some sort of some sort of being in their own right, that might draw upon the power of human worship but not require it to exist, but rather creations of the human collective unconscious. Beings made of belief, now forced to take human form and live among us, gradually being forgotten by the modern world. Think less modern-day Exalted and more Neil Gaiman's <i>American Gods</i>. There would be some vague similarities to Beast, Demon, and oWoD's CtD, but with a distinct theme and focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:39:25-07:00","id":961973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>who.is.matt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961972#post961972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about gods? hellovg has another current thread about his idea for &quot;Celestial: the Reclamation&quot;, but this idea is a bit different. I'm not thinking about gods as some sort of some sort of being in their own right, that might draw upon the power of human worship butnot require it to exist, but rather creations of the human collective unconscious. Beings made of belief, now forced to take human form and live among us, gradually being forgotten by the modern world. Think less modern-day Exalted and more Neil Gaiman's <i>American Gods</i>. There would be some vague similarities to Beast, Demon, and oWoD's CtD, but with a distinct theme and focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>With <i>Scion 2e </i>Kickstarting literally this month, I'm not sure you're gonna have much luck with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:45:48-07:00","id":961977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961973#post961973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With <i>Scion 2e </i>Kickstarting literally this month, I'm not sure you're gonna have much luck with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion is actually pretty much nothing like I'm thinking at all, except that it deals with gods. Scion is more like <i>Percy Jackson &amp; the Olympians</i>, which has very few similarities to <i>American Gods</i> in either theme or plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:46:16-07:00","id":961978,"title":"","content":"Hard to say. Beast and Changeling might be able to cover anything the other splats don't already focus on. And even then, the other splats are more of a broad spectrum than a specific depiction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:55:04-07:00","id":961981,"title":"","content":"I feel like some corebooks based on Mirrors might be interesting alternatives to new lines. I agree with Jakki that there are so many lines that need books that that's what OP should probably focus on, but for the future, releasing a Bleeding Edge of Infinite Macabre or Woundgate corebook might be really fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T17:05:18-07:00","id":961985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961945#post961945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like an Alien game is one that could be done well, but it needs to fit the CofD setting: Demon is about as close to sci-fi as I think anyone is comfortable with (some might say it's already passed that point, but I think they're wrong), and that game succeeds because it's full of occultism and other High Strangeness dressed in a technological skin. Doing an actual &quot;from another planet and smashed to earth in a space ship&quot; Alien would be a thematic mismatch that would chafe with the wider setting, but drawing on some of the stuff hinted at by Werewol'f material on the idigam as strange things foreign to reality and uncomfortable with the physical world. A game about aliens from somewhere else - some sort of inner realm, or the depths of a known realm - who <i>do not belong here</i> and want to go home but cannot for whatever reason might work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Demon's premise from &quot;literal fallen angels escaped from the pits of Hell&quot; to &quot;sentient drones created by a god-like cosmic computer that have gone off the grid and become human&quot; was a pretty big jump. But I can agree that &quot;visitors from another dimension&quot; might be a better fit in the CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T17:09:51-07:00","id":961986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961985#post961985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing Demon's premise from &quot;literal fallen angels escaped from the pits of Hell&quot; to &quot;sentient drones created by a god-like cosmic computer that have gone off the grid and become human&quot; was a pretty big jump. But I can agree that &quot;visitors from another dimension&quot; might be a better fit in the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that it's a thin coat of chrome paint over a fairly traditional Gnostic narrative, but that's neither here nor there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T17:23:22-07:00","id":961991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961986#post961986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would argue that it's a thin coat of chrome paint over a fairly traditional Gnostic narrative</div> </div> </div> </div>And you'd be right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:13:35-07:00","id":962004,"title":"","content":"In regards to incubus/succubus:<br /> <br /> Sex is too narrow for an entire splat. We have succubi and incubi in just about every line-pay attention and you see the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:31:19-07:00","id":962009,"title":"","content":"What about buyer's remorse, where the characters voluntarily step into power and come to regret their decision in doing so?<br /> Geist and Vampire vaguely touch on this, but both the Bound and the Kindred could be considered as being under duress when they make that decision. A game where the metamorphosis is completely voluntary and not a matter of self-preservation places blame immediately on the character: there is no scapegoat onto which the weight of responsibility may be deflected.<br /> That's one of the thought spaces the fansplat Dragon the Embers tried to fill (This fire can burn for eternity! Be like the fire and you'll live forever. ...You ate the Heart? Great! Oh, by the way, we're out of fuel to stoke the fire), and it appears relatively untouched by major templates (Vampires can blame their sire and the Bound can blame their Geist).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for stranded aliens, I think there's room there to emphasize the difference between ethnocentrism and cultural relativism. If you have a <i>community</i> of extraterrestrial organisms living on Earth, there is more opportunity to explore their differences with humanity (beyond biology or tech, as social structure can be explored) than with a single alien organism who crashed or escaped from a military facility. The game then becomes Dian Fossey living among the gorillas; characters are forced to live with an 'inferior' species and cleave to their cultures for survival (despite holding the opinion those practices are backward or downright savage) and come to realize there's something to be learned from that way of life and maybe it isn't so primitive after all.<br /> <br /> There was a television show &quot;The Neighbors&quot; which approached this concept from a comedy angle (Larger alien presence than &quot;Third Rock&quot;, but that same sort of culture shock model. The Zavronians referred to their life on Earth and the lack of their technology and comforts as 'camping'), and the movie &quot;District Nine&quot; looked at it from the horror perspective (Alien refugee camp devolves into a slum, with the aliens having forgotten how their tech works within a generation). It also explores the trials of immigration, particularly in the early 1900s when families would have to abandon their language and hide their traditions for fear of reprisal if they were perceived as 'foreign'.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, what One Vorlon said about Earth being the Wild West of the galaxy would be equally intriguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". Sometimes I fixate on a word and unintentionally use it repeatedly, sorry about that. 09-01-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:34:15-07:00","id":962011,"title":"","content":"@CJC I believe Deviant will touch on &quot;I did this to myself and now I can't go back.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:36:16-07:00","id":962012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962004#post962004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to incubus/succubus:<br /> <br /> Sex is too narrow for an entire splat. We have succubi and incubi in just about every line-pay attention and you see the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Femme/homme fatale (I never took French in any seriousness, I hope I got the grammar right) is more of an individual character concept, and each splat more-or-less includes an x-splat or goodies dedicated to playing that kind of character. I have no idea how you would take that idea and turn it into an entire splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:46:54-07:00","id":962017,"title":"","content":"Another idea about aliens; what if we went the Doctor Who route in that the player characters, like the Doctor and the Master, are renegades from a race of aliens who have a large or focused influence on reality. The retain some part of their smarts and power, but they go against the grain of their race's philosophy and interfere, resulting in lowered ability/power.<br /> <br /> ...no wait, that's Demon. :/ Darnit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T18:54:30-07:00","id":962019,"title":"","content":"Here's a thought... could we take the idea of Alien... and throw it into a Lovecraftian framework?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T19:15:07-07:00","id":962025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962011#post962011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@CJC I believe Deviant will touch on &quot;I did this to myself and now I can't go back.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Deviant all accidental, though? I mean, the comparison to Brundlefly seems to imply that. Yeah, your actions may lead to you shattering like a dropped mirror, but I didn't get the impression it was &quot;Drink this potion and you will be as eternal as the mountains tall&quot; only to turn you into a walking statue. It's not consent; it's effectively random isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T19:34:11-07:00","id":962029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962025#post962025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Deviant all accidental, though? I mean, the comparison to Brundlefly seems to imply that. Yeah, your actions may lead to you shattering like a dropped mirror, but I didn't get the impression it was &quot;Drink this potion and you will be as eternal as the mountains tall&quot; only to turn you into a walking statue. It's not consent; it's effectively random isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Deviant is a game about humans changing you into the monster. Sometimes that asshole human is <i>you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T21:16:01-07:00","id":962056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962017#post962017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...no wait, that's Demon. :/ Darnit.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/9chfpZK.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Associated demotivator</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962019#post962019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a thought... could we take the idea of Alien... and throw it into a Lovecraftian framework?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that hit the problem that the players are human, so you'll have to make the Aliens understandable from a human perspective and in just doing that you're defying the entire point of the lovecraftian framework?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:41:26-07:00","id":962105,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much agreeing with everything everyone else has said. <br /> <br /> Honestly? I think Onyx Path could do four more Dark Eras books without running out of ideas. I don't think there's any risk of OP running out of books to write, is what I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-02-2016, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:00:20-07:00","id":962112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962105#post962105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty much agreeing with everything everyone else has said. <br /> <br /> Honestly? I think Onyx Path could do four more Dark Eras books without running out of ideas. I don't think there's any risk of OP running out of books to write, is what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Four more Dark Eras books would be a dream come true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:10:51-07:00","id":962117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961933#post961933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever run across the <b>Witchcraft</b>/<b>Armageddon </b>RPGs? It has both angels and saints as playable splats, handled in WoD style. As they remember it, the angels were ordered to &quot;look after&quot; humanity. Tens of thousands of years later, they're still trying to follow that order. But dissension has fractured their ranks into three factions, every day humanity comes up with new ways to tempt them, and . . . its just been so long!<br /> <br /> One faction leader preaches a very fascist version of hardcore fundamentalism as a solution. Another, wiping out humanity. And the third is pro-humanity largely because its members are hooked on vices that only humanity can supply. . .<br /> <br /> Saints/prophets/etc. could be an interesting addition to the WoD. Humans touched by divinity (for better or worse), and having to deal with the &quot;profane&quot; world Might take a bit of work, but keeping it distinct from <b>Demon</b> and <b>Mage</b> should be doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... dunno. I'm less interested in &quot;mature take on Christianity&quot; and more interested in &quot;mature take on the <i>idea</i> of religion&quot;, I guess. Saints and angels and stuff aren't very interesting to me, but on the other hand, messing around with exemplars of religious ideals or the mythological metaphors make for something that perks me up a bit more.<br /> <br /> Western culture has been engaging with the Christian narrative in interesting ways for centuries upon centuries now. And while it's not like we'll ever run out of material, examining that stuff has lost its shine for me. (Demon: the Fallen was <i>super</i> interesting to me 10-15 years ago; these days it's mostly nostalgia for how cool it seemed to a younger me.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=961945#post961945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a>, <i>Red Markets</i> has been awesome so far; there are several actual play podcasts for it, and I have the backer draft of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very pleased to hear that. There's an earnestness to Stokes that makes me root for him. I probably have the backer draft somewhere, too, but I haven't gotten around to actually downloading and reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:19:16-07:00","id":962122,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I really don't think ChroD is going to go down an explicitly christian route for anything in the future. All the other concerns aside, that was such a huge, defining, polarizing feature of oWoD, and it's something they've clearly been trying to move away from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:03:44-07:00","id":962185,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that I think that the whole christian route has been kind of been done to death between Vampire (two of five covenants define themselves in relationship to God), Mage and the God-Machine. The CofD is already choking under different takes on Christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:37:20-07:00","id":962199,"title":"","content":"Other possibilities for the &quot;monster story&quot; avenue of looking at the question...<br /> <br /> We've had creatures who need humanity to feed upon, or for whom ties to humanity are a way to progress (Promethean) or resist degradation (Vampire and Deviant especially), but none where it's central to their power and nature. I had a vague idea (mostly as a Mummy hack) of a &quot;Ancestor&quot; monster psychically tied to a family/community/cult/other definable group, with the breadth and depth of ties determining the scope of their abilities. That one was mostly about community, duty and politics - but it could be approached in other ways. The Phoenix fangame presented creatures that would make good mentors, or &quot;builders&quot; of something in the human world.<br /> <br /> We haven't had a line that's explicitly about more than one type of creature (the preceding idea touched on this in that I imagined Ancestors varyingly being humans who inherited the role and will pass it on, humans who use their ties to render themselves immortal, ghosts who live &quot;in&quot; their people and possess or manifest when they are needed), or undead who &quot;live&quot; in preserved bodies becoming animate when needed). I've remarked in the past how I would like a 2nd edition of Geist to actually be about sineaters, wraiths, and revenants. Depending on how broadly we define them, djinn could do this (marid, ifrit, zar, and ghilan are certainly more diverse than the x-splats of existing lines).<br /> <br /> And we haven't had a line where the creatures are a new phenomenon; I mean really really new, like Hunter the Reckoning new - one where the player characters will be at the forefront of learning the scope of their metaphysics, inventing their powers, and defining their culture. Geist touches on the last, and Deviant probably has a little of it, but it's not been a big deal so far.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:41:28-07:00","id":962229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960806#post960806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people who use &quot;retarded&quot; to refer to things they find stupid don't do it with the intent of attacking people with developmental disabilities. Most poeple who use &quot;gay&quot; to refer to things they don't like don't do it with the intent of attacking people who are attracted to people of the same sex or gender. They're still not ok things to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I can't argue that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960793#post960793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reseru, I'm coming to you as a friend; there is literally no reason to defend your stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thank you. I hope you don't take it all the wrong way. I know the conversation has mostly died down (and thankfully didn't derail the thread or get too heated) but I did just want to come back in to say that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:57:18-07:00","id":962282,"title":"","content":"For a game like a potential Djinn line, what if ome of the aspects is the desire forfulfilling wishes clashing with the desire to be in their bottle? What if said bottle was out of their reach, or destroyed, or they are stuck in a human form/role they need to end/break free from without dying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:08:55-07:00","id":962377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962229#post962229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, I can't argue that one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, thank you. I hope you don't take it all the wrong way. I know the conversation has mostly died down (and thankfully didn't derail the thread or get too heated) but I did just want to come back in to say that</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you meant no harm. Don't sweat it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:25:56-07:00","id":962439,"title":"","content":"I'm really liking the Idea of Djinn as a playable creature/faction/what have you.<br /> <br /> Really I would like to see two types of Stories:<br /> 1. Stories where the players <i>serve</i> humanity.<br /> 2. Stories less about the monster and more about the society.<br /> <br /> I'll elaborate on what I'd like to see with these.<br /> <br /> 1.<br /> We have 10 game lines now and a lot of them have predation as a central mechanic/theme (save for a few).<br /> - Vampires: Predation for Blood.<br /> - Changelings: Predation for willpower.<br /> - Beast: Predation in and of itself.<br /> - Demon: Predation for lives.<br /> - <b>Edit: </b>Deviants: Those who are predated on.<br /> These are the biggest ones. Then there's:<br /> - Mages: Who are more about themselves then humanity.<br /> - Werewolves: More focused on the Shadow if not hunting humanity<br /> - Prometheans: Their existence harms humanity.<br /> - Mummies: They are at best indifferent towards humans<br /> <br /> <br /> Best we have are hunters and serving humans isn't so much a theme as a side effect.<br /> <br /> I want to see a whole set of stories where the focus is benefiting humanity but the personal horror of it is: how much of yourself do you lose? Especially with those that fail and actively attempt to harm. Then you have to try so much harder. It would be interesting if the mechanic was almost the opposite of the Hungers of Beasts. Where it's specific how you're helping. I don't know something like that. Doppelgangers maybe? I don't know but that isn't really an avenue that we've really explored yet.<br /> <br /> 2.<br /> What if we have a game line that is not at all united by a common origin. What if there's a game line that can have any Supernatural and has rules to easily create a new supernatural creatures but the uniting factor is the organization that they've found themselves inducted into. Like some sort of mega-cult or a secret society with many tiers. Being a member changes the fundamental being of the player's character. Their powers change to reflect something integral in the tier or circle. They have banes that reflect where they came from. It's all shadowy and secret and you naturally change in many different ways throughout the game till you're more or less what you used to be.<br /> <br /> I don't really know how we would handle that or create that. But that really isn't a kind of horror or a kind of story that we've explored yet. The closest of &quot;conglomeration&quot; that we have is Beast but it's not really a society. Then there's Hunter/Sin-eater/Mage giant organizations but those aren't really conglomerate-like. idk, it sounds like an interesting thing to explore. It's rife with a type of horror that we haven't really seen before. Almost like &quot;no matter how unique you make yourself you're still part of the fodder&quot; or something of the like. idk, just the idea of a major template that only exists to be applied over/replace other major templates.<br /> <br /> The powers could be like dread powers. idk. just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 10-28-2019, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T16:11:31-07:00","id":962549,"title":"","content":"On the serving front, what if the more powerful a Djinn is, the more literally they must follow the wish? That is, they can affect things more widely and thoroughly, but they have less wiggle room to meddle with the wish itself, either to make it less costly or less destructive, or even to simply say &quot;no&quot; to doing it. To do that triggers a breaking point, possibly sapping their self-identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-02-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:28:42-07:00","id":962586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962439#post962439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have 10 game lines now and a lot of them have predation as a central mechanic/theme (save for a few).<br /> - Vampires: Predation for Blood.<br /> - Changelings: Predation for willpower.<br /> - Beast: Predation in and of itself.<br /> - Demon: Predation for lives.<br /> These are the biggest ones. Then there's:<br /> - Mages: Who are more about themselves then humanity.<br /> - Werewolves: More focused on the Shadow if not hunting humanity<br /> - Prometheans: Their existence harms humanity.<br /> - Mummies: They are at best indifferent towards humans<br /> - Renegades: Focused on their agendas.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are Demon and Changeling more focused on predation than Werewolf, the game whose player characters are defined by being the ultimate predators, whose obligation to their nature is <i>to hunt</i>, and whose cultural roles and societal responsibilities are focused on hunting particular prey in ways they are suited to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-02-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T18:05:27-07:00","id":962608,"title":"","content":"Because they're talking about which splats feed off of humanity, not just who's the best predator.<br /> <br /> Yes, werewolves can eat human flesh for Essence but it's a breaking point, they can feed off spirits anyway, and their social splats are defined by what <i>Shadow</i> beings they prey on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T18:20:52-07:00","id":962615,"title":"","content":"The Iron Masters have humanity as their sacred prey, even if they often hunt human organizations over individual humans. But more to the point, I find it a fairly notable oversight to pass over Werewolves from the top of a listing of predation in splats. Many of<i> their prey</i> pose a danger to humanity as much as to the balance of worlds, and are heavily connected with human actions in the physical world.<br /> <br /> I confused myself a bit at the context though, I'll admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-02-2016, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:21:02-07:00","id":962662,"title":"","content":"Also, changeling's aren't really predatory unless they are reaping rather than harvesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:47:14-07:00","id":962672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962662#post962662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, changeling's aren't really predatory unless they are reaping rather than harvesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>#dontbesosure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:30:57-07:00","id":962685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962672#post962672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#dontbesosure</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess things have changed rather largely from the previews then. Which is disappointing since I prefer changelings not Having to be psychic vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-03-2016, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:43:57-07:00","id":962690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962685#post962685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess things have changed rather largely from the previews then. Which is disappointing since I prefer changelings not Having to be psychic vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Predatory_lending\" target=\"_blank\">They haven't</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:46:02-07:00","id":962693,"title":"","content":"Predatory is a broad concept. Changelings are not safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:03:14-07:00","id":962715,"title":"","content":"Djinn was an interesting concept, but the backstory was very explicitly based on religious themes, and that probably wouldn't work out for the reasons people have mentioned. It assumes that The Big G and his angels are major cosmic forces, and I can't really see ChroD canonizing (ha ha) that.<br /> <br /> And then there's the overlap problem, since Djinn-related themes have cropped up quite a lot in other lines. Changeling pretty much has it handled, IMO, but then again Changeling can handle almost any kind of monster story you can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-03-2016, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:29:25-07:00","id":962722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962715#post962715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Djinn was an interesting concept, but the backstory was very explicitly based on religious themes, and that probably wouldn't work out for the reasons people have mentioned. It assumes that The Big G and his angels are major cosmic forces, and I can't really see ChroD canonizing (ha ha) that.<br /> <br /> And then there's the overlap problem, since Djinn-related themes have cropped up quite a lot in other lines. Changeling pretty much has it handled, IMO, but then again Changeling can handle almost any kind of monster story you can think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the fangame, or the legends of the djinn themselves? If from the Djinn, it can be reworked to fit the universe much like most of the gamelines are (such as Demon). If it's the fangame, well, that's just one concept that could be applied, but for legal reasons likely won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:31:29-07:00","id":962724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962722#post962722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean the fangame, or the legends of the djinn themselves? If from the Djinn, it can be reworked to fit the universe much like most of the gamelines are (such as Demon). If it's the fangame, well, that's just one concept that could be applied, but for legal reasons likely won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I meant the fangame. If anyone who worked on it is reading this, I'd actually urge them to read up on some cWoD stuff, because it could be a really good fit there and you could potentially come up with something very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:33:49-07:00","id":962726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962724#post962724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I meant the fangame. If anyone who worked on it is reading this, I'd actually urge them to read up on some cWoD stuff, because it could be a really good fit there and you could potentially come up with something very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I was pondering on making my own fansplat for them :-p I'm actually not sure where the already existing Dinn fangame-stuff is at though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:36:58-07:00","id":962727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962726#post962726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And here I was pondering on making my own fansplat for them :-p I'm actually not sure where the already existing Dinn fangame-stuff is at though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got a wiki link from googling Djinn: The Binding, not sure if there's more somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T00:00:48-07:00","id":962732,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes, I remember reading a bit about that. Interesting ideas, but the morality stat is a bit too close to a mortal's for my liking, and the godly/angelic influence seems a triffle odd considering the origins of classic Djinn...as far as I know. I could be dramatically wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T02:22:22-07:00","id":962743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962615#post962615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Iron Masters have humanity as their sacred prey, even if they often hunt human organizations over individual humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah you're right. That's an oversight on my part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:49:54-07:00","id":964584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=962615#post962615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Iron Masters have humanity as their sacred prey, even if they often hunt human organizations over individual humans. But more to the point, I find it a fairly notable oversight to pass over Werewolves from the top of a listing of predation in splats. Many of<i> their prey</i> pose a danger to humanity as much as to the balance of worlds, and are heavily connected with human actions in the physical world.<br /> <br /> I confused myself a bit at the context though, I'll admit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah sorry if the list is a little wonky or off. I've not played Werewolf in it's entirety (or rather outside of a cross-over) so I didn't think about that. <br /> <br /> My point in the list still stands though. There really hasn't been a set of stories where &quot;Serving&quot; humanity was a major theme. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how it would work but there is definite Horror in the loss of self along with the raising of... service? idk, I liken it to Legend from Psion but twisted into a personal horror style. In Psion, the characters get stronger and humanities expectations start mattering more and more until, for the most part, Humanity starts to seem to have more control over the destinies than the character. <br /> <br /> I mean that's not exact (i've not technically played it either) but I look at that and see a game of personal horror inside that... Somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:57:38-07:00","id":964594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=964584#post964584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how it would work but there is definite Horror in the loss of self along with the raising of... service?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's called Mummy. So it'd need to be some other form of horror to be the focus to not just be a rehash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:28:29-07:00","id":964612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=964594#post964594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's called Mummy. So it'd need to be some other form of horror to be the focus to not just be a rehash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I've not played that either. I guess I mean beneficial help. Correct me if I'm wrong but Mummies do not seem to be beneficial to humanity. They seem more bound to service than what I'm looking for. I'm thinking of something closer to selfless figures of history and I'm thinking about the horror of what it would be doing to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:03:38-07:00","id":964638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=964612#post964612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I've not played that either. I guess I mean beneficial help. Correct me if I'm wrong but Mummies do not seem to be beneficial to humanity. They seem more bound to service than what I'm looking for. I'm thinking of something closer to selfless figures of history and I'm thinking about the horror of what it would be doing to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are bound to serve their human cults to the end of time, and the main type of horror present in the game is that the characters are constantly losing their identity and sense of self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:19:20-07:00","id":964649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=964638#post964638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are bound to serve their human cults to the end of time, and the main type of horror present in the game is that the characters are constantly losing their identity and sense of self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, you're right. Perhaps I should Play Mummy then ^.^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:34:02-07:00","id":964661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=964584#post964584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how it would work but there is definite Horror in the loss of self along with the raising of... service?</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's a perfect description of <b>Mummy</b>, I'd argue it's not so much about service to cults as it is to otherwordly powers. Cults have a huge presence and are very important, but thematically, in relevance to this topic, they're present as a juxtaposition with the otherworldly powers and a mummy's own power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T04:54:06-07:00","id":964897,"title":"","content":"And neither cults nor otherworldly powers are the same thing as service to humanity <i>as a whole</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T04:59:58-07:00","id":964901,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I gave that description to better explain my previous statement that it'd need a different sort of horror to &quot;loss of self after becoming consumed by service&quot;, since that's the primary horror of Mummy. Not that Mummy's serve all of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:04:59-07:00","id":965080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=964901#post964901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I gave that description to better explain my previous statement that it'd need a different sort of horror to &quot;loss of self after becoming consumed by service&quot;, since that's the primary horror of Mummy. Not that Mummy's serve all of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Then let's see. <br /> <br /> you know how, on the forums, each of the sub-forums have a small phrase to describe their purview? Like &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Visceral drama and personal horror</span>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of a way to describe the purview that I have in my mind:<br /> &quot;Finding the Balance of Power and Domination.&quot;<br /> &quot;The example for those to follow.&quot;<br /> &quot;A Game of Sacrifice and Just Rewards.&quot;<br /> &quot;Entangled Plots and Twisted Influence.&quot; <br /> &quot;There must always be two sides to a conflict.&quot;<br /> &quot;There's not always two sides to a conflict.&quot;<br /> &quot;Inspirational Figures or Villains most foul.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know, the more I try to think of it, the less I can see it's Story potential. There's also what kind of creature would go with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T11:07:52-07:00","id":965084,"title":"","content":"So, I was thinking about it this morning and it occurred to me:<br /> <br /> My original suggestion wasn't really about service. It was trying to do Ender's Game in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T05:01:53-07:00","id":965607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=964901#post964901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I gave that description to better explain my previous statement that it'd need a different sort of horror to &quot;loss of self after becoming consumed by service&quot;, since that's the primary horror of Mummy. Not that Mummy's serve all of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy the Resurrection includes service to humanity, and does it by concentrating on an external enemy - as well as a certain fear that &quot;service to humanity&quot; is a product of the current times, and might change.<br /> <br /> But maybe it's something like mentorship - you have the blood of the Simurgh, and to you falls the task of making sure humans (collectively and individually) become what they can and must be. But it's not like everyone who shares that blood agrees on the whats and hows of that. And it's not like you'll never doubt yourself - hopefully anyway - never doubting yourself can lead to bad places. And it's not like there isn't an external enemy in the form of the Dahaka (of which there are many rather than mytholgy's one), humans that spread poison - be it physical, spiritual, or moral - into the world around them. [This all draws on Persian mythology of course, though I'd stick to old hero myths, rather than trying to bring in figures like Ahuramazda or Ahriman]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:54:33-07:00","id":966571,"title":"","content":"Back to my topic of &quot;cool stuff OP could do for big releases instead of new lines&quot;, some really high-profile Blue Book or Minor Template stuff would be awesome. Like, imagine if we got something like 2e Second Sight as a big, lavish kickstarted release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:06:43-07:00","id":966647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=966571#post966571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to my topic of &quot;cool stuff OP could do for big releases instead of new lines&quot;, some really high-profile Blue Book or Minor Template stuff would be awesome. Like, imagine if we got something like 2e Second Sight as a big, lavish kickstarted release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give me a gigantic crossover book on Cults that's equal parts the kin of <i>Slasher</i> and a guide to having a subservient organization for every gameline (Vampire, Mage, Mummy, Demon, and Beast all explicitly have this, and Changeling and Geist can easily fit it as well - to say nothing of whether or not a Werewolf pack is just a cult with a nice name) and I'll never complain again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:38:48-07:00","id":969527,"title":"","content":"Back on the idea of big blue book stuff that OP could do as a major release instead of a new line, I'd really love a Dark Eras-level huge multi-author kickstarted book that's all about minor templates. Maybe divide it into two: one about new minor templates, 2e updates, new tools, making your own, and gameplay stuff. And have the second be devoted to fleshing out minor templates from a storytelling perspective. I'd say, have authors choose their favorite and write a section for it, with hooks and settings and themes and all of that. <br /> <br /> Also, hopefully it would have something that makes mortal sorcerers something better than &quot;shittier mages&quot;. Basically, compelling reasons why a sorcerer who had a button that would instantly turn them into a Mage wouldn't push it, and why a Mage with a button that would instantly turn them into a sorcerer would seriously consider pushing it. <br /> <br /> I think my philosophy about horror games where the players have superpowers can be distilled down to: Power Sucks. Or rather, in a horror setting, there should be a direct correlation between power and danger and an inverse correlation between power and humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:57:16-07:00","id":969537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=969527#post969527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on the idea of big blue book stuff that OP could do as a major release instead of a new line, I'd really love a Dark Eras-level huge multi-author kickstarted book that's all about minor templates. Maybe divide it into two: one about new minor templates, 2e updates, new tools, making your own, and gameplay stuff. And have the second be devoted to fleshing out minor templates from a storytelling perspective. I'd say, have authors choose their favorite and write a section for it, with hooks and settings and themes and all of that. <br /> <br /> Also, hopefully it would have something that makes mortal sorcerers something better than &amp;quot;shittier mages&amp;quot;. Basically, compelling reasons why a sorcerer who had a button that would instantly turn them into a Mage wouldn't push it, and why a Mage with a button that would instantly turn them into a sorcerer would seriously consider pushing it. <br /> <br /> I think my philosophy about horror games where the players have superpowers can be distilled down to: Power Sucks. Or rather, in a horror setting, there should be a direct correlation between power and danger and an inverse correlation between power and humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of why I'm hoping sekhem sorcerers continue Mummy's theme of &quot;power is a chain you wrap around yourself.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:31:55-07:00","id":969698,"title":"","content":"Alan Moore's Swamp Thing and the post-Morrison Animal Man come to mind: creatures that represent raw, primal aspects of life without necessarily being an environmentalist screed. I picture something that's thematically a sort of inversion of Prometheus while reversing the Touchstone model from Requiem. You start out as human, but you're a vessel for some higher form: maybe it's vegetative or animal life or the endless depths of the ocean. You have the potential to become something alien and elemental, something that can better protect the people you love and the world they live in, but each stage in your ascension means shedding the things you love and becoming something more surreal. I could see sprites, dryads, nymphs, and djinn being the sort of template basis, and like Prometheus, it would be set with a definitive goal in mind, a hopeful if bittersweet end as your characters slowly gives up their identitie to become something greater than themselves.<br /> <br /> I too would like to see an actual spiritual successor to Wraith come into being. I think it could coexist well with Geist without the two games stepping on one another's toes.<br /> <br /> I also think some variation of a zombie or revenant game is doable, though I think it comes down to making something that doesn't seem too derivative of Requiem. Perhaps, like Beast, you focus more on crossover? Your body is dying, and while you start by feeding on animals and corpses, that's eventually not enough to sustain you. Human bodies will last you a bit, but other supernaturals is where the money's at. Something about your transformation makes it so that eating the flesh of something more than human transfers a level of their power to you. Maybe? I don't know... I'm not sure a game where all the characters are cannibals would be all that... palatable.<br /> <br /> Maybe a twist on Lovecraftian mythology? You play a cultist but, contrary to the typical spin where cultists are trying to raise Old Gods from the Depths to feast on All Existence, you're there to preserve our being. Keeping this terribly, otherworldly thing asleep and placid is your responsibility, and sometimes that means doing horrible, horrible things. You're tethered to this extradimensional creature, and being so tethered gives you access to a portion of its powers, but you're forced to further its agendas, its power plays against other slumbering gods, because doing so ensures that it doesn't awaken in a rage, ready to devour everything you know. Your powers grow stronger the closer it comes to wakefulness. So you want your powers to be weak. You want to be able to accomplish the agendas set out for you using practical and mundane tools, because your powers growing is a terrifying sign that you aren't doing good enough, that the apocalypse is nigh. I'd imagine each player would play a different member of the cult, and they'd work together to build their god at the beginning of the game, with each PC getting some distinct portion of their god's powers. The cult would have a shared experience pool sort of similar to practical experience in Hunter, but rather than being used to buy tactics and new traits for cell members, it would be used to expand the cult via a sort of merit system: getting politicians and policemen in the cult's pocket, expanding their base of operations, creating sleeper cells in other cities, possibly with a late game that's more strategic and focused on inter-cult espionage and politics (not dissimilar from what was introduced in Damnation City). Meanwhile, you know that a lot of these cultists are in the same predicament you are, trying to stave off the awakening of something equally as monstrous as your patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-15-2016, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:48:24-07:00","id":969704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=969698#post969698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a twist on Lovecraftian mythology? You play a cultist but, contrary to the typical spin where cultists are trying to raise Old Gods from the Depths to feast on All Existence, you're there to preserve our being. Keeping this terribly, otherworldly thing asleep and placid is your responsibility, and sometimes that means doing horrible, horrible things. You're tethered to this extradimensional creature, and being so tethered gives you access to a portion of its powers, but you're forced to further its agendas, its power plays against other slumbering gods, because doing so ensures that it doesn't awaken in a rage, ready to devour everything you know. Your powers grow stronger the closer it comes to wakefulness. So you want your powers to be weak. You want to be able to accomplish the agendas set out for you using practical and mundane tools, because your powers growing is a terrifying sign that you aren't doing good enough, that the apocalypse is nigh. I'd imagine each player would play a different member of the cult, and they'd work together to build their god at the beginning of the game, with each PC getting some distinct portion of their god's powers. The cult would have a shared experience pool sort of similar to practical experience in Hunter, but rather than being used to buy tactics and new traits for cell members, it would be used to expand the cult via a sort of merit system: getting politicians and policemen in the cult's pocket, expanding their base of operations, creating sleeper cells in other cities, possibly with a late game that's more strategic and focused on inter-cult espionage and politics (not dissimilar from what was introduced in Damnation City). Meanwhile, you know that a lot of these cultists are in the same predicament you are, trying to stave off the awakening of something equally as monstrous as your patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is essentially Mummy, though that focuses more on &quot;I am enslaved by the thing that grants me powers&quot; more than &quot;I serve something horrible&quot; - though the Judges are alien and terrifying. It even has the Cult merit you want!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:58:15-07:00","id":969706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=969704#post969704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is essentially Mummy, though that focuses more on &quot;I am enslaved by the thing that grants me powers&quot; more than &quot;I serve something horrible&quot; - though the Judges are alien and terrifying. It even has the Cult merit you want!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd considered whether it was too close to Mummy (which is a fantastic game I haven't completely wrapped my head around yet), but I think there's enough leverage there to distinguish the two ideas as separate cores.You aren't a slave to something higher than yourself. You could choose to turn your back on it and live out your life, but you continue to enforce its will because the consequences of not keeping this thing sleepy and sated is unfathomable. I suppose it would be a game about voluntarily doing evil, knowing that it's the only way to prevent or at least stall something far worse.<br /> <br /> Also, as I recall, Mummy has you starting off as a nearly omnipotent god and gradually losing your powers after each slumber, right?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a game where your power trait is essentially a doomsday clock, and you have to scramble to stall it from climbing higher or ideally reverse the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:06:39-07:00","id":969715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=969706#post969706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd considered whether it was too close to Mummy (which is a fantastic game I haven't completely wrapped my head around yet), but I think there's enough leverage there to distinguish the two ideas as separate cores.You aren't a slave to something higher than yourself. You could choose to turn your back on it and live out your life, but you continue to enforce its will because the consequences of not keeping this thing sleepy and sated is unfathomable. I suppose it would be a game about voluntarily doing evil, knowing that it's the only way to prevent or at least stall something far worse.<br /> <br /> Also, as I recall, Mummy has you starting off as a nearly omnipotent god and gradually losing your powers after each slumber, right?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a game where your power trait is essentially a doomsday clock, and you have to scramble to stall it from climbing higher or ideally reverse the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's the kind of clever idea we can work with! A Power Stat that starts low and then you frantically try to stop it rising on its own is super neat mechanical territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:24:39-07:00","id":969724,"title":"","content":"I think Deviant is going to be kind of like that, in that gaining power is super risky and something a character could conceivably be trying to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:51:41-07:00","id":970000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=969724#post969724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Deviant is going to be kind of like that, in that gaining power is super risky and something a character could conceivably be trying to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. It sounds like they're doing the body horror thing where you just get progressively worse and worse until you self-destruct. I think it's a great idea that really plays to a sense of Cronenberg horror.<br /> <br /> I think where this game would differentiate itself is in the group aspect. Every game is about a team of people working together, but so often, players are put at odds. Mummy is about cults, but it's about the horrible god-monster that everyone else worships.<br /> <br /> Thrall: The Supplication (or whatever it would hypothetically be called), would foster a sense of community from the start, in terms of both character and mechanics. You're all members of the same cult. The players work together to create their patron monster, and they have to cooperate to decide on the form that their cult takes through collaborative XP spending. Your power stat is linked, so that doomsday clock is scaled to everyone in the party, but there'd be differentiation in how the individual respond to this sort of growth. I think Integrity (or whatever the equivalent trait is) would relate closely to your power rating. The closer your god comes to awakening, the more at danger you are of suffering derangement and becoming a creature for this thing you're keeping in check. What do you do when your brother or sister in the cult becomes a dangerous liability because exposure to this Old God has made them crack? And how far are you willing to push your cult for the greater cause? You have a noble ambition, as a custodian of a sleeping monster baby, but keeping it placid requires ruthless decisions. How far will you go with brainwashing, blackmail, and indoctrination to keep your people loyal to the cause? How much will you upset the delicate balance of society for the sake of keeping that society afloat? Will you turn a blind eye while one of your cultists goes on a ritualistic murder spree to feed your master's sick desires? Will you encourage it? Will you use your ties in the PD and the media to cover it up? Or will your natural, moralistic instincts force you to clamp down hard, knowing that doing so will make this Old God stir in its slumber, and potentially upend your delicate grasp on sanity?<br /> <br /> I think the crux of the game would be about the horror of cults, these groups where zealotry and the righteousness of the cause is used as pretext to convince members to do monstrous things. The twist is that you're right. Your sins do keep the world alive. But how far are you willing to go, and what are you willing to lose in the process","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:30:51-07:00","id":970020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=966647#post966647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give me a gigantic crossover book on Cults that's equal parts the kin of <i>Slasher</i> and a guide to having a subservient organization for every gameline (Vampire, Mage, Mummy, Demon, and Beast all explicitly have this, and Changeling and Geist can easily fit it as well - to say nothing of whether or not a Werewolf pack is just a cult with a nice name) and I'll never complain again.</div> </div> </div> </div> At least one group of Changelings, the Ivory Court, has a Cult devoted to it called the Cult of Mithra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:54:03-07:00","id":970123,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see an entire gameline focused around the idea of a Hive Mind (or many instances of hive minds.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:22:24-07:00","id":970367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=970123#post970123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see an entire gameline focused around the idea of a Hive Mind (or many instances of hive minds.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Head over to Monarch: the Endless? Basic monster-concept there is the Alien Master/Mistress of a Hive-Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:51:55-07:00","id":975687,"title":"","content":"Watching Penny Dreadful, it occurs to me that in 2e at least, there isn't really anything that exactly matches Dorian Gray (I'm not sure if 1e immortals did or not). The portrait of Dorian Gray is, and perhaps my words aren't quite correct, about corrupting innocence if there aren't consequence. I Suppose in some ways it's similar to Vampire, and yet vampire has other stronger themes. Vampire isn't necessarily about giving into the excess of human experience (it can be).<br /> <br /> So I might propose something that focuses on immortals that are bound to an item (Like the Portrait) that is a representation of them, that absorbs their sins. They should be as rare as Prometheans, in fact I could see some tie ins, what if it's the divine fire that creates them as well.<br /> <br /> Being this kind of immortal, that is still human, but bound to this object, and being this rare, they could make another good crossover splat.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's too close to the existing lines, just an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T03:02:50-07:00","id":976439,"title":"","content":"Yes, first edition covered Dorian Grey- The eternals in Immortals.<br /> <br /> However, since any damage that happens to the object happens to them, they tend to prefer stone, metal, or at least hard woods.<br /> <br /> You could probably do something similar with the abmortals of Geist too, but it would take an even darker turn than normal as an abmortal- Perhaps their portrait keeps them young as long as they feed it by causing others to lose integrity in their presence or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:35:02-07:00","id":977246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=960121#post960121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the question that should be asked is not, &quot;what monsters are left,&quot; but rather, &quot;what kind of monster stories are left?&quot;<br /> <br /> As noted, pretty much any monster can be made in at least one of the games at this point, even if that isn't the focus of the game. The Gill-man is a bit flat for a game. He's a cryptid at best, with simple bestial motivations. So if there's going to be a Creature from the Black Lagoon inspired game, one of the key things to ask is, &quot;what's the focus of this game, and what kind of stories does it tell?&quot; and see if those answers are really different from what's already there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, considering the humanist nature of CoD games, I'm of the opinion that games focusing on a particular kind of story themed around a social something that gives us pause leaves plenty of space for more gamelines. To date there are no games that take on themes like cultural assimilation/appropriation (something I tried to focus on in my Alien: the Stranded fangame), what it means to grow old and irrelevant (which sounds like a great theme for a game about Deities), chronic illness (Zombies), or the sense of alienation that soldiers have when they return from war. Sure, we could argue many games like Vampire, Promethean, and Beast, do touch upon some or all of these issues but none of them are deeply focused on it. So really, I think the question is less of what gribbly hasn't been done yet and more of what humanistic, naturalistic, psychological, or sociological issue haven't we focused on yet? By my count we can easily get up to 15 gamelines going and that's just looking at issues from the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:08:04-07:00","id":977332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977246#post977246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, considering the humanist nature of CoD games, I'm of the opinion that games focusing on a particular kind of story themed around a social something that gives us pause leaves plenty of space for more gamelines. To date there are no games that take on themes like cultural assimilation/appropriation (something I tried to focus on in my Alien: the Stranded fangame), what it means to grow old and irrelevant (which sounds like a great theme for a game about Deities), chronic illness (Zombies), or the sense of alienation that soldiers have when they return from war. Sure, we could argue many games like Vampire, Promethean, and Beast, do touch upon some or all of these issues but none of them are deeply focused on it. So really, I think the question is less of what gribbly hasn't been done yet and more of what humanistic, naturalistic, psychological, or sociological issue haven't we focused on yet? By my count we can easily get up to 15 gamelines going and that's just looking at issues from the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I rather like your ideas, but I think the last one (alienated soldiers) does fall squarely into the province of Changeling, which is very much about coping with trauma and alienation of that very sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:47:14-07:00","id":977365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977246#post977246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, considering the humanist nature of CoD games, I'm of the opinion that games focusing on a particular kind of story themed around a social something that gives us pause leaves plenty of space for more gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point wasn't inherently arguing for or against there being more gamelines.<br /> <br /> It was to argue that the focus of &quot;what should be a new gameline,&quot; needs to be around what kind of story the game tells, not what kind of creature hasn't been used yet (or at least hasn't been used for standard PC types since everything has been used so far)..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To date there are no games that take on themes like cultural assimilation/appropriation (something I tried to focus on in my Alien: the Stranded fangame), what it means to grow old and irrelevant (which sounds like a great theme for a game about Deities), chronic illness (Zombies), or the sense of alienation that soldiers have when they return from war. Sure, we could argue many games like Vampire, Promethean, and Beast, do touch upon some or all of these issues but none of them are deeply focused on it. </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think there's a lot of focus on these already, and certainly enough that making a whole new gameline can become forced:<br /> <br /> Cultural assimilation is a major aspect of Promethean, Changeling (there's a reason why &quot;kidnapped by aliens&quot; is considered a valid Durance), Mummy, and assumed to be for Deviant (who seem like they're going to cover more of the &quot;alien stranded on Earth&quot; side of it even if they're not aliens). These are all games were being an &quot;outsider&quot; - either by birth or by supernatural influence - and trying to come to terms with modern life and how (if at all) to assimilate into a new culture are core parts of the play experience. Assimilation as a negative external factor is present in a lot of the antagonists of the games, but probably most strongly in the Seers of the Throne with Mage who's whole MO is to assimilate to the wishes of the Exarchs and be content with the culture they promote.<br /> <br /> Cultural appropriation is literally a source of magical power in Mage as well, making it fodder for both sides of the main struggle of the game. It's not as core as assimilation is to the other games above, but one of the five major PC Orders treats it as their special magical skill, and none of the Orders think poorly of using Sleeper cultural practices to their own ends with minimal to no respect for those cultures, with a second PC Order that has using appropriation to control Sleeper occult societies to direct mages to proper instruction and keep everyone else &quot;safe.&quot; The Free Council, Guardians of the Veil, and the Seers all deal with this in spades. Demon also gets in significantly on appropriation issues considering you have to literally appropriate human lives to create Covers to hide yourself.<br /> <br /> Growing old and irrelevant aren't something I think are a valid single theme. They're two related themes (being old doesn't stop you from being relevant, but it does make it more difficult, and it's easy to be irrelevant and young). Vampire is very strongly focused on the themes of the detachment that comes with age. The whole 2e Humanity/Touchstone system is built specifically around the narrative conflict of remaining emotionally attached to fragile mortal things that die as you continue on in your immortality; living too long is a direct source of detachment rolls in the game. Mummy and Demon are the two games with relevancy being core themes. Mummy does &quot;old and irrelevant&quot; as a core thematic issue, because that's essentially what they are. Ancient immortal beings who are bound to the whims of masters that died out so long ago no humans know about them. They awaken with huge gaps of time lost as cultures move on during their sleep, leaving them detached from all this new &quot;young&quot; stuff, and the are forced to do seemingly pointless tasks for the Judges while using the time before going back to sleep to try to make themselves relevant again through their cults. Demons are more just about relevancy, because they are entities born of a singular purpose that they abandoned. The whole task of trying to find a purpose and create your Hell is about defining what makes you relevant again. In some ways this is also a core theme of Geist, but only in the rejection of being concerned with such things.<br /> <br /> Chronic illness isn't a theme or a story. It's a myriad of conditions people have. And zombies are not a metaphor for any of them.<br /> <br /> Alienation due to traumatic experience is a huge part of Werewolf, and Changeling (Promethean and Deviant, again assuming from spoiled stuff about it, are about different sorts of alienation). Werewolves hunt and kill things that threaten both sides of the Gauntlet for their territory, only to return home to people that don't understand them, or their mental struggles as they don't get a real off switch from hunter mode. Even the wolf-blooded and humans of their Pack never really understand what its like. Changelings have assimilation as a major theme precises because they left home, and came back to find themselves completely alienated from their old lives. The vast majority can't just slip back in from where they left off, and even then it will never be like it was as the demands of being one of the Lost constantly draw them away from family and friends; who aren't going to be able to break through and connect to the changeling's twisted experiences with the Gentry.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I don't agree we can dismiss the existing game lines as &quot;not deeply focused&quot; on any of these issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:54:03-07:00","id":977369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point wasn't inherently arguing for or against there being more gamelines.<br /> <br /> It was to argue that the focus of &quot;what should be a new gameline,&quot; needs to be around what kind of story the game tells, not what kind of creature hasn't been used yet (or at least hasn't been used for standard PC types since everything has been used so far)..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, I think there's a lot of focus on these already, and certainly enough that making a whole new gameline can become forced:<br /> <br /> Cultural assimilation is a major aspect of Promethean, Changeling (there's a reason why &quot;kidnapped by aliens&quot; is considered a 