ke it was as the demands of being one of the Lost constantly draw them away from family and friends; who aren't going to be able to break through and connect to the changeling's twisted experiences with the Gentry.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I don't agree we can dismiss the existing game lines as &quot;not deeply focused&quot; on any of these issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you could possibly argue that alienation is sort of the core theme that runs through the entirety of CoD game lines.They're all either about (either through choice or circumstances) being something that was once human but will now never really be human ever again or being something that was never human but is trying to desperately understand what that means. Hell, with the addition of Touchstones, that's become one of the core mechanics of a Requiem game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-27-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:56:36-07:00","id":977524,"title":"","content":"I agree, but I think that would fall into <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1630_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1630\" data-vbnamecard=\"1630\">Jacob</a>'s point about being in the games without being a &quot;core&quot; part of the games. A general sense of alienation is part of the core CofD atmosphere, so it seeps into all the games in various ways. I wanted to highlight the games were alienation - and that specific source of alienation - was a direct central aspect of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:31:51-07:00","id":977895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=970367#post970367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Head over to Monarch: the Endless? Basic monster-concept there is the Alien Master/Mistress of a Hive-Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took a quick gander at this and LOVE it. Is there something in there where the characters are in a hive-mind together a la Sense8?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:36:31-07:00","id":977900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Growing old and irrelevant aren't something I think are a valid single theme. They're two related themes (being old doesn't stop you from being relevant, but it does make it more difficult, and it's easy to be irrelevant and young). Vampire is very strongly focused on the themes of the detachment that comes with age. The whole 2e Humanity/Touchstone system is built specifically around the narrative conflict of remaining emotionally attached to fragile mortal things that die as you continue on in your immortality; living too long is a direct source of detachment rolls in the game. Mummy and Demon are the two games with relevancy being core themes. Mummy does &quot;old and irrelevant&quot; as a core thematic issue, because that's essentially what they are. Ancient immortal beings who are bound to the whims of masters that died out so long ago no humans know about them. They awaken with huge gaps of time lost as cultures move on during their sleep, leaving them detached from all this new &quot;young&quot; stuff, and the are forced to do seemingly pointless tasks for the Judges while using the time before going back to sleep to try to make themselves relevant again through their cults. Demons are more just about relevancy, because they are entities born of a singular purpose that they abandoned. The whole task of trying to find a purpose and create your Hell is about defining what makes you relevant again. In some ways this is also a core theme of Geist, but only in the rejection of being concerned with such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'm kinda digging the idea of Growing Old and Irrelevant as a central theme. Something that can be focused on from the fluff to the power stat. I know vampire and mummy kind of have something similar but what about something that's more in the process of becoming irrelevant. Think Psion but in reverse. That's not something we've really tried before.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:42:27-07:00","id":978040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977900#post977900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I'm kinda digging the idea of Growing Old and Irrelevant as a central theme. Something that can be focused on from the fluff to the power stat. I know vampire and mummy kind of have something similar but what about something that's more in the process of becoming irrelevant. Think Psion but in reverse. That's not something we've really tried before.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everybody: The Aging? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, I'm curious to see where you'd go with this. Vampire and Mummy really do seem to have it pretty well covered in my mind, and I know that Requiem is designed for it as well (blood potency and torpor practically ensure that any vampire that survives a while is going to end up waking up in an era where they know nothing), and touchstones are all about trying to hold onto things that once mattered but are slowly slipping out of your reach. My understanding of Mummy is that it does something similar. What do you see the core mechanics looking like, and what breed of creature would you use as the template?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-28-2016, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:49:36-07:00","id":978045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978040#post978040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Everybody: The Aging? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, I'm curious to see where you'd go with this. Vampire and Mummy really do seem to have it pretty well covered in my mind, and I know that Requiem is designed for it as well (blood potency and torpor practically ensure that any vampire that survives a while is going to end up waking up in an era where they know nothing), and touchstones are all about trying to hold onto things that once mattered but are slowly slipping out of your reach. My understanding of Mummy is that it does something similar. What do you see the core mechanics looking like, and what breed of creature would you use as the template?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lulz. To be fair, one arguable weakness of ChroD is that you only get stronger with age (I don't think mummies actually get weaker with age... the whole rest cycle thing is inverted but...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:09:23-07:00","id":978051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978045#post978045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lulz. To be fair, one arguable weakness of ChroD is that you only get stronger with age (I don't think mummies actually get weaker with age... the whole rest cycle thing is inverted but...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh! I'd heard that Mummy used an inverted power scale, but I haven't read the book myself. Good to know, but kind of a pity. I thought it was a cool idea.<br /> <br /> And I haven't read it in a while, but doesn't VtR institute a system where you weaken with age? I thought rising blood potency more or less forced you to drop into torpor (due to increased weaknesses and feeding restrictions), and the longer you're asleep, the more your power chips away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:50:48-07:00","id":978118,"title":"","content":"Mummies get weaker with time, but stronger with age. To explain that a bit, the basics are that they start with their power stat at 10 when they wake up, and it only goes down until they go to sleep (though they can control how fast it happens). However they also get XP to spend as usual on traits, so the more time they spend awake, the more tricks they can learn.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't weaken with age exactly. Like most of the CofD games, the drawbacks of being a supernatural critter are scaled to things that are impacted by age, but isn't necessarily &quot;weaker.&quot; Vampires that grow in Blood Potency and lose Humanity grow weaker to banes and such, but there's plenty of perks that go along with high BP. Vampires can go into torpor to reduce their BP, since many find the drawbacks inconvenient, and vampires automatically gain BP with time to they are forced into that choice where many other supernaturals don't have to increase their power stats unless they want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T20:10:16-07:00","id":978160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977895#post977895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took a quick gander at this and LOVE it. Is there something in there where the characters are in a hive-mind together a la Sense8?</div> </div> </div> </div> Deviant lists sense8 as on of the inspirations, so there's a good chance that it will be able to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:41:25-07:00","id":978328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was to argue that the focus of &quot;what should be a new gameline,&quot; needs to be around what kind of story the game tells, not what kind of creature hasn't been used yet (or at least hasn't been used for standard PC types since everything has been used so far).</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, there are a few cases where they go together. Which I don't mean as a nitpick so much as the cases where that happens are the most golden spots. Eg, one reason why I was pleased to see Demon the Descent (and rejected prior arguments about vampires or possessed being just as a good) was the storytelling potential in a being that's never been, isn't now, and never will be, human. One reason I want a djinn or a naga (especially, but not exclusively) game is that I think a critter rooted in non-Western legend/pop-culture, but treated in the game as a global phenomenon, is <i>in itself</i> a worthwhile addition (not enough for a line by itself, obviously, but a worthwhile ingredient for one). Again, I just mean that as an observation, not a disagreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:10:56-07:00","id":978463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978328#post978328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this is true, there are a few cases where they go together. Which I don't mean as a nitpick so much as the cases where that happens are the most golden spots. Eg, one reason why I was pleased to see Demon the Descent (and rejected prior arguments about vampires or possessed being just as a good) was the storytelling potential in a being that's never been, isn't now, and never will be, human. One reason I want a djinn or a naga (especially, but not exclusively) game is that I think a critter rooted in non-Western legend/pop-culture, but treated in the game as a global phenomenon, is <i>in itself</i> a worthwhile addition (not enough for a line by itself, obviously, but a worthwhile ingredient for one). Again, I just mean that as an observation, not a disagreement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We'd need more non Western writers for that. The main reason we don't have as much Eastern/non-European centric rooted splats is due to limited exposure for many of these creatures in popculture combined with the fact that by default most of us are in/very close to the Anglo-world by default... which tends to be a big bias on monster sources. We see minor splats and creatures from other cultures, but we'd need more things first.<br /> <br /> I will support Djinn over Naga though. I am really against snakes. And Robin Williams's Genie would make for a intersting shoutout character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:21:10-07:00","id":978472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978463#post978463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We'd need more non Western writers for that. The main reason we don't have as much Eastern/non-European centric rooted splats is due to limited exposure for many of these creatures in popculture combined with the fact that by default most of us are in/very close to the Anglo-world by default... which tends to be a big bias on monster sources. We see minor splats and creatures from other cultures, but we'd need more things first.<br /> <br /> I will support Djinn over Naga though. I am really against snakes. And Robin Williams's Genie would make for a intersting shoutout character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see djinn being a splat in a system that deals with things like nymphs, nature spirits, and animist creatures: beings that were once humans but have become something far more and are now bound to a place, thing, person, or element. You could pull from contemporary works like Swamp Thing and maybe some of the weirder Japanese and Korean ghost stories too. You've been touched by something greater than yourself, and you have the power to help the people and ideals that you love with your powers more than you could as a mere mortal, but every act of altruism makes you more alien and less able to connect with the things you once cared for. Maybe you were cursed or blessed by a god or touched by a being beyond the veil. But now you're something more. You could find antagonists in those of your kin who have become so alien that they've forgotten their base selves entirely, or poor unfortunate creatures who have become bound to would-be sorcerers who have subverted these creatures to their will. As you move closer to your pure form, your virtues and vices become more rigid obligations and compulsions, making it harder for you to connect to the world around you and making it easier for clever and dubious mortals to manipulate you to serve their ends. I suppose obsession would be the core theme?<br /> <br /> I think that would create a unified setting with a broad sense of globalism that can pull in Native American, Middle Eastern, Greco-Roman, and SE Asian sensibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-29-2016, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:32:00-07:00","id":978477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978472#post978472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see djinn being a splat in a system that deals with things like nymphs, nature spirits, and animist creatures: beings that were once humans but have become something far more and are now bound to a place, thing, person, or element. You could pull from contemporary works like Swamp Thing too. You've been touched by something greater than yourself, and you have the power to help the people and ideals that you love with your powers more than you could as a mere mortal, but every act of altruism makes you more alien and less able to connect with the things you once cared for. Maybe you were cursed or blessed by a god or touched by a being beyond the veil. But now you're something more. You could find antagonists in those of your kin who have become so alien that they've forgotten their base selves entirely, or poor unfortunate creatures who have become bound to would-be sorcerers who have subverted these creatures to their will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not bad, though I'd make them &quot;vibes&quot; rather than former humans* - starting off as a more robust version of what Werewolf would call an area's resonance - but more and more consistent reinforcement by humans gives them a kind of identity. Deliberately interacting with humans reinforces them as distinct things, and helps them stay whole (rather than fuelling them, it might heal them) - which is why so many of them do favours for people (which is what &quot;granting wishes&quot; originally referred to) - but might be why others become terrors.<br /> <br /> * A similar sort of origin to the Beasts of Bethlehem in Antagonists. But intelligent, and not necessarily monstrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T10:55:14-07:00","id":978484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978477#post978477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not bad, though I'd make them &quot;vibes&quot; rather than former humans* - starting off as a more robust version of what Werewolf would call an area's resonance - but more and more consistent reinforcement by humans gives them a kind of identity. Deliberately interacting with humans reinforces them as distinct things, and helps them stay whole (rather than fuelling them, it might heal them) - which is why so many of them do favours for people (which is what &quot;granting wishes&quot; originally referred to) - but might be why others become terrors.<br /> <br /> * A similar sort of origin to the Beasts of Bethlehem in Antagonists. But intelligent, and not necessarily monstrous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, I was going to go a different direction. They start off as humans with &quot;patrons&quot; that represent the sort of mercurial and fickle obsessions of the traditional Greek gods or utterly alien beings representing incomprehensible concepts.<br /> <br /> The young woman born and raised in Bakersville, a quiet and sleepy town that saw drastic change as she started to grow up. She was the first to stand up when the factories moved in and started polluting the nearby river. She was one of the first to start protesting, and eventually the obsession cost her her comfortable job at the bank. She led local political action against the transgressions of the big businesses nearby. In her dreams, the River would speak to her, offering her the power she needed to push those negative influences out of the town. What started as peaceful protests and lobbying expanded to acts of industrial espionage and murder. And like all rivers, the one that wound through the city was just a tributary in a greater form. As her obsession spins out of control, she's becoming more than just the crusader of this river's health. She's becoming the water itself.<br /> <br /> A middle aged man who's once happy marriage fell into stasis. His midlife crisis found him increasingly disconnected from his wife and kids. The final straw was his purchase of a cherry red vintage Mustang. It cost him everything. His wife left him, his kids became distant, and he lost everything in the settlement, including his prized car. The Mustang has hopped from owner to owner, every one speaking of how it seemed haunted. He would dream of his car, not of owning it but of being it, free and liberated on the open road, but eventually the dreams weren't enough. He stalks the car conventions throughout the Eastern seaboard. They talk to him, and he can commune through them. He's found himself as a nomad, traveling from convention to convention, shacked up in cheap roach motels, injecting motor fluid into his veins.<br /> <br /> The earnest and driven Tokyo detective who's husband and children were murdered in a horrific gangland attack. She tracked down the killers and delivered swift justice, but she quickly discovered it wasn't enough. Locals started whispering about the spirit that haunts the underworld. She demands blood, and the spirit of vengeance that purrs in her ear insists more and more that blood is the only valid currency for any ethical transgression.<br /> <br /> The graffiti artist who found his muse in a modern Aphrodite. Her patronage transformed his pedestrian scrawls into works of transgressive beauty. She enlivened him. In her presence, he felt human, felt greater than human. But then her fickle interests waned and he was left nothing more than a shell. Now the only time he can feel alive is when he is in the presence of mosaics and tags. He can crawl through the inner workings of the city, feel the pulse of life that permeates everything. Unfortunate then that the new mayor has implemented an aggressive stance towards beautifying the city and whitewashing street art.<br /> <br /> Virtue/Vice would become a core element of the characters and eventually a trap that makes them vulnerable to the agendas of others. Obsessions would replace ambitions and would be the crux of power levels, becoming increasingly grandiose and dangerous as the characters grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-29-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:18:38-07:00","id":978623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978040#post978040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Everybody: The Aging? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been larping and I didn't even realize!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978040#post978040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all seriousness though, I'm curious to see where you'd go with this. Vampire and Mummy really do seem to have it pretty well covered in my mind ...<br /> What do you see the core mechanics looking like, and what breed of creature would you use as the template?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first things you learn is everything is cyclical. It was your first mistake.<br /> <br /> You were no one. You had no contacts, no resources, and you had nothing... or so you thought. Day in-day out your life repeats the same social interactions, the same menial tasks, and the same complaints. Everything is Cyclical. But then you are in the right place at the right time, you decide to skip work today to hunt for that ridiculous legend of a hermit in the swamp, or you're simply found by some fancy suit driving a fancy car. You're given a wish, a demand, or a chance to change things for you. You take it, this is what you've wanted but you didn't know the price. <br /> <br /> Now you <i>are</i> someone. You <i>have</i> contacts, more resources than you can <i>count</i>, and you have <u><i>everything</i></u>... or so you think. By making the choice you've bound yourself. Not to any one thing or one person in particular. In fact it's to everything all at once. You find that you have all that you need and much much more but this has a cost on your soul, if what you have can be called such. The Universe gives you what ever is your desire but the more you use it and the more your desire increases the more the more detached you become. The less <i>real</i> you become. And there are things hunting you, things that desire what you have: the infinity essence that threatens to swallow your being into oblivion. It is coveted greatly and only the powerful succeed in combating these (would-be) thieves. But the stronger you become the more your threads of reality start to unravel themselves. You are losing yourself to irrelevance and reality loses<i> you</i> amongst infinity.<br /> <br /> The only way to gain equilibrium is to drain infinity. And draining that which is infinite is deceptively simple. It just takes a simple wish, a single demand, or a thorned chance to change things, for them... Everything is Cyclical.<br /> <br /> <br /> ____________________________________________<br /> <br /> My idea is what if the entire game is about how you've already gained relevance in one way or form. But the more you grow the more your hold on reality thins. Your entire essence is infinity and the natural end of that to cease to exist and yet exist in infinity. I think it terrifying to see yourself build up but then watch actively as your everything, resources, social merits, and relevance in common human society just drain right before your eyes during play. It's all a choice. <br /> <br /> Like changelings they can drain their powerstat to re-anchor themselves and to do that you need to give that to someone else. It is always safe to give it to those of your kind but it increases their powerstat (or does something with it). Giving it to random humans is less common due to the risk: it's possible that infinity will take hold in their wish and they will find themselves in your place. There are tales that given certain circumstances you may exchange places with a human. But attempts in recent knowledge have all failed (most of the time in disaster). Most of these wishes are temporary and help you to stave off critical increases in your powerstat. It's a battle between having what you want and the threat of irrelevance. <br /> <br /> The &quot;Monster&quot; template? I'm still stuck Djinn. My brain wants to play a genie really bad and the above sounds fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:29:12-07:00","id":978628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978623#post978623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been larping and I didn't even realize!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The first things you learn is everything is cyclical. It was your first mistake.<br /> <br /> You were no one. You had no contacts, no resources, and you had nothing... or so you thought. Day in-day out your life repeats the same social interactions, the same menial tasks, and the same complaints. Everything is Cyclical. But then you are in the right place at the right time, you decide to skip work today to hunt for that ridiculous legend of a hermit in the swamp, or you're simply found by some fancy suit driving a fancy car. You're given a wish, a demand, or a chance to change things for you. You take it, this is what you've wanted but you didn't know the price.<br /> <br /> Now you <i>are</i> someone. You <i>have</i> contacts, more resources than you can <i>count</i>, and you have <u><i>everything</i></u>... or so you think. By making the choice you've bound yourself. Not to any one thing or one person in particular. In fact it's to everything all at once. You find that you have all that you need and much much more but this has a cost on your soul, if what you have can be called such. The Universe gives you what ever is your desire but the more you use it and the more your desire increases the more the more detached you become. The less <i>real</i> you become. And there are things hunting you, things that desire what you have: the infinity essence that threatens to swallow your being into oblivion. It is coveted greatly and only the powerful succeed in combating these (would-be) thieves. But the stronger you become the more your threads of reality start to unravel themselves. You are losing yourself to irrelevance and reality loses<i> you</i> amongst infinity.<br /> <br /> The only way to gain equilibrium is to drain infinity. And draining that which is infinite is deceptively simple. It just takes a simple wish, a single demand, or a thorned chance to change things, for them... Everything is Cyclical.<br /> <br /> <br /> ____________________________________________<br /> <br /> My idea is what if the entire game is about how you've already gained relevance in one way or form. But the more you grow the more your hold on reality thins. Your entire essence is infinity and the natural end of that to cease to exist and yet exist in infinity. I think it terrifying to see yourself build up but then watch actively as your everything, resources, social merits, and relevance in common human society just drain right before your eyes during play. It's all a choice.<br /> <br /> Like changelings they can drain their powerstat to re-anchor themselves and to do that you need to give that to someone else. It is always safe to give it to those of your kind but it increases their powerstat (or does something with it). Giving it to random humans is less common due to the risk: it's possible that infinity will take hold in their wish and they will find themselves in your place. There are tales that given certain circumstances you may exchange places with a human. But attempts in recent knowledge have all failed (most of the time in disaster). Most of these wishes are temporary and help you to stave off critical increases in your powerstat. It's a battle between having what you want and the threat of irrelevance.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Monster&quot; template? I'm still stuck Djinn. My brain wants to play a genie really bad and the above sounds fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really, really like this. It's a cool idea, and I get the idea that the antagonists might potentially be harvesting characters? They can't create essence by themselves, but they can give a human the push to become a vessel for essence and then milk them when they've ripened?<br /> <br /> Maybe you have obligations to play up the whole Djinn theme. As in, there are periodic sacrifices you have to make in return for your power, things that seem generous at first but chip away at your own well-being for the sake of others. It could be a reversal of the whole &quot;everything comes at a price&quot; theme at the heart of wish-based stories, but that price effects both parties.<br /> <br /> So maybe every character has a Desire crux. Maybe the flavor of their essence is wealth or fame or political power, and they're required once a season to use their essence to bestow that trait upon someone in need. They quickly learn that doing so comes with a price. A charity organization that's struggling is in need of money, and their serendipity comes from a disaster that would otherwise not happen, a disaster that earns them government funding. A once-famous movie star is looking for a comeback and earns it in the form of a vicious attack from a rabid fan that pushes her right back into the spotlight. An aspiring politician who has always been overshadowed by his senator wife wants to be powerful in his own right, and he gets that opportunity when she's assassinated on stage. It's bittersweet opportunities, and they wear down on the soul of the djinn as well... Moreover, those wins are hard earned, so when things go south again for them, they'll be more inclined to take a wish granted to them by the patrons, more inclined to perpetuate the virus of djinnness(TM).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:34:43-07:00","id":978633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978628#post978628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually really, really like this. It's a cool idea, and I get the idea that the antagonists might potentially be harvesting characters? They can't create essence by themselves, but they can give a human the push to become a vessel for essence and then milk them when they've ripened?<br /> <br /> Maybe you have obligations to play up the whole Djinn theme. As in, there are periodic sacrifices you have to make in return for your power, things that seem generous at first but chip away at your own well-being for the sake of others. It could be a reversal of the whole &quot;everything comes at a price&quot; theme at the heart of wish-based stories, but that price effects both parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>couldn't you run Demon this way? or Changeling? let's make a deal...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:36:36-07:00","id":978634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978633#post978633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">couldn't you run Demon this way? or Changeling? let's make a deal...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I think you could (and I hadn't thought about it before, but it is a pretty large part of both those games), but I think with the right mechanical overlay and mythology, you could make it something unique as well.<br /> <br /> Perhaps as I said about (via edit) by making it something of a contagion. A man comes to you offering you something you always dreamed of. And through the ups and downs of your life, you keep coming back. Then you perpetuate the same cycle, nurturing that same addiction in others as the pact you've made demands. There's a bit of a pyramid scheme thing going on there, and everybody is stuck in the same position (and slowly fading away from reality in the process). Maybe making more contracts stalls the fading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-29-2016, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:37:07-07:00","id":978635,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Djinn could be interesting if you go for the idea that they are *still* servants, where as Demon's and Changelings are &quot;free&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:44:11-07:00","id":978645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978635#post978635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Djinn could be interesting if you go for the idea that they are *still* servants, where as Demon's and Changelings are &quot;free&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But then, isn't that Mummy? Do the Arisen not answer the &quot;Wishes&quot; of their Cults?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:51:55-07:00","id":978716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978628#post978628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually really, really like this. It's a cool idea, and I get the idea that the antagonists might potentially be harvesting characters? They can't create essence by themselves, but they can give a human the push to become a vessel for essence and then milk them when they've ripened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was trying to think of possible antagonists. Like what about Selfish Djinn that go allwrong and end up going ravenous time bombs (very low on the Integrity Stat). What about humans for which wishes don't go as planned and search out the Djinn for Revenge and to make it right but to do that they go after character's essence or contacts or family. What about Djinn who are exactly like you but desire to use you as a repository for their wish-giving without your consent. You gain power quickly and so does the edge of oblivion creep closer dangerously fast.<br /> <br /> My idea for the theme of losing relevance was that the higher up your power stat you go (possibly with interactions between levels of your integrity stat or something) the more your soul starts to become absorbed into infinity. They start becoming everything all at once which translates to nothing happening. The character's parents and friends forget about them. Eventually they just stop existing. In game terms they lose their social merits. <br /> <br /> Maybe you can stave off the Powerstat from climbing too high too fast by channeling infinity into a target. It's easy enough between Djinn but then it's (usually) like osmosis. It equalizes (somewhat) the power between them. But with non-Djinn, you need a desire from the subject. They have to really want the manifestation of infinity. They have to really wish for it. No contract, just straight up desire. Most Djinn choose carefully. They find someone who would want their wish bad enough. Some nefarious Djinn cause situations in which the a subject would desire something only for the Djinn to randomly show up plucking the subject from their sticky situation. <br /> <br /> But say desire does not match the wish. Say the wish is big enough that infinity might take hold creating another Djinn. Now say Infinity not only denies the wish but the Desire mismatch causes a vacuum and creates a creature the exact opposite of a Genie. Something with inherently nothing and absence instead of infinity and a desire for infinity itself. You're now it's food. These creatures are bad enough antagonists that Djinn rarely grant large wishes just in case this occurs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978628#post978628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you have obligations to play up the whole Djinn theme. As in, there are periodic sacrifices you have to make in return for your power, things that seem generous at first but chip away at your own well-being for the sake of others. It could be a reversal of the whole &quot;everything comes at a price&quot; theme at the heart of wish-based stories, but that price effects both parties.<br /> <br /> So maybe every character has a Desire crux. Maybe the flavor of their essence is wealth or fame or political power, and they're required once a season to use their essence to bestow that trait upon someone in need. They quickly learn that doing so comes with a price. A charity organization that's struggling is in need of money, and their serendipity comes from a disaster that would otherwise not happen, a disaster that earns them government funding. A once-famous movie star is looking for a comeback and earns it in the form of a vicious attack from a rabid fan that pushes her right back into the spotlight. An aspiring politician who has always been overshadowed by his senator wife wants to be powerful in his own right, and he gets that opportunity when she's assassinated on stage. It's bittersweet opportunities, and they wear down on the soul of the djinn as well... Moreover, those wins are hard earned, so when things go south again for them, they'll be more inclined to take a wish granted to them by the patrons, more inclined to perpetuate the virus of djinnness(TM).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Flavours of Desire. Though I was more thinking of how new CofD games are going with different interpretations of the stats and I was thinking of something like a merge of Demon and Mummy where the character has access to cosmic power and can perpetuate and grant wishes to themselves (not sure how to make the powers. small at first prolly with larger powerstat powers being larger and more biblical in proportion). The more they use their own power for their own Desire the higher the powerstat will climb (slow at first but at exponential growth (to make high power desirability but also scary)). It is Infinity growing within you/your soul. The only way to stave it off is to channel infinity elsewhere. This takes the form of either osmosis (My minds eye looks at it like a liquid for some reason) with other Djinn or through Desire of humans (aka wish granting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:55:51-07:00","id":978719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978645#post978645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then, isn't that Mummy? Do the Arisen not answer the &quot;Wishes&quot; of their Cults?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, It would have to be wish fulfillment for your own self-interest. The self-interest being fear of withering away so it looks like altruism. I like the idea of an asymmetrical exchange. To the human subject it looks like a wish fulfillment or even demands being met. to the Genie it is a matter of survival and resource management.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:04:39-07:00","id":978724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978716#post978716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I was trying to think of possible antagonists. Like what about Selfish Djinn that go allwrong and end up going ravenous time bombs (very low on the Integrity Stat). What about humans for which wishes don't go as planned and search out the Djinn for Revenge and to make it right but to do that they go after character's essence or contacts or family. What about Djinn who are exactly like you but desire to use you as a repository for their wish-giving without your consent. You gain power quickly and so does the edge of oblivion creep closer dangerously fast.<br /> <br /> My idea for the theme of losing relevance was that the higher up your power stat you go (possibly with interactions between levels of your integrity stat or something) the more your soul starts to become absorbed into infinity. They start becoming everything all at once which translates to nothing happening. The character's parents and friends forget about them. Eventually they just stop existing. In game terms they lose their social merits.<br /> <br /> Maybe you can stave off the Powerstat from climbing too high too fast by channeling infinity into a target. It's easy enough between Djinn but then it's (usually) like osmosis. It equalizes (somewhat) the power between them. But with non-Djinn, you need a desire from the subject. They have to really want the manifestation of infinity. They have to really wish for it. No contract, just straight up desire. Most Djinn choose carefully. They find someone who would want their wish bad enough. Some nefarious Djinn cause situations in which the a subject would desire something only for the Djinn to randomly show up plucking the subject from their sticky situation.<br /> <br /> But say desire does not match the wish. Say the wish is big enough that infinity might take hold creating another Djinn. Now say Infinity not only denies the wish but the Desire mismatch causes a vacuum and creates a creature the exact opposite of a Genie. Something with inherently nothing and absence instead of infinity and a desire for infinity itself. You're now it's food. These creatures are bad enough antagonists that Djinn rarely grant large wishes just in case this occurs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I like the idea of Flavours of Desire. Though I was more thinking of how new CofD games are going with different interpretations of the stats and I was thinking of something like a merge of Demon and Mummy where the character has access to cosmic power and can perpetuate and grant wishes to themselves (not sure how to make the powers. small at first prolly with larger powerstat powers being larger and more biblical in proportion). The more they use their own power for their own Desire the higher the powerstat will climb (slow at first but at exponential growth (to make high power desirability but also scary)). It is Infinity growing within you/your soul. The only way to stave it off is to channel infinity elsewhere. This takes the form of either osmosis (My minds eye looks at it like a liquid for some reason) with other Djinn or through Desire of humans (aka wish granting).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have some expansive thoughts, but I'm about to maybe head out the door.<br /> <br /> But maybe having relationships with other people/djinn (particularly granting wishes?) is what keeps them anchored and prevents them from being dispersed in the ether of infinity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:26:34-07:00","id":978733,"title":"","content":"Djinn might be viable. Muslim folklore even lists five varieties: Marids, Ifrits, Shaitans, Ghuls, and Janns. So we have the good-old &quot;5 inborn splats&quot; deal going on. They are associated with fire *gives the Qashmallim the side-eye* and are imbued with free will. After Demon took a more technognostic view of angels and demons, djinn could be an interesting way to introduce a splat rooted in a more traditional view of divinity, but still have an alien perspective open to interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 09-29-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:05:04-07:00","id":978745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978645#post978645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then, isn't that Mummy? Do the Arisen not answer the &quot;Wishes&quot; of their Cults?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure... do mummies serve their cults in that way? I've never read it (now waiting for 2e), in many ways I presume that the cults are largely supposed to be serving the mummy. I was also thinking for ChroD, maybe the genie isn't stuck in their bottle but perhaps tries to live a normal life elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:09:15-07:00","id":978747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978719#post978719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, It would have to be wish fulfillment for your own self-interest. The self-interest being fear of withering away so it looks like altruism. I like the idea of an asymmetrical exchange. To the human subject it looks like a wish fulfillment or even demands being met. to the Genie it is a matter of survival and resource management.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got nothing against Djinn, but this still sounds like Demon is currently, in many ways... because I believe Demon's make pacts largely as a matter of survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:47:24-07:00","id":978966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978747#post978747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got nothing against Djinn, but this still sounds like Demon is currently, in many ways... because I believe Demon's make pacts largely as a matter of survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>But djinn don't make pacts in a metaphysical sense. &quot;Granting wishes&quot; means performing a service, not altering reality - eg, when (the original) Aladdin wished for a palace, the djinn didn't conjure one up, it built one (just that it was powerful enough to do so &quot;normally&quot; in a single night). Likewise, twisting wishes into ending badly wasn't a big theme - djinn who offered them were more likely to play straight - if they wanted to hurt you, they'd just hurt you (djinn compelled into service might fuck with you, but that's kinda legitimate, really).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a djinn granting a wish was a common subset of another kind of story, where a character lucks into something great, and then shows by their subsequent actions whether they deserve it - if they don't, it turns on them, if they do, they go on to fame and fortume. In that sense, a djinn's wish might be less a trick than a test - while in folk tales, that's a meta thing rather than the djinn's Watsonian agenda, it could be something they're aware of in-game. Maybe interacting with humans - especially doing stuff for them - exaggerates the most telling parts of their character (ie, lays some condition relating to vice, virtue, and aspirations, forces the human to &quot;show themselves&quot; in some way, and focusses fate on them for good or ill).<br /> <br /> Not sure where to go from that, though, except if wishes are a test, they have to be one for the djinn as well. It would necessarily turn into a game about morality and consequence; Vampire is already one of those, but from an internal perspective rather than an external one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T16:32:46-07:00","id":979319,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Djinn aren't normally supernatural creatures, but souls that are being put through tests themselves - people who started out corrupted in some way and are transformed into beings of service, teaching not only humility but a proper lesson unto themselves? In that sense, to become human again (if perhaps with a few benefits of the process) they need to prove they have not only grown but provide a replacement, to keep the cycle going and make sure humanity grows as a species?<br /> <br /> Or does that sound too close to Promethean?<br /> <br /> Edit: Just realized I hadn't gotten the full story, and when I read back I realized I'd just effectively reposted what others posted better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:31:12-07:00","id":979347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979319#post979319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Djinn aren't normally supernatural creatures, but souls that are being put through tests themselves - people who started out corrupted in some way and are transformed into beings of service, teaching not only humility but a proper lesson unto themselves? In that sense, to become human again (if perhaps with a few benefits of the process) they need to prove they have not only grown but provide a replacement, to keep the cycle going and make sure humanity grows as a species?<br /> <br /> Or does that sound too close to Promethean?<br /> <br /> Edit: Just realized I hadn't gotten the full story, and when I read back I realized I'd just effectively reposted what others posted better.</div> </div> </div> </div>idk other people seem to be describing Demon (at least in what I've read). The lesson of promethean isn't humility. Prometheans are usually composed of human peaces but never were human themselves, so that's a pretty big difference. Prometheans aren't &quot;enslaved&quot; in any way, so that'd be big. Prometheans don't *have* to kill in order to make another, but this kind of Djinn would have to enslave another human (sure prometheans do have to make another).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T17:41:01-07:00","id":979356,"title":"","content":"That said lesson teaching is a key focus of beast...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:22:47-07:00","id":979385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979347#post979347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">idk other people seem to be describing Demon (at least in what I've read). The lesson of promethean isn't humility. Prometheans are usually composed of human peaces but never were human themselves, so that's a pretty big difference. Prometheans aren't &quot;enslaved&quot; in any way, so that'd be big. Prometheans don't *have* to kill in order to make another, but this kind of Djinn would have to enslave another human (sure prometheans do have to make another).</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case it's sort of a redemption by force; either you grow better than you were before and learn humility, or you are stuck in that life. Transferring that state of being to another person was both to show how Djinn not only make more of themselves, but also gives an end-goal to them. However, I'm not sure if &quot;enslaving&quot; would be the right term here. Certainly a Djinn <i>could</i> force another person to take on their role, and perhaps that's how it was done when Djinn were new, but they could find it easier to gift it to someone who is homeless or starving, or perhaps someone who genuinely wants to do good and needs to learn their own self worth. Maybe they trick someone deplorable into taking the role, or use it as revenge on the person who referred them or forced them to take the role. The role is a curse, yes, but it could be a blessing to someone who genuinely has nowhere kinder to go (and in the world/chronicles of darkness, such kindnesses are few and far between).<br /> <br /> Heck, someone could wish for the role themselves, either in a bid for power or for fun, only to learn that such power not only comes with consequences but expectations. It'd amount to a lesson that Djinn and Genie are often used for - be careful what you wish for.<br /> <br /> Not perfect, I know. Just trying to hash out an idea that has been niggling at the back of my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:56:45-07:00","id":979628,"title":"","content":"Personally I would like to see Magical Girls, I know there are fan-games such as Princess: The Hopeful (and its humorous oWoD predecessor Senshi: The Merchandising) but I'd like to see it done officially. Or alternately, I'd want to see superheroes and supervillains done in the CofD as a gameline.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr Ninjas. I tried to make a fan-game on RPG.net years ago called Ninja: The Hidden, inspired by works such as Naruto and Ninja Gaiden, but I later got banned from that site after getting into a fight with a guy who turned out to be one of the more influential mods on that site. Stupid of me to do so, but I digress.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe point is, I could complete my concept for the fan-game Ninja: The Hidden on this forum. I would use the 1E rules though, as I dislike 2E's mechanics and I'm more familiar with 1E anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 10-01-2016, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:06:19-07:00","id":979699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977524#post977524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but I think that would fall into <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1630_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1630\" data-vbnamecard=\"1630\">Jacob</a>'s point about being in the games without being a &quot;core&quot; part of the games. A general sense of alienation is part of the core CofD atmosphere, so it seeps into all the games in various ways. I wanted to highlight the games were alienation - and that specific source of alienation - was a direct central aspect of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, the specific source of alienation is a central aspect of these games but I don't agree with what you've picked out. (See subsequent reply to earlier post.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:49:11-07:00","id":979734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point wasn't inherently arguing for or against there being more gamelines.<br /> <br /> It was to argue that the focus of &quot;what should be a new gameline,&quot; needs to be around what kind of story the game tells, not what kind of creature hasn't been used yet (or at least hasn't been used for standard PC types since everything has been used so far).</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that your position it primarily against, but I may be reading too much into what you've written below. As for creature, I'd argue that the kind of creature does make a difference from a branding point of view. I know that a game were you play wraiths or aliens is far more exciting to me than one where you play maho-shojo (but that's just me not wanting to mix my superhero genre with my horror genre).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think there's a lot of focus on these already, and certainly enough that making a whole new gameline can become forced:<br /> <br /> Cultural assimilation is a major aspect of Promethean, Changeling (there's a reason why &quot;kidnapped by aliens&quot; is considered a valid Durance), Mummy, and assumed to be for Deviant (who seem like they're going to cover more of the &quot;alien stranded on Earth&quot; side of it even if they're not aliens). These are all games were being an &quot;outsider&quot; - either by birth or by supernatural influence - and trying to come to terms with modern life and how (if at all) to assimilate into a new culture are core parts of the play experience. Assimilation as a negative external factor is present in a lot of the antagonists of the games, but probably most strongly in the Seers of the Throne with Mage who's whole MO is to assimilate to the wishes of the Exarchs and be content with the culture they promote.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that cultural assimilation isn't a major aspect of Promethean as the signature monsters aren't faced with the dilemma of giving up what they are to become what is around them. That choice is all loaded onto the end and from a plot perspective, the game makes the assumption that it is a desirable end. Now imagine you're a native american and in a position where you must give up bits and pieces of your culture if you're going to survive (and maybe even prosper) in the white man's world. Promethean doesn't confront that issue at all. Prometheans steadily gain more of what they are (rather like consistently winning at the craps table) until they cash out at the chronicle's end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cultural appropriation is literally a source of magical power in Mage as well, making it fodder for both sides of the main struggle of the game. It's not as core as assimilation is to the other games above, but one of the five major PC Orders treats it as their special magical skill, and none of the Orders think poorly of using Sleeper cultural practices to their own ends with minimal to no respect for those cultures, with a second PC Order that has using appropriation to control Sleeper occult societies to direct mages to proper instruction and keep everyone else &quot;safe.&quot; The Free Council, Guardians of the Veil, and the Seers all deal with this in spades. Demon also gets in significantly on appropriation issues considering you have to literally appropriate human lives to create Covers to hide yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, there's no focus on this issue. And arguably that's kind of a good thing because if Mage remarked too closely on cultural magical practices it would just further illuminate how the Euro-centric thaumaturgical tradition it's loosely based on is an example of the worst kinds of cultural (mis)appropriation. And at no time does its text wrestle with the problem of cultural appropriation. It's core themes are obsession with mysteries. Which is exactly as it should be, another game can deeply focus on the humanistic issues of cultural (mis)appropriation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Growing old and irrelevant aren't something I think are a valid single theme. They're two related themes (being old doesn't stop you from being relevant, but it does make it more difficult, and it's easy to be irrelevant and young). Vampire is very strongly focused on the themes of the detachment that comes with age. The whole 2e Humanity/Touchstone system is built specifically around the narrative conflict of remaining emotionally attached to fragile mortal things that die as you continue on in your immortality; living too long is a direct source of detachment rolls in the game. Mummy and Demon are the two games with relevancy being core themes. Mummy does &quot;old and irrelevant&quot; as a core thematic issue, because that's essentially what they are. Ancient immortal beings who are bound to the whims of masters that died out so long ago no humans know about them. They awaken with huge gaps of time lost as cultures move on during their sleep, leaving them detached from all this new &quot;young&quot; stuff, and the are forced to do seemingly pointless tasks for the Judges while using the time before going back to sleep to try to make themselves relevant again through their cults. Demons are more just about relevancy, because they are entities born of a singular purpose that they abandoned. The whole task of trying to find a purpose and create your Hell is about defining what makes you relevant again. In some ways this is also a core theme of Geist, but only in the rejection of being concerned with such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we agree to disagree here. Growing old and irrelevant is closely linked to feelings of disenfranchisement and is a ongoing phenomenon playing itself right now in U.S. politics (on the global scale) and Hollywood (on a smaller but still broad scale). I agree that age is an important core theme in V:tR but I'd argue that it isn't irrelevance that the Vampire's (especially Elders) face, but rather the ennui that accompanies extreme success. I'd also not that the detachment/touchstone mechanic in V:tR isn't designed to show us how relevant a Vampire remains to the society around her but rather how relevant that society remains to her. That's very different from what's happening in an anime like Noragami (which indeed is exactly what I picture when I envision what a CoD take on gods/goddesses would be like).<br /> <br /> I simply don't agree about D:tD. They're highly relevant because they can simply rewrite the reality around them (not to mention that they have built in mechanics for granting powers to mortals through contracts). Seems pretty relevant to me. One might also argue that they are closer to newborns than ancient things since the Fall leaves them in a very different existential place than their previous Angelic one.<br /> <br /> Finally, I get why you would argue that Mummy fulfills this role but with their lack of memories I'd argue that Mummy fulfills another core theme related to age--forgetting what you once were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronic illness isn't a theme or a story. It's a myriad of conditions people have. And zombies are not a metaphor for any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree here too. Chronic illness is a valid theme and the plots of many stories do revolve around it (think of Raistlin in the Dragonlance Chronicles). And especially in the humanistic tradition of storytelling, it easily becomes an antagonist that characters must cope with (think also of A Beautiful Mind). And Zombies are a perfect metaphor, especially for chronic diseases where things like leprosy and TB (which may soon once again be incurable and even untreatable at the rate drug-resistance is growing) are often show-cased as the poster children.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that point of humanistic literary traditions is to remark upon the human condition and chronic illness is a part of that condition (as are disabilities).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=977365#post977365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alienation due to traumatic experience is a huge part of Werewolf, and Changeling (Promethean and Deviant, again assuming from spoiled stuff about it, are about different sorts of alienation). Werewolves hunt and kill things that threaten both sides of the Gauntlet for their territory, only to return home to people that don't understand them, or their mental struggles as they don't get a real off switch from hunter mode. Even the wolf-blooded and humans of their Pack never really understand what its like. Changelings have assimilation as a major theme precises because they left home, and came back to find themselves completely alienated from their old lives. The vast majority can't just slip back in from where they left off, and even then it will never be like it was as the demands of being one of the Lost constantly draw them away from family and friends; who aren't going to be able to break through and connect to the changeling's twisted experiences with the Gentry.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I don't agree we can dismiss the existing game lines as &quot;not deeply focused&quot; on any of these issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I think the central focus of both Werewolf and Changeling are vastly different from alienation due to voluntary experience. In Werewolf's case alienation has a familial source. You're different from normal people because you are part of a Pack. And in Changeling's case the trauma very clearly has an involuntary source. Being assualted is vastly different than military service in a warzone. Both leave you changed but those changes aren't the same and these days U.S. society has an easier time coping with victim's of involuntary trauma than those who voluntarily suffered trauma.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I don't agree that we can agree that the existing game lines are deeply focused on any of these issues. Or that a singular take on any of the issues either of us highlighted is sufficient. There's always room for more stories.<br /> <br /> More to the point though, I think there's plenty of space for more gamelines. I don't think OPP needs to stick to a one new game per year schedule though. I'd rather they take their time and make each game the best it can be. If (and hopefully it's when) they give us games with Wraiths, Aliens, Zombies, Mad Scientists, and Dieties, I know that I'll be one of the first in line to tell them, &quot;shut up and take my money.&quot; Because these are all games I would play (Wraith 1E especially remains my favorite WoD gameline and I've eagerly looked forward to a CoD version for going on 1.5 decades now).<br /> <br /> And for the record, I'm super-excited for D:tR because finally we'll be getting a game that covers a multitude of experimental victim horror ranging from The Alligator People to The Invisible Man, Dr. Jekyll &amp; Mr. Hyde, on through to Firestarter, Carrie, and Stranger Things (well-played Netflix, #howtimely). I'm every bit as excited by the <i>what</i> we play as I am about the social themes the game digs into. And while the games do need a good story, the <i>what</i> the gribbly is, is no less important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 10-01-2016, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:08:12-07:00","id":979816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979734#post979734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that your position it primarily against, but I may be reading too much into what you've written below.</div> </div> </div> </div>My position is open but skeptical/critical. I'm largely viewing things from how I'd imagine Rich has to think when he's getting pitched ideas for new games. It's not that I'm against new games, but I want to see people make really good pitches for them that translate into good games, rather than, &quot;hey this is a neat idea!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for creature, I'd argue that the kind of creature does make a difference from a branding point of view. </div> </div> </div>It does, but it swings both ways. Adding playable ghosts (something that's probably one of the most asked for creature types the CofD hasn't done so far) makes things messy for all the brands that operate on the idea of ghosts not being that sort of creature.<br /> <br /> As to your responses, I'm not going to go through each point by point.<br /> <br /> I find most of the rebuttals very unconvincing, because they defeat themselves constantly, or just focuses on one example and skips the other which comes off as simply trying to avoid one. You say Promethean doesn't have assimilation as a major aspect, yet you acknowledge that it is literally built into the game. Mage isn't doesn't have cultural appropriation as a thing, but it rankles you as being culturally appropriative in a negative way. Etc.<br /> <br /> You argue for humanistic metaphor, but reject examples for being metaphorical instead of literal. And yes, exploring the human condition is important, individual aspects of the human condition are not inherently what makes a full game. Just because X is something humans go through, doesn't mean it can carry a game by itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Growing old and irrelevant is closely linked to feelings of disenfranchisement... </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are. However growing old is not the same as growing irrelevant. Both lead to feelings to feelings of disenfranchisement separately. That's why I argued these are two different issues. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're highly relevant because they can simply rewrite the reality around them (not to mention that they have built in mechanics for granting powers to mortals through contracts). </div> </div> </div>Power is not the same as relevance. Demons certainly have the power to become relevant. If they didn't the theme would be lost on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chronic illness is a valid theme and the plots of many stories do revolve around it (think of Raistlin in the Dragonlance Chronicles). And especially in the humanistic tradition of storytelling, it easily becomes an antagonist that characters must cope with (think also of A Beautiful Mind). And Zombies are a perfect metaphor, especially for chronic diseases where things like leprosy and TB (which may soon once again be incurable and even untreatable at the rate drug-resistance is growing) are often show-cased as the poster children. </div> </div> </div>Chronic illness is a thing, not a theme. War isn't a theme. The glory of war is a theme. The horror of war is a theme. War itself is just a setting that you insert themes into. Chronic illness can be used to frame all sorts of themes, but it is not a theme in and of itself.<br /> <br /> I also don't see how your argument for zombies is ever going to work as a game. It's very hard to take, &quot;mindless undead cannibals that should be destroyed before they spread,&quot; as anything other than an argument for eugenics and &quot;euthanizing&quot; people with chronic conditions. CofD splats are monsters. Sane and rational humans should be able to come to the conclusion that any of them are too dangerous to be kept alive (hence militant Hunters). When you say that zombies are a perfect metaphor for chronical illness, you're saying that <b>people with chronic ailments are monsters</b> to be put down.<br /> <br /> And that's before even getting into the issue of never addressing how you keep the idea of zombies (and really any iteration of them) as playable characters without just making them non-vampire, non-promethean, non-geist, smart undead that tells a story that none of other game lines could tell just as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I think the central focus of both Werewolf and Changeling are vastly different from alienation due to voluntary experience. </div> </div> </div>The alienation of soldiers has nothing to do with the level of voluntary choice in becoming a soldier. Plenty of drafted soldiers have the same issues as volunteer ones.<br /> <br /> As well highlighted in American media, the narrative of the drafted Vietnam vet's return to civilian life being rife with alienation and difficulty doesn't really change as we move to media that focuses on the related narrative for vet's of more recent wars. There are differences of course for individual characters and stories. But the point remains that the core thematic story does not hinge on whether service was voluntary or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Werewolf's case alienation has a familial source. You're different from normal people because you are part of a Pack. And in Changeling's case the trauma very clearly has an involuntary source. </div> </div> </div>These are both factually inaccurate to the games in question.<br /> <br /> Werewolves alienation is because they were drafted into an endless war whether they wanted it or not. It doesn't come from a familial source as the default; Luna chooses their hunters as they wish. You are different whether you have a Pack or not. Werewolves form Packs both because of instinct, and because Packs are the only source of camaraderie available to them. Just like soldiers tend to find other soldiers even after leaving their service to form social units with.<br /> <br /> Changeling does not present things as solely involuntary. Lots of eventual-Lost went along with their Keepers perfectly willingly and blind to the reality of the horrors they would face (again, plenty of overlap with many soldiers experiences; esp. ones sold on the myth of the glory of war). Once a human is in Arcadia, yes, they lose agency and their continual trauma becomes involuntary, but that doesn't mean it started that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:59:49-07:00","id":980119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979628#post979628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would like to see Magical Girls, I know there are fan-games such as Princess: The Hopeful (and its humorous oWoD predecessor Senshi: The Merchandising) but I'd like to see it done officially. Or alternately, I'd want to see superheroes and supervillains done in the CofD as a gameline.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr Ninjas. I tried to make a fan-game on RPG.net years ago called Ninja: The Hidden, inspired by works such as Naruto and Ninja Gaiden, but I later got banned from that site after getting into a fight with a guy who turned out to be one of the more influential mods on that site. Stupid of me to do so, but I digress.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe point is, I could complete my concept for the fan-game Ninja: The Hidden on this forum. I would use the 1E rules though, as I dislike 2E's mechanics and I'm more familiar with 1E anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious question, putting aside the problem that we're not going to get major templates that aren't based on recognizable monsters: what would a magical girl game do that isn't already covered by Mage and the upcoming Deviant?<br /> <br /> And what character concepts would be possible in ninja that couldn't be done in any of the other existing games? Wouldn't ninjas be better as a splat for an existing game? I'd suggest you try making a bloodline, a Lodge, a Legacy, an Entitlement or Court, or a Compact or Conspiracy instead of a full splat. <br /> <br /> Actually, here's an idea: a Conspiracy of ninjas with an Endowment that allows them to shapeshift who fight for the common people against monsters who hide in the ranks of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T00:57:44-07:00","id":980148,"title":"","content":"Note to self: Eventually run Demon in a feudal Japan setting where the players are ninja rather than spies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T06:51:17-07:00","id":980221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980148#post980148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note to self: Eventually run Demon in a feudal Japan setting where the players are ninja rather than spies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... Aren't ninja's spies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T07:49:33-07:00","id":980236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980221#post980221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Aren't ninja's spies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Difference between a cow and a mammal. That said, spies have very different associated imagery than ninjas, and spying's primary focus is on information gathering while a ninja's isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-02-2016, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:45:35-07:00","id":980305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980236#post980236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Difference between a cow and a mammal. That said, spies have very different associated imagery than ninjas, and spying's primary focus is on information gathering while a ninja's isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually an appropriated, Americanized vision of what a Ninja is. They primarily gather intelligence and are really no different from spies and/or commandos (depending on their mission parameters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:27:06-07:00","id":980321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My position is open but skeptical/critical. I'm largely viewing things from how I'd imagine Rich has to think when he's getting pitched ideas for new games. It's not that I'm against new games, but I want to see people make really good pitches for them that translate into good games, rather than, &quot;hey this is a neat idea!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Herein is probably the problem. OPP, like most businesses tends to work with a small stable of known Developers (afterall, nothing is actually so personal as business). Beyond a game like Deviant I'm not actually sure what their current stable of devs would propose that isn't one of the gribblies we've discussed and that I'd actually be willing to pay money for (maybe Hill's Furies game but that's about it). Wraiths, Aliens, and other monster movie monsters are what remains. I don't mind if OPP takes its time and I wouldn't venture to guess exactly how they decide which pitch to support (and I think Rich isn't the only filter it has to go through). I only know what I'm going to pay money for. The fact that there are not less than three fangames that do Aliens on these boards alone might be an indicator that the market is ready for one should OPP find the right developer to lead the effort. But ultimately, let us not forget that business realities play an important role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, but it swings both ways. Adding playable ghosts (something that's probably one of the most asked for creature types the CofD hasn't done so far) makes things messy for all the brands that operate on the idea of ghosts not being that sort of creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your assumption is that Wraiths == &quot;playable ghosts&quot;. This is not the assumption I would make and not the kind of thing I would pitch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to your responses, I'm not going to go through each point by point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that you more or less did...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find most of the rebuttals very unconvincing, because they defeat themselves constantly, or just focuses on one example and skips the other which comes off as simply trying to avoid one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say Promethean doesn't have assimilation as a major aspect, yet you acknowledge that it is literally built into the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry backending assimilation into a game's end state is not sufficient to say that game addresses assimilation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">age isn't doesn't have cultural appropriation as a thing, but it rankles you as being culturally appropriative in a negative way. Etc.<br /> <br /> You argue for humanistic metaphor, but reject examples for being metaphorical instead of literal. And yes, exploring the human condition is important, individual aspects of the human condition are not inherently what makes a full game. Just because X is something humans go through, doesn't mean it can carry a game by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>My rule of thumb is if it can carry a novel then it can carry a game. Look again, examples were given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they are. However growing old is not the same as growing irrelevant. Both lead to feelings to feelings of disenfranchisement separately. That's why I argued these are two different issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we agree &quot;young+irrelevant&quot; =/= &quot;old+irrelevant&quot; =/= &quot;young&quot; =/= &quot;old&quot;. Still not seeing your point. I'm arguing for the &quot;old+irrelevant&quot; one BTW. If we wanted to reduce it down to just &quot;old&quot; then we might as well reduce gamelines down to just V:tR which can be used to address themes that appear in all of the other games. But that rather begs the question of why we have so many games...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power is not the same as relevance. Demons certainly have the power to become relevant. If they didn't the theme would be lost on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree to disagree. When one has power, one automatically has relevance. It's foolish to think otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronic illness is a thing, not a theme. War isn't a theme. The glory of war is a theme. The horror of war is a theme. War itself is just a setting that you insert themes into. Chronic illness can be used to frame all sorts of themes, but it is not a theme in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again examples were given but also I think you both lack a working knowledge of the notion of theme, the definition of thing, and any imagination to see how you might surface themes like chronic illness and war in stories. On the whole your argument is similar to &quot;Jesus is a person and not a theme&quot; but, Jesus is definitely a theme of Where the Red Fern Grows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't see how your argument for zombies is ever going to work as a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of imagination. Consider iZombie (or even the song re:Your Brains).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very hard to take, &quot;mindless undead cannibals that should be destroyed before they spread,&quot; as anything other than an argument for eugenics and &quot;euthanizing&quot; people with chronic conditions. CofD splats are monsters. Sane and rational humans should be able to come to the conclusion that any of them are too dangerous to be kept alive (hence militant Hunters). When you say that zombies are a perfect metaphor for chronical illness, you're saying that <b>people with chronic ailments are monsters</b> to be put down.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've gone overboard here. I don't see the eugenics and euthanasia angle at all. But then again I don't limit my worldview of Zombies to brainless rotting shamblers. (Again, see above examples and start thinking outside of the tiny box you've drawn for yourself.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's before even getting into the issue of never addressing how you keep the idea of zombies (and really any iteration of them) as playable characters without just making them non-vampire, non-promethean, non-geist, smart undead that tells a story that none of other game lines could tell just as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the V:tR reduction problem all over again. We can tell the same stories that D:tD, W:tF, B:tP, M:tAw, P:tC, C:tL, etc. do with just V:tR. By your argument, if we have V:tR, why do we need the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alienation of soldiers has nothing to do with the level of voluntary choice in becoming a soldier. Plenty of drafted soldiers have the same issues as volunteer ones.<br /> <br /> As well highlighted in American media, the narrative of the drafted Vietnam vet's return to civilian life being rife with alienation and difficulty doesn't really change as we move to media that focuses on the related narrative for vet's of more recent wars. There are differences of course for individual characters and stories. But the point remains that the core thematic story does not hinge on whether service was voluntary or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I'm just not buying your coolaid that C:tL addresses this kind of alienation. Also not buying that a single gameline couldn't focus on it but I sense we've been talking past each other for a while now...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979816#post979816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are both factually inaccurate to the games in question.<br /> <br /> Werewolves alienation is because they were drafted into an endless war whether they wanted it or not. It doesn't come from a familial source as the default; Luna chooses their hunters as they wish. You are different whether you have a Pack or not. Werewolves form Packs both because of instinct, and because Packs are the only source of camaraderie available to them. Just like soldiers tend to find other soldiers even after leaving their service to form social units with.<br /> <br /> Changeling does not present things as solely involuntary. Lots of eventual-Lost went along with their Keepers perfectly willingly and blind to the reality of the horrors they would face (again, plenty of overlap with many soldiers experiences; esp. ones sold on the myth of the glory of war). Once a human is in Arcadia, yes, they lose agency and their continual trauma becomes involuntary, but that doesn't mean it started that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>We agree to disagree. Werewolf is very much a game about peer pressure (see some of its inspirations, especially Sons of Anarchy). But also I think you're forgetting that Luna doesn't choose who is a Werewolf (there are the Pure afterall) and who is a Pack member (which is controlled by the Pack itself). And Changeling, taking place after the eponymous gribblies make their escape (this alone makes it different from military service) from Arcadia, doesn't focus on the how &quot;it started that way&quot; aspect. The important part is &quot;they lose agency and their continual trauma becomes involuntary.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the whole, when you can develop some compelling examples beyond your one-dimensional interpretations of the gamelines (I'd look at other media if I were you) then I might admit you have some basis for your position. But as I see it right now, it's completely unsupportable reductionism that whimsically picks and chooses what to reduce rather than applying reductionist principles in any consistent and justified fashion. I'd also keep in mind that imagination is the key component to creativity. Just because you can't imagine how a thing might be done, doesn't entail that a thing is impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:44:56-07:00","id":980330,"title":"","content":"Is this thread going to be &quot;Jacob tries to explain why Heavy Arms is wrong in long, laborious detail&quot;, or are we still talking about potential ideas for gamelines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:53:58-07:00","id":980436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978724#post978724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have some expansive thoughts, but I'm about to maybe head out the door.<br /> <br /> But maybe having relationships with other people/djinn (particularly granting wishes?) is what keeps them anchored and prevents them from being dispersed in the ether of infinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is what I was thinking. This is making my brain go wild with ideas. (enough that I'm actually a little afraid that a developer might want to make it but might not want to after all our theory crafting. I REALLY want this ^.^. Genies man! how cool!)<br /> <br /> Honestly, this would satisfy everything that I would want from a new gameline. It has something to explore that hasn't been fully explored, has lots of story potential, and would thematically be a lot of fun!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978733#post978733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Djinn might be viable. Muslim folklore even lists five varieties: Marids, Ifrits, Shaitans, Ghuls, and Janns. So we have the good-old &quot;5 inborn splats&quot; deal going on. They are associated with fire *gives the Qashmallim the side-eye* and are imbued with free will. After Demon took a more technognostic view of angels and demons, djinn could be an interesting way to introduce a splat rooted in a more traditional view of divinity, but still have an alien perspective open to interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So This is Awesome. I did a bit of research, not much, but found enough that Djinn are actually a lot more expansive than I thought. There's folklore elements and pop culture elements and just in general a lot of stuff to pull from!<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed when I read <a href=\"http://www.djinnuniverse.com/types-of-djinn\" target=\"_blank\">this site</a> is that the colors of Djinn seem to actually be relatively important which brings to mind maybe that could be a very different version of the social splat. See below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> COLORS<br /> Djinn are also denoted by colors:<br /> <br /> BLUE<br /> Older, intelligent djinn, often ambivalent about humans.<br /> <br /> YELLOW<br /> Leaders of families and small clans. Less powerful than Blue but more powerful than Green.<br /> <br /> GREEN<br /> Young and immature djinn, ofter playful and mischievous.<br /> <br /> BLACK<br /> Powerful djinn, thought to be kings. It is not known if there is one king or multiple ones.<br /> <br /> RED<br /> Hostile and aggressive djinn. </div> </div> </div>Could prolly change those around a bit but really this could be a type of quasi-pyramid style social splat. Imagine that as soon as Infinity takes hold in the proto Genie. The character''s soul (or something) gets connected to all and everything and in that matter has a somewhat tie to all others that have had their souls replaced by Infinity, aka other Djinn. So at the moment of becoming a Djinn, they are already a color. They can change colors but for the most part that could be story long adventures. Due to the Nature of Djinn higher colors like Black and Blue may not be literally as powerful as others but there could definitely be perks to each color and, even though it's almost a secondary X splat it is regarded as quasi-social. <br /> <br /> I don't really know, but I feel like you could make something out of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=978966#post978966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But djinn don't make pacts in a metaphysical sense. &quot;Granting wishes&quot; means performing a service, not altering reality - eg, when (the original) Aladdin wished for a palace, the djinn didn't conjure one up, it built one (just that it was powerful enough to do so &quot;normally&quot; in a single night). Likewise, twisting wishes into ending badly wasn't a big theme - djinn who offered them were more likely to play straight - if they wanted to hurt you, they'd just hurt you (djinn compelled into service might fuck with you, but that's kinda legitimate, really).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a djinn granting a wish was a common subset of another kind of story, where a character lucks into something great, and then shows by their subsequent actions whether they deserve it - if they don't, it turns on them, if they do, they go on to fame and fortume. In that sense, a djinn's wish might be less a trick than a test - while in folk tales, that's a meta thing rather than the djinn's Watsonian agenda, it could be something they're aware of in-game. Maybe interacting with humans - especially doing stuff for them - exaggerates the most telling parts of their character (ie, lays some condition relating to vice, virtue, and aspirations, forces the human to &quot;show themselves&quot; in some way, and focusses fate on them for good or ill).<br /> <br /> Not sure where to go from that, though, except if wishes are a test, they have to be one for the djinn as well. It would necessarily turn into a game about morality and consequence; Vampire is already one of those, but from an internal perspective rather than an external one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, this gives me ideas.So I was thinking about what kind of powers Genies would have and was having trouble trying to figure out how to differentiate their powers from a Mage's. I still like the near super cosmic power a la the Disney Genie but I really think a mixture of &quot;service&quot; based, and near unlimited reality warping would be best. There needs to be some sort of distinction between what a Djinn can do at lower levels and at higher levels as well as a distinction between using them for yourself or for others. <br /> <br /> I was talking with my boyfriend the other day about it and one of the ideas he had was that the powers/abilities of Djinn were all &quot;target&quot; based. So like what ever powers you had to be able to fulfill wishes/demands/&amp;c would need a target who had an appropriate amount of Desire. If you imagine Infinity as a liquid, imagine how you would use up that resource (so that it doesn't just well up inside you... more on that idea in a moment...keyword: multiplier). You would need a receptacle for that liquid (aka the Target). Now you need to pour a certain amount of liquid (aka the wish/service/demand), for that the opening on the receptacle needs to be large enough for all of the liquid that is being poured (aka the desire of the target). The consequence for a large wish on a target without the appropriate amount of Desire would be like trying to pour water from a bathtub into a 500mL bottle (aka this could be what creates those Vaacuum creature antagonists that I thought about earlier.). There would have to be something like that amount of Infinity could only be poured (either effectively or at all) at higher powerstat levels or something of the like but I still like the idea.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about using it on yourself but I imagine that it would have to be either that you would need to use the powers on yourself at a cost of some sort of fuel stat (with Desire being automatic so no need to calculate that) or that the Djinn would still need a (not-them) target but with the intended function to benefit the Djinn more than the Subject (imagine Jafar using that one short guy in the Movie Return of Jafar in how he used him as a proxy). Either would satisfy the theme of using the power on yourself increases the powerstat (imagine pouring Infinity into a target only to be channeled back at yourself) which can be a good thing but does get the character closer to the banes of higher powerstat (actually... wouldn't that be interesting if banes existed more in early powerstat since, thematically, the higher powerstat necessarily means that the character is closer to becoming infinity and washing away in cosmic relevance? hmmm got to think on this) and it is supposed to feel like a slippery slope between high powerstat and Oblivion.<br /> <br /> On a related note to that, what I meant by Multiplier is a thought I had a few days ago. I'm thinking that it could be somewhat hard to get out of the small powerstat stages so that those who are in it would have the Desire to increase it to accomplish the things they want to accomplish. For that there could be a... a something where not doing wishes/services/something for not your benefit causes some sort of multiplier on the possibility in rising in the Powerstat. This could because Infinity is just kind of &quot;welling&quot; inside the character so that it makes it easier to increase in size when a feedback loop (using powers for yourself) occurs. idk, exactly how it would be done but I like the thought. <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979385#post979385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case it's sort of a redemption by force; either you grow better than you were before and learn humility, or you are stuck in that life. Transferring that state of being to another person was both to show how Djinn not only make more of themselves, but also gives an end-goal to them. However, I'm not sure if &quot;enslaving&quot; would be the right term here. Certainly a Djinn <i>could</i> force another person to take on their role, and perhaps that's how it was done when Djinn were new, but they could find it easier to gift it to someone who is homeless or starving, or perhaps someone who genuinely wants to do good and needs to learn their own self worth. Maybe they trick someone deplorable into taking the role, or use it as revenge on the person who referred them or forced them to take the role. The role is a curse, yes, but it could be a blessing to someone who genuinely has nowhere kinder to go (and in the world/chronicles of darkness, such kindnesses are few and far between).<br /> <br /> Heck, someone could wish for the role themselves, either in a bid for power or for fun, only to learn that such power not only comes with consequences but expectations. It'd amount to a lesson that Djinn and Genie are often used for - be careful what you wish for.<br /> <br /> Not perfect, I know. Just trying to hash out an idea that has been niggling at the back of my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the &quot;Be careful what you wish for&quot; and &quot;this is a test&quot; portions. and I think they would be great as core themes to how it works. The &quot;Be careful what you wish for&quot; I feel is almost already really easy to include since becoming a Djinn could be a &quot;well I got my wish, now here's the consequences and/or responsibilities that came with it. <br /> <br /> The Tests I'm less certain how it would be done, so I'm curious: Could you elaborate? Cause I really like the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979734#post979734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I simply don't agree about D:tD. They're highly relevant because they can simply rewrite the reality around them (not to mention that they have built in mechanics for granting powers to mortals through contracts). Seems pretty relevant to me. One might also argue that they are closer to newborns than ancient things since the Fall leaves them in a very different existential place than their previous Angelic one.<br /> <br /> Finally, I get why you would argue that Mummy fulfills this role but with their lack of memories I'd argue that Mummy fulfills another core theme related to age--forgetting what you once were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda was thinking something similar here, yeah.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=979734#post979734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for the record, I'm super-excited for D:tR because finally we'll be getting a game that covers a multitude of experimental victim horror ranging from The Alligator People to The Invisible Man, Dr. Jekyll &amp; Mr. Hyde, on through to Firestarter, Carrie, and Stranger Things (well-played Netflix, #howtimely). I'm every bit as excited by the <i>what</i> we play as I am about the social themes the game digs into. And while the games do need a good story, the <i>what</i> the gribbly is, is no less important.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record: heck yeah! I'm really excited for this too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T15:13:45-07:00","id":980439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980436#post980436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the &quot;Be careful what you wish for&quot; and &quot;this is a test&quot; portions. and I think they would be great as core themes to how it works. The &quot;Be careful what you wish for&quot; I feel is almost already really easy to include since becoming a Djinn could be a &quot;well I got my wish, now here's the consequences and/or responsibilities that came with it.<br /> <br /> The Tests I'm less certain how it would be done, so I'm curious: Could you elaborate? Cause I really like the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I wrote that releasing oneself from being a Djinn required a test, I was thinking of it in terms of positive character growth. A redemption arc, as it were. However, I've rethought the idea, as the world in Chronicles of Darkness is not nearly that kind or optimistic.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Test in this case isn't so much improving oneself, but by becoming wise to the world in a way that doesn't break them. Know how people work across different types of places, the signs of how a person is thinking or feeling. In short, true empathy. This doesn't mean the character needs to be kind to other people with it - con artists use empathy simply to know what the people they're conning are thinking.<br /> <br /> Another aspect of the Test could involve making wishes happen without using supernatural powers - a feast for a city without conjuring it up, a new lease on life without changing a person's body, making a real change without forcing reality to accept it. In short, wisdom about the world, be it on social, physical or scientific principles, and making impossibilities work from within the system. Again, this can be both positive and negative.<br /> <br /> And one more idea could be making something happen while also being aware of the consequences, or removing oneself from said consequences. True foresight into an event, at least as far as one could be; this could involve the Djinn crafting a wish so it does not backfire on them, so it will go exactly as they entail it to without outside factors swinging it out of control. Rather difficult given the supernaturals and other forces (who can see the future already) already mucking about, but no test worth its mettle is easy for those partaking in it.<br /> <br /> In short, one of the things holding a Djinn back from being a Djinn is simply not being wise enough for it. That rather makes it a chicken and egg paradox then - you need wisdom to use your powers right, but once you have wisdom you're no longer a Djinn (or at least you need to take a successor afterwards). This does need more workshopping though. Hope its inspires more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T15:39:00-07:00","id":980450,"title":"","content":"As a crossover type, maybe the djinn could be interesting, maybe their &quot;Lamp&quot; has to be carried by another character. Maybe you couldn't have just a group of Djinn. Improsonment, and enslavement could be powerful themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:33:36-07:00","id":980495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980321#post980321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">This is actually an appropriated, Americanized vision of what a Ninja is. They primarily gather intelligence and are really no different from spies and/or commandos (depending on their mission parameters).</span></div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, their primary focus was sabotage rather than gathering intelligence (though of course as spies they still did gather intelligence, it just doesn't seem to be their primary focus).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry I'm just not buying your coolaid that C:tL addresses this kind of alienation. </div> </div> </div>.... the point of the game is that you are messed up from your durance (which explicitly can be willing) and now that you're back everything is different, that other people will never understand what you went through or understand how you changed, and you will never be the same. I mean god, Soldier specifically represents that horror. The thing that messed up the soldier kiths were the horrors of war and now they are forever separate from everyone, even their own family can't understand how they've changed or see you for how you really are anymore. And yet you think that the game doesn't address that kind of alienation.... It's not coolaid to think it's part of the game, it's explicitly part of the game if you just read the book for more than 2 minutes. The closest thing to an argument you could even reasonably have is that &quot;It's covers more than just that kind of alienation, and you want this theoretical gameline to Only describe that specific kind of alienation.&quot; But that sounds like a weird option when it's a major theme of C:tL but only want one character option from it rather than being able to be things other than just soldiers... ugh... *facedesk*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-02-2016, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T21:56:26-07:00","id":980581,"title":"","content":"On Magical Girls as gameline: Look, speaking as the guy who would do that, no one would do that.<br /> <br /> On Ninjas as gameline: And that's even more of a no.<br /> <br /> On Jacob missing the point: *drinks coffee, goes back to work*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:49:16-07:00","id":980610,"title":"","content":"I was talking to a friend today about a vague idea involving <i>genius loci</i>, and things of that ilk, but I feel like it's covered by other games, or just a really specific take on spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span st