ters-are-left?p=980610#post980610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking to a friend today about a vague idea involving <i>genius loci</i>, and things of that ilk, but I feel like it's covered by other games, or just a really specific take on spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, Mage 2e explicitly mentions them as Weird Inexplicable Shit and leaves it as an exercise for the ST. Too lazy to actually go search.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:32:27-07:00","id":980822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980623#post980623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, Mage 2e explicitly mentions them as Weird Inexplicable Shit and leaves it as an exercise for the ST. Too lazy to actually go search.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's basically just Mysterious Places stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T22:43:18-07:00","id":981280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980581#post980581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Magical Girls as gameline: Look, speaking as the guy who would do that, no one would do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A paradox, a paradox, a most ingenious paradox ...<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do magical girls straight up, I expect Scion 2e will suit you admirably - a world protected by ancient divinities and their descendants <i>looks</i> much more like the typical magical girl show than the CofD world where everything supernatural is horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:41:55-07:00","id":981292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=980618#post980618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I do think a ninja Conspiracy could work, now. And I would love the shit out of a True Fae antagonist that styled itself as either a magical girl or the Cute Animal Mentor of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I ever get to write a conspiracy for hunting changelings, you can bet your bottom dollar I will try very hard to lampoon magical girls and Changeling the Dreaming all in one go in doing so.<br /> <br /> Note: I say this as a rabid fan of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:49:53-07:00","id":981297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981280#post981280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A paradox, a paradox, a most ingenious paradox ...<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do magical girls straight up, I expect Scion 2e will suit you admirably - a world protected by ancient divinities and their descendants <i>looks</i> much more like the typical magical girl show than the CofD world where everything supernatural is horrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why on earth would I want to do them straight up though when I can tie them in knots and make their end point multiple choice though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:03:17-07:00","id":981304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981292#post981292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I ever get to write a conspiracy for hunting changelings, you can bet your bottom dollar I will try very hard to lampoon magical girls and Changeling the Dreaming all in one go in doing so.<br /> <br /> Note: I say this as a rabid fan of both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god arc here's an idea<br /> <br /> You know how Mage has conspiracies that hunt mages because they're being dicked around into doing it by the seers/the abyss<br /> <br /> What about a conspiracy secretly run by the true fae that hunts changelings by telling people they're eeeeeevil emotion eating monsters and giving them magic powers by showing up in the shape of cute animals and giving magic wands to teenagers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:35:42-07:00","id":981398,"title":"","content":"Magical Girls seems like the Japanese equivalent of the superhero genre to me. At least, that's how I feel. At its core, magical girls fight monsters as their raison d'etre. To me, that kind of story is already covered by Hunter of all games. I think that a Conspiracy would probably be better than anything else. Or, just as fun imho, use the Lucifuge - demonic familiars that make deals for granting powers, anyone? <br /> <br /> I don't really get the whole Djinn thing going on. I know that there are some people who really love the idea of djinn, but I don't get the themes that are going on here. What's up with being increasingly irrelevant? Doesn't that kind of contradict the idea of being a protagonist? IE- the persons who go out and do stuff to affect the world and shape the story? How would that even be playable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T06:45:26-07:00","id":981413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981304#post981304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh my god arc here's an idea<br /> <br /> You know how Mage has conspiracies that hunt mages because they're being dicked around into doing it by the seers/the abyss<br /> <br /> What about a conspiracy secretly run by the true fae that hunts changelings by telling people they're eeeeeevil emotion eating monsters and giving them magic powers by showing up in the shape of cute animals and giving magic wands to teenagers</div> </div> </div> </div>Way ahead of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:49:47-07:00","id":981441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981398#post981398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get the whole Djinn thing going on. I know that there are some people who really love the idea of djinn, but I don't get the themes that are going on here. What's up with being increasingly irrelevant? Doesn't that kind of contradict the idea of being a protagonist? IE- the persons who go out and do stuff to affect the world and shape the story? How would that even be playable?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like some of the ideas there, but I'm having some trouble figuring out what the game would even look like. What does a typical adventure look like, and don't these characters become less interesting as the game goes on?<br /> <br /> I suppose you could get very experimental with it, making a game that's less about your character and more about serving as a proxy for the people you grant wishes to, having this complicated network of patrons where you have to balance giving them what you want against keeping them coming back for more. In other words, you play a magical dealer, and you collaborate with the ST to tell stories about your stable of junkies. But that's a pretty far cry from the typical TT game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:25:33-07:00","id":981456,"title":"","content":"Aliens was brought up earlier in the thread as a possibility, especially since it's been done multiple times, meaning that there might be a niche open for it.<br /> <br /> Having seen most of them (atleast, the big ones), one notices that for the majority of them, the use of technology, specifically as discrete items seperate from the character, is used to justify abilities and powers. For some reason, this is one of the reasons I felt OPP would never make an Aliens themed game, atleast, in that style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-04-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:31:40-07:00","id":981486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981441#post981441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like some of the ideas there, but I'm having some trouble figuring out what the game would even look like. What does a typical adventure look like, and don't these characters become less interesting as the game goes on?</div> </div> </div> </div> Indeed. I'd love to hear some more fleshed out ideas on what a typical story would be like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose you could get very experimental with it, making a game that's less about your character and more about serving as a proxy for the people you grant wishes to, having this complicated network of patrons where you have to balance giving them what you want against keeping them coming back for more. In other words, you play a magical dealer, and you collaborate with the ST to tell stories about your stable of junkies. But that's a pretty far cry from the typical TT game. </div> </div> </div> Ehh... that's when we start hitting back into Mummy space. The point of that particular game is to serve as a cult's god and grant their prayers, even as you have to serve as an &quot;angel&quot; for the godlike Judges of Death, who in turn were servants of another god-like being, etc. Mummy is all about the compulsion to serve. There's a whole give and take built around the relationship of god to servant in that game. Any similar concept is just going to overlap. <br /> <br /> Now, rather than being a game about granting wishes, perhaps we could in the direction of focusing on Touchstones and Anchors. Vampire needs humans to relate to. Werewolves have spirit-based and flesh-based anchors. Changelings need people they relate to as touchstones. Not every game has formal touchstones, but the idea is solid. However, not sure how much this will overlap with Promethean - there's a lot of picking people to relate to, then moving on to new &quot;touchstones,&quot; even if its not given that formal name. I personally would prefer such a game that had a &quot;remember where you came from&quot; vibe, though. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:34:06-07:00","id":981490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981456#post981456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aliens was brought up earlier in the thread as a possibility, especially since it's been done multiple times, meaning that there might be a niche open for it.<br /> <br /> Having seen most of them (atleast, the big ones), one notices that for the majority of them, the use of technology, specifically as discrete items seperate from the character, is used to justify abilities and powers. For some reason, this is one of the reasons I felt OPP would never make an Aliens themed game, atleast, in that style.</div> </div> </div> </div> What other themes would the game have beyond just &quot;use technology?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:38:45-07:00","id":981493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981490#post981490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What other themes would the game have beyond just &quot;use technology?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have trouble coming to grips with an Alien game (and I think Changeling already has a lot of the natural themes covered), but I think the most easy hook is focusing on assimilation and xenophobia. Maybe there's an angle of wanting to share what your species has learned countered by the concern that humanity simply can't handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:09:52-07:00","id":981645,"title":"","content":"Generally, I find the alien fangame projects to focus on... being literally an alien in multiple sense of the world. Usually, you're a refugee or someone who was a refugee. The reason you're on Earth is because it's a convient hiding spot away from prying eyes... or because of crash landing generations ago. <br /> <br /> And to justify why you can't go into space? You lack the tech or doing so is real bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, you're an altered experimented human. Even I am admittedly not free of that as it's the easy way to justify having aliens be closer to humans.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:37:13-07:00","id":981665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981645#post981645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, I find the alien fangame projects to focus on... being literally an alien in multiple sense of the world. Usually, you're a refugee or someone who was a refugee. The reason you're on Earth is because it's a convient hiding spot away from prying eyes... or because of crash landing generations ago.<br /> <br /> And to justify why you can't go into space? You lack the tech or doing so is real bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, you're an altered experimented human. Even I am admittedly not free of that as it's the easy way to justify having aliens be closer to humans.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The latter sounds like it's directly in the wheelhouse for Deviant.<br /> <br /> I'm not a <i>huge</i> fan of Alien as a core game concept, but I could see it potentially working as a sort of inversion of CtL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:02:14-07:00","id":981920,"title":"","content":"I feel like I want Aliens as an antagonist blue book more than I want to play them. I want bug like horrors (Starship Troopers/Alien(s)), I want actual alien abductions (different but similar from the greys in changeling), I want alien invasion (and some post invasion settings (District 9, Defiance)), I'd love ancient alien style mysteries (oh it really was aliens that one time). To be fair I think sans the first and last points (though maybe the abyss has something? ) you can technically cover the rest (though I'd also love a book on ancient ruins).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T22:21:55-07:00","id":981964,"title":"","content":"Ooh had another thought, what if the core concept was madness... I don't have an idea for the monsters themselves, but I can see this being basically Malkavian's as their own splat, kind of thing, but ChroD style and they don't have to be vampires at all. As your power stat grows the madder you get. Basically a splat about dealing with mental illness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T00:46:00-07:00","id":982002,"title":"","content":"That's already pretty solidly in Changeling's wheel house though. While not apt for all forms of mental illness (I don't think all forms of mental illness make for compelling games though), as the Lost go up in Wyrd and down in Clarity, they struggle harder and harder to keep a solid grasp on reality as fae logic and reality logic bleed into each other.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what else you'd really do with a game that has a strong focus on mental illness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:04:04-07:00","id":982033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=981964#post981964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh had another thought, what if the core concept was madness... I don't have an idea for the monsters themselves, but I can see this being basically Malkavian's as their own splat, kind of thing, but ChroD style and they don't have to be vampires at all. As your power stat grows the madder you get. Basically a splat about dealing with mental illness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling literally had Beautiful Madness as a tagline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:00:28-07:00","id":982084,"title":"","content":"Changeling is is a different kind of madness in my mind, or not entirely different. The game has never really seemed to focus on mental illness though, at least not outside of PTSD (abuse/stolkholm), really. It doesn't even really cover stolkholm all that well. I always felt like Changeling the madness is more about the Fae, and the Hedge, it never felt like it was about the Changeling themselves losing it (yes I know clarity stat), at least not in the way you think of a person suffering from mental illness. Perhaps that's just my experience. It certainly doesn't feel like (except perhaps in the hedge) like it's a good fit for generally modeling someone with chemical anxiety, depression, bipolar, schizophrenia, dementia, etc. See what happened to a Changeling actually happened, and could happen again. They're like a vietnam vet, or an abused spouse. People with innate mental disorders, can often conjur up things that never happened, and aren't likely to. Often you are your own worst enemy. Having a real panic attack, over a whole lot of nothing for the first time... An interesting thing about Malk's is there ability to impose this on others.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I don't really have a monster in mind, I feel like the &quot;nightmare monster&quot; would have been a good fit, but Beast didn't really go in that direction. So far I haven't thought of another good monster fit for this (old gods aside).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:59:23-07:00","id":982152,"title":"","content":"I'd been left wanting a proper Demon game, after Demon came out. <br /> <br /> To be specific, Abrahamic style. <br /> <br /> Maybe we could get this style back, including Angels and Demons in a Divine: the Rebellion or something.<br /> <br /> Scanning through the thread though, I'm pretty enchanted with Aliens (especially if we're talking grays sneaking around among the populace and dodging the MiBs) and Kaiju.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:34:02-07:00","id":982229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=966647#post966647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give me a gigantic crossover book on Cults that's equal parts the kin of <i>Slasher</i> and a guide to having a subservient organization for every gameline (Vampire, Mage, Mummy, Demon, and Beast all explicitly have this, and Changeling and Geist can easily fit it as well - to say nothing of whether or not a Werewolf pack is just a cult with a nice name) and I'll never complain again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see an expanded set of rules for creating bases/hideouts, minions, webs of intrigue, connections, and so on. Both friendly and hostile.<br /> <br /> (apologies if borrowing antecedents from other IPs is bad form)<br /> <br /> Ninjas &amp; Superspies lets you create your organization and gain perks from it.<br /> <br /> Illuminati CCG lets you build a web of influence while trying to thwart the other webs conspiring against you.<br /> <br /> Star Trek Online lets you send your minions (ahem, crew) on away missions while you're busy doing other things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:28:39-07:00","id":982263,"title":"","content":"Aaaaaaaand.... thread caught up.<br /> <br /> Let me add something (hopefully) new and (hopefullyer) fun to the list of ideas!<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Relic: the Borrowing</b></span><br /> <br /> The world is scattered with artifacts of bygone eras. They hide in attics, or sit on display in museums. Some few of them are compulsively collected. Some are discarded and forgotten.<br /> <br /> But some few of them collect and discard their owners, rather than the reverse.<br /> <br /> The Bones of Saint Examplename rattle in their glass reliquary whenever the supernatural draws close. Their bearer somehow always manages to survive the creatures of the night, only to retreat from the world as mute hermits shortly after.<br /> <br /> Maru Marumaru was borne into battle for the last time in 1944, lost, and collected my the advancing American Navy. The katana has sat, sleeping, in a display case in a retired Admiral's study ever since. But now he has passed on, and the sword will do anything to return to its home temple.<br /> <br /> A peculiar silver coin has been in circulation for over two centuries. It has been won and lost in many gambles, and used nearly as often to decide a heads-or-tails call. In all its years, it has brought extreme streaks of luck - wondrous and terrible - to its wielders. It yearns to find the one person who can always call its face when it's flipped, and in searching, it's discarded so many hundreds of owners.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Relic: the Borrowing (RtB) is a Storytelling game of magic items. These are not the plain old &quot;+1&quot; sword, nor the ever-cooperative artifacts, weapons, gizmos, doodads, or enchantments hiding behind points of Merits. <br /> <br /> A Relic possesses its own magic, motivation, history and destiny. However it comes to be, it is called to some purpose. What a Relic lacks, however, is a body to wield it and a mind to guide it in the short term.<br /> <br /> Bodies can be borrowed, and minds can be steered, but at a cost. Every wielder of a Relic risks their health and sanity, and often even their soul, to carry it just a little longer. A Relic may choose its wielders carelessly and wrack them voraciously, leaving behind a trail of the broken and mad. A more careful Relic may chose carefully and shepherd their wielders along with caution. <br /> <br /> Both paths risk Disrepair, the condition which costs a Relic a bit of its own power or durability. Disrepair may be staved off with use matching the Relic's or wielder's motivations, or with careful Repairs.<br /> <br /> A careless Relic that does not mind its own purpose and disregards its own destiny runs the risk of becoming Jinxed. A Jinx is a dark stain on the Relic's history, throwing off the entire nature of its own magic. Some Relics fall to their Jinx entirely, becoming one of the Banjaxed. The Banjaxed sometimes associate with Gremlins - beings of a darkly paradoxical nature, who seem to be drawn to the presence of a Relic out of its own time and place.<br /> <br /> The cold, cruel end of so many Relics is to become an Antique. Antiques have fallen so far into Disrepair, or been so badly Jinxed, that their peculiar destinies dwindle away to nothing.<br /> <br /> A very fortunate few among the Relics succeed in following and protecting their destinies, to become celebrated as Icons. Icons are Relics that have become touchstones of their era, cementing their history in a world where even the past can sometimes be all too fluid. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:27:08-07:00","id":982352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982152#post982152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd been left wanting a proper Demon game, after Demon came out.<br /> <br /> To be specific, Abrahamic style.<br /> <br /> Maybe we could get this style back, including Angels and Demons in a Divine: the Rebellion or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you do is take demon, and just not use the technological names for things. The technological element really is a coat of paint rather than anything concrete, and even in non-altered demon the demon form section lists two descriptions for each form power a technological appearance and a abrahamic style demon appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T14:47:43-07:00","id":982362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982084#post982084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People with innate mental disorders, can often conjur up things that never happened, and aren't likely to. Often you are your own worst enemy. Having a real panic attack, over a whole lot of nothing for the first time... An interesting thing about Malk's is there ability to impose this on others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, lets divide mental illness into three unscientific categories:<br /> <br /> Traumatic mental illness. We seem to agree Changeling does this.<br /> Chronic mental illness: These are the things like personality disorders, depression, developmental disorders, etc.<br /> Degenerative mental illness: These are things like Alzheimer's, dementia, etc.<br /> <br /> The issue with chronic mental illness is that it isn't a good exploration of them to have them be an inevitable progression towards worse symptoms. Most chronic mental illnesses are relatively stable after they mature. Even if to external observers they look irregular and sporadic, to those with these conditions they are usually a constant presence that is usually not visible to others.<br /> <br /> The issue with degenerative mental illness is that while it follows a progression, it is coupled with a loss of practical faculties that would make for a questionable play experience where your character loses the ability to meaningfully interact with the setting over time rather than having increased capacity to do so.<br /> <br /> Both groups of mental illnesses also have major issues with being respectful to the real world conditions in question and maintaining a playable game. CofD 1e is a great example of how this can go awry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:52:15-07:00","id":982410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982362#post982362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, lets divide mental illness into three unscientific categories:<br /> <br /> Traumatic mental illness. We seem to agree Changeling does this.<br /> Chronic mental illness: These are the things like personality disorders, depression, developmental disorders, etc.<br /> Degenerative mental illness: These are things like Alzheimer's, dementia, etc.<br /> <br /> The issue with chronic mental illness is that it isn't a good exploration of them to have them be an inevitable progression towards worse symptoms. Most chronic mental illnesses are relatively stable after they mature. Even if to external observers they look irregular and sporadic, to those with these conditions they are usually a constant presence that is usually not visible to others.<br /> <br /> The issue with degenerative mental illness is that while it follows a progression, it is coupled with a loss of practical faculties that would make for a questionable play experience where your character loses the ability to meaningfully interact with the setting over time rather than having increased capacity to do so.<br /> <br /> Both groups of mental illnesses also have major issues with being respectful to the real world conditions in question and maintaining a playable game. CofD 1e is a great example of how this can go awry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Last point hit the nail on the head, I think. CtL isn't about PTSD as such. It's about coping with trauma and can serve as a metaphor for any number of traumas without being a one-for-one allegory for PTSD. There are the seeds there for players to deal with questions of paranoia, survivor's guilt, and outright delusions, but it can be amped up or reduced depending on the sensibilities and sensitivities of the players.<br /> <br /> I don't think we need a game &quot;about&quot; mental disease. We can have games that speak to raw trauma or incurable conditions or the slippery slope of reality, but to make it about those things just strikes me as insensitive and blunt. And frankly, it's something that's hard to pull off well. Just look at the Malkavians from the original WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:56:38-07:00","id":982413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982362#post982362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, lets divide mental illness into three unscientific categories:<br /> <br /> Traumatic mental illness. We seem to agree Changeling does this.<br /> Chronic mental illness: These are the things like personality disorders, depression, developmental disorders, etc.<br /> Degenerative mental illness: These are things like Alzheimer's, dementia, etc.<br /> <br /> The issue with chronic mental illness is that it isn't a good exploration of them to have them be an inevitable progression towards worse symptoms. Most chronic mental illnesses are relatively stable after they mature. Even if to external observers they look irregular and sporadic, to those with these conditions they are usually a constant presence that is usually not visible to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>sure but this is a game... most people aren't abused by magical fairies... either...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue with degenerative mental illness is that while it follows a progression, it is coupled with a loss of practical faculties that would make for a questionable play experience where your character loses the ability to meaningfully interact with the setting over time rather than having increased capacity to do so. </div> </div> </div>Mummy... in a sense does this... so does vampire, sort of... I mean, not exactly but... and I've always found it odd in the game that mortals only ever get stronger... age never impacts them so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Both groups of mental illnesses also have major issues with being respectful to the real world conditions in question and maintaining a playable game. CofD 1e is a great example of how this can go awry. </div> </div> </div>so... you don't think Malkavian's should be played in Vampire either I'm guessing?<br /> <br /> personally think it could be done... done respectfully, in a similar way to changelings respect to the traumatic variant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:01:12-07:00","id":982419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982413#post982413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sure but this is a game... most people aren't abused by magical fairies... either...<br /> <br /> Mummy... in a sense does this... so does vampire, sort of... I mean, not exactly but... and I've always found it odd in the game that mortals only ever get stronger... age never impacts them so...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> so... you don't think Malkavian's should be played in Vampire either I'm guessing?<br /> <br /> personally think it could be done... done respectfully, in a similar way to changelings respect to the traumatic variant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's something I'm hesitant about, but what would your hypothetical game look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:11:00-07:00","id":982424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982352#post982352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you do is take demon, and just not use the technological names for things. The technological element really is a coat of paint rather than anything concrete, and even in non-altered demon the demon form section lists two descriptions for each form power a technological appearance and a abrahamic style demon appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I want them to do a dark era or just a story for demons that just reads heavily biblical, if for no other reason than to hit this point home. I think seeing god, from the cultists perspective would also help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:28:54-07:00","id":982427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982419#post982419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something I'm hesitant about, but what would your hypothetical game look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>admittedly that's the problem, I think that there's something to it, and the struggle, but... I'm still trying to think of what kind of monster (that's not a vampire) fits. I don't think you would have characters that were purely crippled, rather like a promethean they gain strengths and weaknesses. I would agree that it has to be done carefully and right. I'm not sure I'm the right person to actually tackle it tastefully.<br /> <br /> I think like Malkavian's though providing insights through the madness would be a key part of the game.<br /> <br /> Brain storming, I like the general problem space, but I haven't really figured out how to mold it into something playable by itself.<br /> <br /> It's possible I need to dig into mage and the other astral realms beyond the primordial dreams... is it the Temenos? that's all of human existance or something? not a mage player. Perhaps you're able to tap into that in some way that leaves you dealing with the feelings and memories of others, but it's hard to sort out what's important what's not, and perhaps what's real (or at least real in a way that you can interact with) and what's not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:42:16-07:00","id":982478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982413#post982413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and I've always found it odd in the game that mortals only ever get stronger... age never impacts them so...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because there's no age stat.<br /> <br /> Age isn't hard to model. Make it a Persistent Condition: &quot;Old (Persistent). Is often discriminated against by people who don't realize old people are extremely diverse and are the culmination of consequences from much more life experience than younger people, by definition, could have. Mechanical penalties subject to who and what they are and what they're up to at the moment. No resolution.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:48:54-07:00","id":982485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982424#post982424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I want them to do a dark era or just a story for demons that just reads heavily biblical, if for no other reason than to hit this point home. I think seeing god, from the cultists perspective would also help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question, have you read the Biblical Shard &quot;Giants in the Earth&quot; in the Demon Storyteller's Guide? It's more straight biblical than the default, though it still retains some technological aspects, so it might be a good stepping-off point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-05-2016, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:52:50-07:00","id":982489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982478#post982478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No resolution.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Beg to differ. Resolution - Reverting your body's physical age (whether via experimental drugs, fountain of youth, or other method).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:49:24-07:00","id":982517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982413#post982413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy... in a sense does this... so does vampire, sort of...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies are caught in a cyclical loop, which is very different from the slide of dementia.<br /> <br /> Vampires in 1e did this kinda, but 2e has dropped it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, not exactly but... and I've always found it odd in the game that mortals only ever get stronger... age never impacts them so... </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about this. Most of the games have drawbacks that increase with their powers, but their increase in power generally outweighs the increase in drawbacks. Nobody really gets weaker with age, even if there are some variations on it (Mummy's get weaker and stronger in a cycle with their power stat, but they can increase in power each time, Prometheans eventually complete their New Dawn, etc.).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so... you don't think Malkavian's should be played in Vampire either I'm guessing? </div> </div> </div>No. I don't think Malkavians are strong enough as a concept to turn into the main focus of a single game.<br /> <br /> Exploring characters that have mental illnesses as a character option is fine as a player/group choice. Having individual characters that can have a carefully crafted approach to mental illness works in ways that turning it into a full game does not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T21:10:04-07:00","id":982538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982485#post982485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, have you read the Biblical Shard &quot;Giants in the Earth&quot; in the Demon Storyteller's Guide? It's more straight biblical than the default, though it still retains some technological aspects, so it might be a good stepping-off point.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah I read it, it wasn't quite what I was looking for? I mean it's a decent setting, but I think it still lacked a certain descriptiveness I was hoping for. There's a reason I'm vying for a cult perspective. Maybe it's possible that I really just want a different period, something of roman catholic cathedral's and priests... one would think constantinople would have covered that... but I was left feeling that even though it's a muslim/christian era, that religion is only glanced at. I think the God Machine only works as God if you have worshippers, and the worshippers are, imo, missing. The world cult is mentioned occasionally, but what that means, imo, is more vague than the God Machine. This is not to say I dislike any of this work, simply that it hasn't quite artistically satisfied what I have felt is missing to make DtD feel like Heaven vs Hell, and not just Techgnostic (I love the Techgnostic btw).<br /> <br /> For example, in my Constantinople some of the first things that my PC's will come across are an electrified crucifix as part of some infrastructure, and the golden angels of the golden gate (actually I'm not sure they were still there at the Fall, but screw history?).<br /> <br /> Angels will appear as whatever the beholders expected visage of one is, Demons are biomechanical horrors that are reminiscent of ... well Demon's. Outside of that, iconography, description of rituals, etc seems to be missing. I've not been able to figure out, are cultists baptized? do they take the wine and bread? do they worship the god of abraham? is the god of abraham the god machine (ok as a general thing I don't expect this to be answered, I mean, they might answer that abraham was worshiping the G-M, but that doesn't mean all abrahamic religious followers are)?<br /> <br /> Demons themselves are almost unilaterally painted in a protagonistic light, and the god machine in an adversarial light. I don't dislike this entirely after all that's definitely intended, but it doesn't give me a Heaven and Hell feel. We could also do with fiction of Demons earning the ire and fear. Tempters acting like succubi, and stealing their way into fortunes. Deals with demons being collected in what feels like a heinous act. Saboteurs making like terrorists and blowing up buildings with people inside, that were also researchers for a cancer cure in a G-M Facility (or something). Instead a scene, which I liked, has a demon taking on cancer for another demon, and a dying man. I like that, gives them a good light, but they don't have the contrast. I have real trouble seeing, outside of propaganda, why demon's are ever considered the bad guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":".  comment on Demon's being the good guy. 10-06-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T21:13:18-07:00","id":982539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982517#post982517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I don't think Malkavians are strong enough as a concept to turn into the main focus of a single game.<br /> <br /> Exploring characters that have mental illnesses as a character option is fine as a player/group choice. Having individual characters that can have a carefully crafted approach to mental illness works in ways that turning it into a full game does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, it definitely needs more thought at least... I like the idea, and maybe if I come up with a way to flesh it out I'll share it here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:36:34-07:00","id":982573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982538#post982538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah I read it, it wasn't quite what I was looking for? I mean it's a decent setting, but I think it still lacked a certain descriptiveness I was hoping for. There's a reason I'm vying for a cult perspective. Maybe it's possible that I really just want a different period, something of roman catholic cathedral's and priests... one would think constantinople would have covered that... but I was left feeling that even though it's a muslim/christian era, that religion is only glanced at. I think the God Machine only works as God if you have worshippers, and the worshippers are, imo, missing. The world cult is mentioned occasionally, but what that means, imo, is more vague than the God Machine. This is not to say I dislike any of this work, simply that it hasn't quite artistically satisfied what I have felt is missing to make DtD feel like Heaven vs Hell, and not just Techgnostic (I love the Techgnostic btw).</div> </div> </div> </div>Worshippers and cults could definitely use more text. As for religion, I think it's an odd topic in Demon, as unlike with religion, faith isn't really there outside of the beliefs of integrators. You don't really need faith when you've had a mental physical link to it and were cast out by it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Outside of that, iconography, description of rituals, etc seems to be missing. </div> </div> </div>That's the whole point of occult matrixes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've not been able to figure out, are cultists baptized? </div> </div> </div>So likely do. Not all. I'd expect most aren't. GM isn't just Christianity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> do they take the wine and bread? </div> </div> </div>^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> do they worship the god of abraham? </div> </div> </div>^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons themselves are almost unilaterally painted in a protagonistic light, and the god machine in an adversarial light. </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this rather severely. I mean GM saves humanity over and over, it is combating global warming, it keeps time moving forward, it makes gravity work, it saves people. All the while demons are stealing peoples lives and intentionally sabotaging the infrastructure that holds not only society together but also the infrastructure that keeps physics running correctly. A single angel falling can ruin so many plans of the GM, one timeline that has been discussed in Demon is one where it is eternally doomed because an angel fell and didn't complete the occult matrix for selfish reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't dislike this entirely after all that's definitely intended, but it doesn't give me a Heaven and Hell feel. </div> </div> </div>In my view, Heaven should operate simply the will of god, not necessarily &quot;Good&quot;. Hell is simply a place where there is no god, not &quot;Evil&quot;. Righteous Angels who simultaneously know all but know nothing, who are sustained by occult sacrifices and rituals, and wear human form as a mere disguise over their true eldritch abomination nature seems heavenly enough to me. Angels who went against their creators commands and get cast out, leaving them to possess their human disguises but retain enough power to be able to warp reality through tricks and pacts, and leaving them on the run from their old family who are guided by a omnipresent deity meaning you are always at risk of getting discovered, seems demonic enough for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tempters acting like succubi, and stealing their way into fortunes. </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what they do though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deals with demons being collected in what feels like a heinous act. </div> </div> </div>The section on agencies that focus on pacts seemed pretty heinous to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saboteurs making like terrorists and blowing up buildings with people inside, that were also researchers for a cancer cure in a G-M Facility (or something). </div> </div> </div>The book talks about how some Saboteurs use brutal and terrorist methods killing and destroying all GM assists they find (including sleeper agents), while others use subtle slow methods of infiltration and destroying the GM from the inside (like cancer cure Demons I guess). Most saboteurs fall between those two extremes. The book even says that many other demons consider them mindless terrorists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-06-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T04:33:09-07:00","id":982639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982352#post982352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you do is take demon, and just not use the technological names for things. The technological element really is a coat of paint rather than anything concrete, and even in non-altered demon the demon form section lists two descriptions for each form power a technological appearance and a abrahamic style demon appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I'd have to read more into it, but it says right up front that the theme is techgnosticism. *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:15:59-07:00","id":982680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982538#post982538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have real trouble seeing, outside of propaganda, why demon's are ever considered the bad guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is because many (perhaps most) Unchained are <i>assholes</i>, in the same vein as Vampires. They use people to their benefit and discard them. Just glance through their powers lists and count all the ways they can manipulate and screw with people. And remember that, unlike Vampire who were human once, and still cling to identifying as somewhat human (see: Humanity), Demons never were, and never will be, and don't really have any incentive to do so (beyond faking being a mere mortal successfully).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:11:04-07:00","id":982985,"title":"","content":"All this Demon discussion ultimately results in is someone saying they want more Heaven/Hell feel, and a bunch of people saying their opinion is invalid because... all you have to do is rename things... rinse repeat. <br /> <br /> we should get back on topic, if you really want to argue over Demon, there are threads in the Demon section of the forum discussing this, I'm sure I'm subscribed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T04:47:29-07:00","id":983251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=982985#post982985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this Demon discussion ultimately results in is someone saying they want more Heaven/Hell feel, and a bunch of people saying their opinion is invalid because... all you have to do is rename things... rinse repeat.<br /> <br /> we should get back on topic, if you really want to argue over Demon, there are threads in the Demon section of the forum discussing this, I'm sure I'm subscribed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. I would say, though, that the good-ol'-fashioned Angels and Demons are monsters that still seem to be &quot;left&quot; to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T05:24:04-07:00","id":983259,"title":"","content":"On topic? *shrugs* We keep ending up hitting Alien and Djinn as game ideas (pretty much every year a new game comes out and this thread makes a new appearance), then people keep saying that its just repeats of old games. Then debates go on and on about new themes.<br /> <br /> Every time, though, there are bids for a number of writers for new concepts and new angles to explore in society. There could be games based on the horrors of supposedly faceless corporations on the world, for instance, with the supernatural aspects being a Tulpa (mascot character come to life as the actual &quot;face&quot; of the corporation?) I don't know, that would need a lot more fleshing out than I'm willing to give it right now. But that's just an example of something that could be done off the top of my head. There's the Fury game I've mentioned before. Liches could be a thing - a game of seeking non-vampire immortality at any cost. As always, I think that cat-shifters need more love somewhere as PCs; we've got wolves as a full game, serpents in Beast, and vamps make excellent spider metaphors. But cats never really get a fair shake so far.<br /> <br /> I think we're moving into an area, however, where we need to be asking the question of &quot;<i>should</i> there be new game lines?&quot; Over-saturation is a thing, and we have had years where the theme was something like Night Horrors for every existing line instead of something new. I'm not personally interested in a million new games, but creating new spins on existing games, improving and expanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983251#post983251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. I would say, though, that the good-ol'-fashioned Angels and Demons are monsters that still seem to be &quot;left&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Please don't post provocative statements like this. I get it, you don't like Descent. But if you post things that come off as saying that another game isn't &quot;really demons&quot; or &quot;really other-supernatural?&quot; It comes off as trollish, condensending and insulting, and only serves as flamebait. Especially when Fallen is still around, and there's the Conversion guide and any number of supportive material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-07-2016, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:20:14-07:00","id":983417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983259#post983259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't post provocative statements like this. I get it, you don't like Descent. But if you post things that come off as saying that another game isn't &quot;really demons&quot; or &quot;really other-supernatural?&quot; It comes off as trollish, condensending and insulting, and only serves as flamebait. Especially when Fallen is still around, and there's the Conversion guide and any number of supportive material.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. Descent is a fine setting, and I've been enjoying reading through the anthology. <br /> <br /> I also don't intend either provocation or flamebait. I am saying, only and specifically, that non-techno demons don't exist and are therefore &quot;left&quot; to do. It's fine if you disagree, and it's fine if you believe that a conversion book or stylistic change counts. Though, I would point out that you can stylistically rewrite lots of splats into other splats, yet those other splats still exist. <br /> <br /> Again, nothing I've said is trolling, flamebait, provocative, or disapproving. I'm answering a question about what I believe to be an available and interesting gap in the setting line. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for cat shifters, I'd like to see a revamp of Changing Breeds to fix a lot of issues and bring them all up to a good 2nd-edition level of coolness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:14:41-07:00","id":983490,"title":"","content":"I think in addition to the issue of over saturation, there's the issue of the 2e books feeling unsupported. I have a feeling that 2e supplements will be coming faster once the games are all updated, but at the moment it feels like we're getting new game-lines faster than 2e supplements to the existing game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:20:38-07:00","id":983492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983417#post983417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am saying, only and specifically, that non-techno demons don't exist and are therefore &quot;left&quot; to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't true, though. Hunter 1E had Lesser and Greater Demons (whether these were Spirits or Unchained in disguise is left to the ST). Mage 1E had Goetic Demons (now just generally called Goetia). Inferno exists. Changeling had(has?) dream beings called Demons as well. Duat apparently has number, too.<br /> <br /> Demons are everywhere throughout the CofD, only one set of them being in any way &quot;techno&quot;. Those just happen to be the PC splat for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:24:22-07:00","id":983587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983251#post983251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps. I would say, though, that the good-ol'-fashioned Angels and Demons are monsters that still seem to be &quot;left&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would like to see the Celestials, and a 2e Inferno... but I'm not sure either of these are PC books...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:28:27-07:00","id":983590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983259#post983259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time, though, there are bids for a number of writers for new concepts and new angles to explore in society. There could be games based on the horrors of supposedly faceless corporations on the world, for instance, with the supernatural aspects being a Tulpa (mascot character come to life as the actual &quot;face&quot; of the corporation?) I don't know, that would need a lot more fleshing out than I'm willing to give it right now. But that's just an example of something that could be done off the top of my head. There's the Fury game I've mentioned before. Liches could be a thing - a game of seeking non-vampire immortality at any cost. As always, I think that cat-shifters need more love somewhere as PCs; we've got wolves as a full game, serpents in Beast, and vamps make excellent spider metaphors. But cats never really get a fair shake so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about enough on Lich's and the Tremere to make them playable... 'cause otherwise mage has got you covered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please don't post provocative statements like this. I get it, you don't like Descent. But if you post things that come off as saying that another game isn't &quot;really demons&quot; or &quot;really other-supernatural?&quot; It comes off as trollish, condensending and insulting, and only serves as flamebait. Especially when Fallen is still around, and there's the Conversion guide and any number of supportive material. </div> </div> </div>... and this is supposed to come off as what? by invalidating someone elses opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 10-07-2016, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:02:28-07:00","id":983604,"title":"","content":"So far as I can tell, there isn't anything for just plain robots, cyborgs, or androids that <i>are not </i>Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12499-alberto-barbosa","name":"Alberto Barbosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:04:47-07:00","id":983605,"title":"","content":"Imbued are basically Prometheans without all the baggage. They're in the Antagonists book.<br /> <br /> Deviant will likely be covering cyborgs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-07-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:11:07-07:00","id":983655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alberto Barbosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983604#post983604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as I can tell, there isn't anything for just plain robots, cyborgs, or androids that <i>are not </i>Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are plenty of options for cyborgs, androids, and robots, depending on just what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Deviants, as nofather mentioned, will definitely include cyborgs.<br /> <br /> Cyborgs are one of the microctemplates that will be included in Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> Bleeding Edge has rules for cybernetics for anyone, template or not.<br /> <br /> The endowment rules for Hunter could definitely be used for cybernetics, they're generic.<br /> <br /> The Mage Chroniclers Guide has a hack for turning mages into mad scientists, in which case you could reskin the proximi rules for android, robot, and cyborg types.<br /> <br /> Dark Heroes from Mirrors could definitely be reskinned as Six Million Dollar Man types.<br /> <br /> If you want something that transforms (not necessarily into machines, but more along the lines of having retractable armor and the like), you could reskin the shapeshifter rules from War Against the Pure.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm saying that OP couldn't make a line about androids, robots, and cyborgs if they so desired, one could play a werewolf type, magician type, or mummy type in Vampire, it didn't stop them from writing forsaken, awakening, or curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:24:54-07:00","id":983660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alberto Barbosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983604#post983604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as I can tell, there isn't anything for just plain robots, cyborgs, or androids that <i>are not </i>Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>and uh, what would you say Demon is if not just plain robots?... I actually feel like most of my robot needs are covered... I could use some robot mechanics for simpler robots (factories, drones), but there's not a game in that (though why do I feel like DSG might have something like this). <br /> <br /> That said if there's something that feels particularly missing from all that's been mentioned, I'd listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:06:51-07:00","id":983679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983660#post983660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and uh, what would you say Demon is if not just plain robots?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vaguely machine themed spirits.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12499-alberto-barbosa","name":"Alberto Barbosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T21:56:18-07:00","id":983755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alberto Barbosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983679#post983679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vaguely machine themed spirits.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean sounds like Angels, since Demons can't use Numina, and don't really share any characteristics with Spirits....<br /> <br /> That said, you don't want the Unfleshed, and you don't want Demons, not entirely sure what you would want? something that's not self aware?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:04:26-07:00","id":983796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983755#post983755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you don't want the Unfleshed, and you don't want Demons, not entirely sure what you would want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this some very subtle form of trolling? Robots that aren't imbued with a mystical pseudo-soul or Abrahamic spirits. Automatons. Droids. They wouldn't be anymore redundant to Prometheans than Blood Bathers to Vampires, Possessed to Sin-Eaters, or Beasts to Changelings. Overlap between types of PCs isn't a new thing at all in CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12499-alberto-barbosa","name":"Alberto Barbosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:35:01-07:00","id":983809,"title":"","content":"The CofD isn't a sci-fi setting. Advanced AIs that aren't the result of some sort of supernatural magic aren't going to be part of the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:42:25-07:00","id":983950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alberto Barbosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983796#post983796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this some very subtle form of trolling? Robots that aren't imbued with a mystical pseudo-soul or Abrahamic spirits. Automatons. Droids. They wouldn't be anymore redundant to Prometheans than Blood Bathers to Vampires, Possessed to Sin-Eaters, or Beasts to Changelings. Overlap between types of PCs isn't a new thing at all in CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's trolling to ask for further explaination, though perhaps I asked in a trolly way, unintentionally. Ultimately though, outside of the &quot;Futuristic Eras&quot; I suggested elsewhere, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>. Machines, currently do not possess free will, thus they lack agency. I can't see that being a game without giving them agency. To give them agency is essentially what Demon, and the Unfleshed do. It might be arguable to have more &quot;inhuman&quot; forms... that they're stuck in (though DSG does mention some angelic covers that are not human) (ChroD's obsession with all monsters having a human &quot;disguise&quot;, is not something I wholeheartedly agree with). Not trying to shoot the idea down, but other than some backstory fiddlyness, I'm trying to figure out what the game would be about that isn't covered.<br /> <br /> obviously we don't currently have androids, so we'll have to modify it to work in 2016. for sake of argument, you're a factory robot, a drone, a mobile computing device, or nasa rover; I don't know how any of these would unmystically gain awareness, so let's say that happens. since not all of these have locomotion, let's assume they make like transformers, and can sprout limbs. now what? what do you invision these characters doing? what is the point of their game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:39:06-07:00","id":984094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left#post960027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The CofD seems to be moving away from a new gameline every single year, and with good reason; it seems like most of the major monster archetypes have already been tapped. But I doubt new games will stop entirely, especially with the willingness to completely alter the narrative (Demon being about renegade eldritch program spies, Promethean taking Frankenstein's monster and turning it into a grand human journey) or move away from a central archetype in favor of a build-your -own model (Beast and Deviant seem especially focused on this), and so we need new monsters to draw upon.<br /> <br /> Are there any you feel are especially prime and untapped territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Politician: the Lying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:42:33-07:00","id":984184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984094#post984094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Politician: the Lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lying politicians are the best urban myth.<br /> <br /> But actually, you could probably do something off the Aldermen from the <i>Matthew Swift</i> books. They grease the wheels of London (or not) as its bureaucratic hands, and can manifest the strength of the city in its defense by turning into a metal dragon. And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:14:58-07:00","id":984194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984184#post984184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But actually, you could probably do something off the Aldermen from the <i>Matthew Swift</i> books. They grease the wheels of London (or not) as its bureaucratic hands, and can manifest the strength of the city in its defense by turning into a metal dragon. And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of like angels, but with cities instead of the God Machine? Or just with the God Machine, depending on how negative your views are about London or the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T23:21:42-07:00","id":984274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984194#post984194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of like angels, but with cities instead of the God Machine? Or just with the God Machine, depending on how negative your views are about London or the God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, didn't occur to me to make that comparison, but yeah. Basic Demon template, but still serving the City (with latitude on exactly what that means because your superior isn't God; he's just a schmuck called the Midnight Mayor). Still lacks something interesting to really be <i>doing</i> (no interlocks; no goal of Hell; etc.), but yeah. I could see hacking Demon to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T00:13:17-07:00","id":984289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=983809#post983809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The CofD isn't a sci-fi setting. Advanced AIs that aren't the result of some sort of supernatural magic aren't going to be part of the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be news to the cyborgs, genetically engineered mutants, psychics, etc in the upcoming Deviant the Renegade.<br /> <br /> Or the people who gain supernatural merits through mutations or scientific processes ala Second Sight.<br /> <br /> Or the people who make a zombie plague ala Antagonists, or make a cyborg out of dead people.<br /> <br /> Or to people who make chimera with genetic engineering ala Skinchangers, or catch a theriomorphic disease.<br /> <br /> Or to the hunters of taskforce valkyrie in Hunter, with their sci fi gadgets.<br /> <br /> Or to the guy with the fountain of youth bacteria in Wicked Dead, or someone who catches that vampiric parasite.<br /> <br /> Or to the cybernetically enhanced lost boys of Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 10-09-2016, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T00:23:46-07:00","id":984290,"title":"","content":"Also.... technically anything GM related isn't supernatural. It's just physics we don't understand yet (which is part of the reason demons don't have kinship with beasts, they are super advanced tech rather than true supernatural creatures).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:41:33-07:00","id":984432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984290#post984290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also.... technically anything GM related isn't supernatural. It's just physics we don't understand yet (which is part of the reason demons don't have kinship with beasts, they are super advanced tech rather than true supernatural creatures).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except, the G-M fully exploits supernatural phenomena to the point where distinction is moot. Demons come from Angels that are formed out of Ephemera, which is very much supernatural. Beasts don't have kinship with Demons because Reasons (which may deal with meta-issues like theme).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  As Satchel said Ephemera, not Essence. My point remains, though. 10-10-2016, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:10:21-07:00","id":984451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984290#post984290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also.... technically anything GM related isn't supernatural. It's just physics we don't understand yet (which is part of the reason demons don't have kinship with beasts, they are super advanced tech rather than true supernatural creatures).</div> </div> </div> </div>While we do mostly use the term supernatural to mean 'magic,' by definition it is about things beyond our understanding. This could mean magic, but it could also mean an iPod to an ancient Egyptian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T13:32:17-07:00","id":984579,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar391_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"391\" data-vbnamecard=\"391\">StSword</a> -<br /> <br /> I didn't say there aren't or shouldn't be sci-fi elements in the CofD. I said one specific thing wasn't going to be a non-supernatural thing (also nofather's point about that above).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:03:23-07:00","id":984634,"title":"","content":"Can we all just agree that we use the same five-ish terms for fairly wide ranges of genres, tropes, and setting elements, with substantial overlap between different persons' specific usage for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:08:28-07:00","id":984641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984432#post984432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons come from Angels that are formed out of Essence</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Ephemera is not Essence. A glass is not the water inside it.<br /> <br /> Angels don't use Essence in the same way that spirits do, for all that the in-the-moment mechanics amount to roughly the same thing. They're not incorporating it into their nature, they're just receiving and burning fuel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T05:08:36-07:00","id":984827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984641#post984641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels don't use Essence in the same way that spirits do, for all that the in-the-moment mechanics amount to roughly the same thing. They're not incorporating it into their nature, they're just receiving and burning fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such could be said about Ghosts as well, though, since they don't have a focus on consuming the &quot;right&quot; kinds of Essence either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:30:51-07:00","id":984850,"title":"","content":"Not read the whole thread... but... Instead of going for the Old and looking for something to link it with how about going for something new.<br /> <br /> Imagine the horror of being the first of your kind, your something new, something that doesn't have a legacy. Your Alone... but you know there are others... you can Feel them. They are a part of you.. they are yours.. and you are theirs. You woke up with no knowledge of what happened to you... But something has. You do not exist, but everyone knows you, you know things you couldn't know about, but you remember them perfectly. You are a Locus. Your are a Hub, things come to you and you can guide people and objects into the places that fit them best. But this is not without danger and horror, the more people rely upon you the less of themselves they can express.<br /> Themes could be dealing with the Growing connectivity of the World and its expression within the supernatural. Secondary theme might be the loss of identity and fear of becoming an &quot;It&quot; rather then an individual.<br /> Mood would be tense fear of growing into a role as something/someone &quot;New&quot; in an environment your not used to (May also be part of the theme).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T09:19:02-07:00","id":984911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960027-what-monsters-are-left?p=984827#post984827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such could be said about Ghosts as well, though, since they don't have a focus on consuming the &quot;right&quot; kinds of Essence either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts have an innate relation to a place that is straight-up another dimension and still hold a connection to the Essence that feeds them while away from it that is not simply &quot;God put the generator here.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can turn otherwise-mundane people into ephemera. Existing in Twilight is not an inherent mark of supernatural being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T09:22:30-07:00","id":984913,"title":"","content":"I like the &quot;nexus of the strange&quot; thing, and the idea that it leads to being an unwitting guide to the people and things around you. It's touched upon in some of the books, but usually as a minor splat/z-splat sort of thing at best. I kind of wish Geist had incorporated this more (though I love of set of novels where this is sort of the function of people selected by death to do so), but that's not the direction Geist took.<br /> <br /> I don't like tying it to the &quot;something new&quot; part. Deviant looks like it will hit on that in a stronger way. And there's always issues with being &quot;unique&quot; in a group oriented game. It's hard to have 3-6 characters all trying to feel like the unique first of their kind at the same time while they're all the same kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}